00:08:10,157 --> 00:08:13,027
I’M A MAGIC MAN.
[IMITATES MUSIC]

240
00:08:13,027 --> 00:08:15,062
I NEED YOU,
TOM.

241
00:08:15,062 --> 00:08:17,632
NO ONE WILL EVER LOVE
YOU MORE THAN I DO.

242
00:08:17,632 --> 00:08:21,668
WELL, THERE’S SOMETHING
ABOUT AN AQUA VELVA MAN.

243
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:22,970
I’M SORRY FOR EVERYTHING.

244
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:25,472
ESPECIALLY PUTTING
WORMS IN YOUR BED.

245
00:08:25,472 --> 00:08:27,908
GOOD NIGHT,
VI.

246
00:08:27,908 --> 00:08:30,477
I STILL HAVE YOUR LETTERS.

247
00:08:30,477 --> 00:08:32,880
WHOA.
SOMEONE GAVE HER A BRA--

248
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:35,182
NO, HONEY.
NO.

249
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,053
HOLD ON.

250
00:08:39,053 --> 00:08:42,423
I’VE NEVER BEEN
IN A LIGHTHOUSE BEFORE.

251
00:08:42,423 --> 00:08:44,825
SHOW ME THE LIGHT,
DARLING.

252
00:08:44,825 --> 00:08:48,528
GOT TO THINK.

253
00:08:51,298 --> 00:08:53,600
HMM. NOW, THIS
COULD BE THE NURSERY.

254
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:57,103
HAVE THE BASSINET OVER
BY THE FRESNEL LENS.

255
00:08:57,103 --> 00:08:58,872
WHAT ABOUT THE LETTERS,
VI?

256
00:08:58,872 --> 00:09:01,475
OH, I NEVER THROW
ANYTHING LIKE THAT AWAY.

257
00:09:01,475 --> 00:09:04,745
YOU NEVER KNOW WHEN
THEY MIGHT COME IN HANDY.

258
00:09:04,745 --> 00:09:07,582
I WONDER HOW SHE’D FEEL
IF I READ THEM TO HER.

259
00:09:07,582 --> 00:09:09,783
PUTTING IN PERTINENT
FOOTNOTES, OF COURSE.

260
00:09:09,783 --> 00:09:10,852
LIKE MAD LIBS.

261
00:09:10,852 --> 00:09:11,785
YEAH.
HMM.

262
00:09:14,688 --> 00:09:17,292
OR MAYBE I HAVE
TO SHOW THEM TO A LAWYER.

263
00:09:17,292 --> 00:09:19,093
I’M SURE HE’D KNOW
WHAT TO DO WITH THEM.

264
00:09:19,093 --> 00:09:20,227
HMM.

265
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:21,495
HOW WOULD
A LAWSUIT FIT IN

266
00:09:21,495 --> 00:09:23,697
WITH YOUR MUSIC CAREER,
TOM?

267
00:09:23,697 --> 00:09:25,532
HOW WOULD THE PIANO
GENIUS OF JAZZ FEEL

268
00:09:25,532 --> 00:09:27,100
ABOUT THAT KIND
OF PUBLICITY?

269
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:28,335
OH,
LIKE THERE’S NEVER BEEN

270
00:09:28,335 --> 00:09:30,370
A SEX SCANDAL
IN JAZZ BEFORE.

271
00:09:30,370 --> 00:09:31,605
DARLING,
YOU LOOK AS IF

272
00:09:31,605 --> 00:09:33,240
YOU WERE READY
TO KILL ME.

273
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,308
BINGO.

274
00:09:34,308 --> 00:09:35,375
NOW,
YOU GET THIS STRAIGHT--

275
00:09:35,375 --> 00:09:36,777
I’M MARRYING MEG.

276
00:09:36,777 --> 00:09:39,213
AND YOU GET THIS STRAIGHT,
TOM STEWART--

277
00:09:39,213 --> 00:09:41,948
NO ONE WILL EVER
HAVE YOU BUT ME.

278
00:09:41,948 --> 00:09:43,083
SCARED STRAIGHT.

279
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,118
[SCREAMS]

280
00:09:44,118 --> 00:09:45,152
[ALL]
HMM.

281
00:09:45,152 --> 00:09:46,220
HELP ME.

282
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:47,288
[ALL]
HMM.

283
00:09:47,288 --> 00:09:48,922
PLEASE, TOM.
HELP ME.

284
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:50,157
WHAT? HUH?

285
00:09:50,157 --> 00:09:51,992
[IMITATES PHONE RINGING]
OH, HONEY,

286
00:09:51,992 --> 00:09:54,195
TELEPHONE’S RINGING.
I GOTTA GO.

287
00:09:54,195 --> 00:09:56,163
SAVE ME, TOM.
PLEASE.

288
00:09:56,163 --> 00:09:58,665
WELL, THAT’S WHAT SHE GETS
FOR RAILING AGAINST HIM.

289
00:09:58,665 --> 00:10:00,067
OOH.
[LAUGHS]

290
00:10:00,067 --> 00:10:01,202
OUCH.

291
00:10:01,202 --> 00:10:02,437
PLEASE.

292
00:10:02,437 --> 00:10:03,737
[SCREAMS]

293
00:10:03,737 --> 00:10:06,307
UH, UH, HOLD ON.
I’VE DECIDED TO SAVE YOU.

294
00:10:06,307 --> 00:10:08,608
WHAT-- OH.
SHOOT.

295
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:11,745
NOTE TO MYSELF--
NEVER DATE IN A LIGHTHOUSE.

296
00:10:11,745 --> 00:10:13,480
MS. JOHNSON,
SEND IN ANOTHER FIANCÉ.

297
00:10:18,052 --> 00:10:19,953
NEXT WEEK,
ON TORMENTED...

298
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:26,060
TONIGHT’S EPISODE--

299
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:28,262
JONATHAN LIVINGSTON
MURDERED.

300
00:10:28,262 --> 00:10:32,467
HI. I’M BILL BURRUD
FOR WORLD OF ADVENTURE.

301
00:10:32,467 --> 00:10:35,202
WHOA. GEE. SHE REALLY
CAME APART ON THE ROCKS.

302
00:10:35,202 --> 00:10:36,703
EW.

303
00:10:36,703 --> 00:10:40,775
[HUMMING]

304
00:10:40,775 --> 00:10:43,310
HUH? NO.
THAT’S NOT HER.

305
00:10:46,647 --> 00:10:48,582
SPALDING,
OLD MAN.

306
00:10:53,687 --> 00:10:55,790
HEY. HE LOOKS LIKE
THE DAD FROM FLIPPER.

307
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:56,823
YEAH.

308
00:10:56,823 --> 00:10:58,758
OH. OW. OOH.
OWIE. OW. OH.

309
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:11,672
OH, NOW HE’S
BODY SURFING.

310
00:11:11,672 --> 00:11:15,075
- LITERALLY.
- [LAUGHS]

311
00:11:15,075 --> 00:11:17,177
OH. NOTHING LIKE
AN INVIGORATING SWIM

312
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,612
WITH A CORPSE
IN THE MORNING.

313
00:11:18,612 --> 00:11:19,747
[LAUGHS]

314
00:11:19,747 --> 00:11:23,850
I GOTTA MAKE THIS
MY DAILY RITUAL HERE.

315
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:25,485
[HUMS]

316
00:11:25,485 --> 00:11:28,388
♪ CATCH A WAVE AND YOU’RE
SITTIN’ ON TOP OF A GIRL ♪

317
00:11:28,388 --> 00:11:29,823
[LAUGHS]

318
00:11:29,823 --> 00:11:34,195
TONIGHT, ON A VERY
SPECIAL BAYWATCH.

319
00:11:34,195 --> 00:11:35,897
LOOK. I’M REALLY SORRY
ABOUT LAST NIGHT.

320
00:11:35,897 --> 00:11:37,363
CAN I MAKE IT UP TO YA?

321
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,133
HERE, FOLKS.
YOU TAKE HER.

322
00:11:40,835 --> 00:11:41,902
[GRUNTS]

323
00:11:41,902 --> 00:11:42,970
HERE.
YOU BE DEBORAH KERR.

324
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:44,838
I’LL BE BURT LANCASTER.

325
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:48,208
HMM?

326
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:49,310
UGH.

327
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:54,115
SHE’S TURNING INTO
A CAESAR SALAD.

328
00:11:54,115 --> 00:11:55,482
HUH?

329
00:11:55,482 --> 00:11:58,152
IT’S, UH, SORT OF AN
HERBAL WRAP, ISN’T IT?

330
00:12:00,187 --> 00:12:02,790
WHAT?
NO CROUTONS?

331
00:12:02,790 --> 00:12:03,823
TOM.

332
00:12:03,823 --> 00:12:04,892
- SOMEBODY "KELP" ME.
- [LAUGHTER]

333
00:12:04,892 --> 00:12:07,795
EVEN IN DEATH,
I’M FUNNY.

334
00:12:07,795 --> 00:12:08,862
WHO IS IT?

335
00:12:08,862 --> 00:12:09,930
IT’S ME.
SANDY.

336
00:12:09,930 --> 00:12:10,998
YOUR LITTLE CONSCIENCE.

337
00:12:10,998 --> 00:12:12,065
SANDY.

338
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:13,267
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

339
00:12:13,267 --> 00:12:16,170
SANDY, LOOK.
DO ME A FAVOR, WILL YA,

340
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:17,370
AND RUN OUT
AND PLAY SOMEWHERE.

341
00:12:17,370 --> 00:12:18,505
I’M BUSY.

342
00:12:18,505 --> 00:12:22,977
OH, I SEE ANOTHER CORPSE
TURNED INTO SEAWEED.

343
00:12:22,977 --> 00:12:26,813
[IMITATES REVERSE SPEECH]

344
00:12:26,813 --> 00:12:29,082
DON’T YOU LIKE ME ANYMORE?

345
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:30,150
WELL,
YOU’RE ASSUMING

346
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,618
I LIKED YOU
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

347
00:12:31,618 --> 00:12:33,087
SURE, I LIKE YOU.
I LOVE YOU.

348
00:12:33,087 --> 00:12:34,322
I JUST WANNA BE BY MYSELF.

349
00:12:34,322 --> 00:12:36,990
WHERE WERE YOU LAST NIGHT?

350
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:38,592
OH, KILLIN’ SOME--
OOH. NO.

351
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:40,760
THE EMERSONS HAD
A BEACH BARBECUE.

352
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,863
AND EVERYONE
ON THE ISLAND WAS THERE.

353
00:12:42,863 --> 00:12:43,930
EXCEPT HEF.

354
00:12:43,930 --> 00:12:45,765
MEG WAS LOOKING
ALL OVER FOR YOU.

355
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,468
SANDY,
PLEASE RUN ALONG.

356
00:12:47,468 --> 00:12:49,403
OKAY.

357
00:12:49,403 --> 00:12:51,705
SORRY TO DISTURB YOU.

358
00:12:51,705 --> 00:12:52,773
OOH.

359
00:12:52,773 --> 00:12:54,040
I ALMOST FORGOT--

360
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,775
THE WEDDING
ANNOUNCEMENTS CAME.

361
00:12:55,775 --> 00:12:57,443
AND MOMMY WANTS
YOU TO LOOK AT ONE

362
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:58,612
BEFORE WE SEND THEM OUT.

363
00:12:58,612 --> 00:13:00,848
THERE’S ONLY A WEEK
TILL THE BIG DAY.

364
00:13:00,848 --> 00:13:02,517
YEAH.
OKAY. OKAY.

365
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,887
WHAT’S THAT?

366
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:10,490
LOOK WHAT I FOUND.

367
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:13,560
I THINK
IT’S A PIECE OF BRAIN.

368
00:13:14,628 --> 00:13:15,662
WONDER WHOSE IT IS.

369
00:13:15,662 --> 00:13:17,898
GILLIGAN,
GIMME THAT.

370
00:13:17,898 --> 00:13:20,000
AND IT’S STILL TICKING.

371
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,435
I’M JOHN CAMERON SWAYZE
FOR TIMEX.

372
00:13:21,435 --> 00:13:23,137
DO YOU KNOW ANYONE
NAMED "VI?"

373
00:13:23,137 --> 00:13:25,638
UH...

374
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:26,740
NO.

375
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:27,808
I’LL TAKE CARE OF THIS.

376
00:13:27,808 --> 00:13:28,908
OH, GEEZ.

377
00:13:28,908 --> 00:13:30,477
HAYLEY MILLS GETS
THE PARENT TRAP,

378
00:13:30,477 --> 00:13:31,812
I GET STUCK IN THIS
LOUSY... [GRUMBLES]

379
00:13:38,385 --> 00:13:40,253
[TOM] (V.O.)
I’VE GOT TO TAKE IT EASY.

380
00:13:40,253 --> 00:13:42,122
I DIDN’T FIND
ANY DEAD WOMAN.

381
00:13:42,122 --> 00:13:43,223
ONLY SEAWEED.

382
00:13:43,223 --> 00:13:44,458
HMM.

383
00:13:44,458 --> 00:13:45,927
I KNOW WHAT’S
THE MATTER WITH ME.

384
00:13:45,927 --> 00:13:47,193
I’M SEEING THINGS.

385
00:13:47,193 --> 00:13:48,728
I’M LETTING
MY IMAGINATION RUN WILD.

386
00:13:48,728 --> 00:13:50,965
YOU’RE ALSO DOING VOICEOVERS
FOR CRAPPY MOVIES.

387
00:13:50,965 --> 00:13:53,267
NO.
WHY SHOULD IT BOTHER ME?

388
00:13:53,267 --> 00:13:55,268
I DIDN’T
DO ANYTHING TO VI.

389
00:13:55,268 --> 00:13:56,537
I DIDN’T KILL HER.

390
00:13:56,537 --> 00:13:57,838
IT’S HER OWN FAULT
SHE’S DEAD.

391
00:13:57,838 --> 00:14:01,442
IT’S HER OWN FAULT
I DIDN’T SAVE HER.

392
00:14:01,442 --> 00:14:03,377
I LOVE MYSELF
UNCONDITIONALLY.

393
00:14:03,377 --> 00:14:05,512
I LOVE MYSELF
UNCONDITIONALLY.

394
00:14:05,512 --> 00:14:06,647
I LOVE MYSELF
UNCONDITIONALLY.

395
00:14:06,647 --> 00:14:09,817
OW. OOH. OW. OOH.
OH. OWIE. OH. OW. OOH.

396
00:14:09,817 --> 00:14:12,018
OW. OW. OW.
OW.

397
00:14:12,018 --> 00:14:14,288
I NEED A VACATION.
SOMETHIN’ URBAN.

398
00:14:14,288 --> 00:14:19,158
THE QUAD CITIES,
OR DAVENPORT...

399
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:21,362
HMM. THINK I’LL RETURN
TO THE SCENE OF THE CRIME

400
00:14:21,362 --> 00:14:24,332
TO CHEER MYSELF UP.

401
00:14:24,332 --> 00:14:26,767
IT WORKED.

402
00:14:26,767 --> 00:14:29,703
HONEY, I’M HO--
OH, YEAH. YOU’RE DEAD.

403
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:35,308
♪ THE LONG
AND WINDING STAIRS ♪

404
00:14:39,247 --> 00:14:40,948
BOY, YOU KNOW,
A PAIR OF PANTS

405
00:14:40,948 --> 00:14:42,548
WOULD FEEL REAL GOOD
RIGHT ABOUT NOW.

406
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:46,887
MM-HMM.

407
00:14:46,887 --> 00:14:49,823
I’M GONNA PAD OUT
THE FILM STARTING... NOW.

408
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,428
UGH. GEEZ.

409
00:14:54,428 --> 00:14:58,365
HER BUTT MUST HAVE
WEIGHED A TON.

410
00:14:58,365 --> 00:14:59,833
LOCKS IN PLACE.

411
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:02,770
READY FOR MY NEXT VICTIM.

412
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:04,672
OH, LIKE COLUMBO’S NOT
GONNA FIGURE THIS OUT.

413
00:15:04,672 --> 00:15:05,738
MM.

414
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:07,675
[CREAKING]

415
00:15:07,675 --> 00:15:08,742
HMM?

416
00:15:08,742 --> 00:15:10,877
NOW,
CUT THAT OUT.

417
00:15:10,877 --> 00:15:12,880
SHE CAME OUT HERE
OF HER OWN ACCORD.

418
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,982
NO,
THE CAMRY.

419
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:16,450
WASN’T MY FAULT
IF IT GAVE WAY.

420
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:18,185
- MM-MM.
- WHY SHOULD I BE BLAMED?

421
00:15:18,185 --> 00:15:19,653
I HAD NOTHING
TO DO WITH IT.

422
00:15:19,653 --> 00:15:20,820
MM-HMM.

423
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,222
ANYWAY, NOBODY EVER
NEEDS TO KNOW.

424
00:15:22,222 --> 00:15:24,525
NOBODY WILL EVEN
CONNECT ME WITH HER.

425
00:15:24,525 --> 00:15:26,193
WHY SHOULD THEY?

426
00:15:26,193 --> 00:15:29,497
EXCEPT FOR THIS
WATCH OF HERS.

427
00:15:29,497 --> 00:15:30,965
THREE SKIPS.

428
00:15:30,965 --> 00:15:32,767
THAT’S THE END OF YOU.

429
00:15:32,767 --> 00:15:35,868
[BIRD SQUAWKING]

430
00:15:35,868 --> 00:15:36,937
YOU’RE GONNA DIE.

431
00:15:36,937 --> 00:15:39,005
YOU EVIL MAN.
[WHISTLES]

432
00:15:39,005 --> 00:15:43,177
I KNOW IT.
I’M LIVING IT.

433
00:15:43,177 --> 00:15:45,512
OH,
I HATE MONDAYS.

434
00:15:45,512 --> 00:15:49,750
[CRASH]

435
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,552
[FOOTSTEPS]

436
00:15:51,552 --> 00:15:53,987
OH, THE BRIDGE CLUB
WILL BE HERE ANY MINUTE,

437
00:15:53,987 --> 00:15:55,055
AND I’M NOT READY.

438
00:15:55,055 --> 00:15:56,490
OH, GEEZ.
DAYS LIKE THIS,

439
00:15:56,490 --> 00:15:59,025
I JUST FEEL LIKE HAVIN’
A SHOWER, A SAMMICH,

440
00:15:59,025 --> 00:16:01,562
AND STRAIGHT TO BED.

441
00:16:01,562 --> 00:16:02,628
[FOOTSTEPS]

442
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:03,630
IS THAT YOU,
BERT I. GORDON?

443
00:16:06,567 --> 00:16:07,802
OH.

444
00:16:07,802 --> 00:16:09,370
OH.
MY 10:00.

445
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:10,770
I’LL BE RIGHT WITH YA.

446
00:16:10,770 --> 00:16:11,838
TOM?

447
00:16:11,838 --> 00:16:14,007
SHE’S WEARING
TODAY’S PAPER.

448
00:16:14,007 --> 00:16:15,242
MEG.

449
00:16:15,242 --> 00:16:17,778
♪ IT WILL COME
BACK TO YOU ♪

450
00:16:17,778 --> 00:16:20,380
MEG.
IT’S YOU.

451
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:24,150
THIS IS THE GREATEST
CHICK TRAP EVER INVENTED.

452
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:25,752
OH, NO.
NO. IT’S...

453
00:16:25,752 --> 00:16:27,520
JUST THAT I WASN’T
EXPECTING ANYONE.

454
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,022
ANYONE ALIVE,
ANYWAY.

455
00:16:29,022 --> 00:16:30,923
WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP HERE?

456
00:16:30,923 --> 00:16:33,260
LOOKING FOR YOU.

457
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,695
WHAT ARE YOU DOING UP HERE
IN THIS OLD LIGHTHOUSE?

458
00:16:35,695 --> 00:16:36,763
WELL, I...

459
00:16:36,763 --> 00:16:37,832
[LAUGHS]
I LIVE HERE.

460
00:16:37,832 --> 00:16:39,933
I LIKE THIS QUIET.
I, UH...

461
00:16:39,933 --> 00:16:41,968
I-- I WANTED TO THINK.

462
00:16:41,968 --> 00:16:42,970
MM-HMM.

463
00:16:42,970 --> 00:16:44,037
I GUESS I’M WORRIED ABOUT

464
00:16:44,037 --> 00:16:45,572
THAT CARNEGIE HALL
THING NEXT MONTH.

465
00:16:45,572 --> 00:16:47,407
I WONDER
IF I’M GOOD ENOUGH.

466
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:49,943
YEAH. BEING AN USHER’S
A BIG RESPONSIBILITY.

467
00:16:49,943 --> 00:16:52,045
YOU’RE THE BEST JAZZ
PIANIST IN THE WORLD.

468
00:16:52,045 --> 00:16:53,513
OH, YEAH.
MUCH BETTER THAN ART TATUM,

469
00:16:53,513 --> 00:16:56,917
BUD POWELL,
BILL EVANS...

470
00:16:56,917 --> 00:16:59,118
I NEVER LOVED ANYONE
BEFORE IN MY LIFE.

471
00:16:59,118 --> 00:17:00,753
NOT THAT SURVIVED,
ANYWAY.

472
00:17:00,753 --> 00:17:05,058
NEITHER DID I.

473
00:17:05,058 --> 00:17:07,693
HMM?
ECLIPSE? HERE?

474
00:17:07,693 --> 00:17:09,195
DO YOU SMELL PERFUME?

475
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:11,932
I LIKE TO WEAR
CHANEL NO. 5, JUST...

476
00:17:11,932 --> 00:17:13,800
IT IS PERFUME.
ARPEGE.

477
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:16,703
I, UH, WANTED TO SMELL
PRETTY FOR YA. [LAUGHS]

478
00:17:16,703 --> 00:17:19,038
IT’S SO COLD
AND GLOOMY IN HERE.

479
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,107
[HUMS]

480
00:17:20,107 --> 00:17:21,175
IT GIVES ME THE CREEPS,

481
00:17:21,175 --> 00:17:22,877
HAVING THAT BIG LAMP
STARING AT US.

482
00:17:22,877 --> 00:17:24,645
I HAVE THE PRYING EYES
OF FURNITURE.

483
00:17:24,645 --> 00:17:26,280
...SINCE THE LIGHT
STOPPED WORKING.

484
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:29,082
I’M GLAD THEY’RE
GOING TO TEAR IT DOWN.

485
00:17:29,082 --> 00:17:31,352
COME ON. LET’S GO OUTSIDE
WHERE THE SUN IS WARM, HUH?

486
00:17:31,352 --> 00:17:32,920
YEAH.

487
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,555
WHAT A MORNING.
HUH?

488
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:38,092
I YI YI.

489
00:17:38,092 --> 00:17:39,427
[MEG]
COMING?

490
00:17:39,427 --> 00:17:42,628
BAH-- I DIDN’T KILL HER.
I’M-- OH. OH. [SIGHS]

491
00:17:42,628 --> 00:17:44,598
HER SWIMSUIT LOOKS LIKE

492
