00:25:33,165 --> 00:25:34,833
♪ I AM-- ♪

727
00:25:34,833 --> 00:25:36,402
HUH?

728
00:25:36,402 --> 00:25:39,772
♪ THE MEMORIES ♪

729
00:25:39,772 --> 00:25:43,977
ALL RIGHT.
ALLEN FUNT, WHERE ARE YOU?

730
00:25:43,977 --> 00:25:45,045
OOPS.

731
00:25:45,045 --> 00:25:46,580
AW, CRIPES.
I JUST REMEMBERED.

732
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:48,515
I BORROWED THIS
FROM THE LIBRARY.

733
00:25:50,883 --> 00:25:55,488
[INTERMITTENT TAPPING]

734
00:25:55,488 --> 00:25:56,555
HMM?

735
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:58,792
WHO’S THERE?

736
00:25:58,792 --> 00:26:00,493
IT’S MRS. ELLIS,
TOM.

737
00:26:00,493 --> 00:26:02,162
[GASPS]

738
00:26:02,162 --> 00:26:06,667
UH, HIYA, MR. B.

739
00:26:06,667 --> 00:26:09,235
HEY, IT’S,
UH, BLIND LEMON PLEDGE.

740
00:26:09,235 --> 00:26:11,070
I BROUGHT YOU
SOME FLOWERS.

741
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,172
UH, YEAH. JUST PUT THAT
IN THE GOLDFISH BOWL.

742
00:26:13,172 --> 00:26:16,008
SOMETHING THE MATTER,
TOM?

743
00:26:16,008 --> 00:26:17,777
WHAT MAKES YOU SAY THAT?

744
00:26:17,777 --> 00:26:19,745
YOU SOUND UPSET.

745
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:21,480
PERHAPS I’D BETTER
CHECK YOU ANOTHER TIME.

746
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,417
OH, NO.
NO, MRS. ELLIS.

747
00:26:23,417 --> 00:26:26,285
NO. COME IN.
SIT DOWN.

748
00:26:26,285 --> 00:26:27,820
THANK YOU FOR THE FLOWERS.
THEY’RE LOVELY.

749
00:26:27,820 --> 00:26:29,788
WATCH OUT, MR. BUCKALEW.
WATCH OUT, HONEY.

750
00:26:29,788 --> 00:26:31,590
LOOK OUT.

751
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:35,028
MRS. ELLIS...

752
00:26:35,028 --> 00:26:36,228
I WANT TO ASK
YOU SOMETHING.

753
00:26:36,228 --> 00:26:37,630
HOW MANY FINGERS
AM I HOLDING UP?

754
00:26:37,630 --> 00:26:38,698
STOP IT.

755
00:26:38,698 --> 00:26:40,333
IT SOUNDS KIND OF SILLY,
BUT...

756
00:26:40,333 --> 00:26:42,735
WELL, DO YOU BELIEVE THAT
THE SPIRITS OF THE DEAD

757
00:26:42,735 --> 00:26:45,072
CAN COME BACK
TO HAUNT THE LIVING?

758
00:26:45,072 --> 00:26:47,007
DO YOU BELIEVE IN GHOSTS?

759
00:26:47,007 --> 00:26:48,273
DO YOU BELIEVE
IN PEANUT BUTTER?

760
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:50,177
WHAT MAKES YOU ASK
A THING LIKE THAT?

761
00:26:50,177 --> 00:26:52,212
YOU HAVEN’T ANSWERED,
MRS. ELLIS.

762
00:26:52,212 --> 00:26:54,813
NOBODY BELIEVES
IN GHOSTS NOWADAYS.

763
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:56,482
DO YOU?

764
00:26:56,482 --> 00:26:58,918
IF ANYBODY WAS
TO ASK ME SERIOUSLY,

765
00:26:58,918 --> 00:27:00,453
I WOULD HAVE TO SAY NO.

766
00:27:00,453 --> 00:27:02,588
WHAT IF I ASKED YOU
DRESSED IN A CLOWN SUIT?

767
00:27:02,588 --> 00:27:04,723
A REAL ESTATE AGENT RUNS
INTO MANY STRANGE THINGS

768
00:27:04,723 --> 00:27:06,727
IN AN EMPTY HOUSE
SOMETIMES.

769
00:27:06,727 --> 00:27:07,927
WHAT KIND OF THINGS?

770
00:27:07,927 --> 00:27:11,597
WELL, THERE WAS
A FAMILY NAMED SAMUELS.

771
00:27:11,597 --> 00:27:13,433
THEY LIVED IN THAT
LAST HOUSE DOWN THE BEACH.

772
00:27:13,433 --> 00:27:14,767
ON THE LEFT?

773
00:27:14,767 --> 00:27:16,168
ONE DAY,
THEIR LITTLE BOY

774
00:27:16,168 --> 00:27:18,838
TOOK HIS DOG
AND WENT FISHING.

775
00:27:18,838 --> 00:27:20,173
THEY NEVER CAME BACK.

776
00:27:20,173 --> 00:27:21,908
AND NOBODY KNOWS
WHAT HAPPENED TO THEM.

777
00:27:21,908 --> 00:27:23,075
COINCIDENCE?
READ THE BOOK.

778
00:27:23,075 --> 00:27:25,245
AFTER THE SAMUELS’
MOVED AWAY,

779
00:27:25,245 --> 00:27:29,448
I SIGNED THREE TENANTS
DURING THAT FIRST MONTH...

780
00:27:29,448 --> 00:27:32,218
BUT NOT ONE OF THEM WOULD
STAY MORE THAN A FEW DAYS.

781
00:27:32,218 --> 00:27:34,487
BELIEVE IT OR NOT.

782
00:27:34,487 --> 00:27:35,955
THAT DOESN’T
PROVE ANYTHING.

783
00:27:35,955 --> 00:27:38,925
THEY COMPLAINED
ABOUT AN UNSEEN DOG,

784
00:27:38,925 --> 00:27:41,060
WHINING AND SCRATCHING
AT THE DOOR.

785
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:43,062
BUT THAT WASN’T WHAT MADE
THEM BREAK THEIR LEASE.

786
00:27:43,062 --> 00:27:45,232
THE DOG PIDDLED THE CARPET
AND I EVICTED THEM.

787
00:27:45,232 --> 00:27:47,267
IT WAS THE COLD
UP IN THE BOY’S ROOM.

788
00:27:47,267 --> 00:27:48,502
OH, YEAH.

789
00:27:48,502 --> 00:27:50,870
YOU COULD FEEL
IT IN YOUR BONES.

790
00:27:50,870 --> 00:27:52,105
A DEATHLY COLD.

791
00:27:52,105 --> 00:27:53,473
[WIND HOWLS]

792
00:27:53,473 --> 00:27:54,740
THE WALLS
WERE ALWAYS DAMP

793
00:27:54,740 --> 00:27:57,677
AND STAINED
WITH SEA WATER.

794
00:27:57,677 --> 00:27:58,745
- WHATEVER CAUSED IT,
- [DOG BARKING]

795
00:27:58,745 --> 00:28:00,680
THE THING CAME
BACK EVERY NIGHT.

796
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:02,415
DID YOU EVER SEE IT,
MRS. ELLIS?

797
00:28:02,415 --> 00:28:05,318
IT’S BEEN MANY YEARS
SINCE I’VE SEEN ANYTHING.

798
00:28:05,318 --> 00:28:06,552
OH,
HE DESERVED THAT.

799
00:28:06,552 --> 00:28:08,655
I’M SORRY.
I KEEP FORGETTING.

800
00:28:08,655 --> 00:28:09,722
DID ANYBODY SEE IT?

801
00:28:09,722 --> 00:28:10,790
YOU KEEP FORGETTING?

802
00:28:10,790 --> 00:28:11,892
PEOPLE WOULD SAY
THEY FOUND

803
00:28:11,892 --> 00:28:14,460
WET SEAWEED
ON THE BOY’S BED.

804
00:28:14,460 --> 00:28:15,528
WELL,
YOU CAN’T CALL

805
00:28:15,528 --> 00:28:17,497
WET SEAWEED A GHOST,
CAN YOU?

806
00:28:17,497 --> 00:28:19,832
TOM...

807
00:28:19,832 --> 00:28:20,967
WHAT’S WRONG?

808
00:28:20,967 --> 00:28:22,502
WELL,
I PUSHED THIS WO--

809
00:28:22,502 --> 00:28:24,470
I MEAN,
UH, NOTHING.

810
00:28:24,470 --> 00:28:26,605
YOU’RE RUNNING AWAY
FROM SOMETHING.

811
00:28:26,605 --> 00:28:29,175
YOU READ ME LIKE
A CHEAP NOVEL.

812
00:28:29,175 --> 00:28:31,343
WELL, TOM?

813
00:28:31,343 --> 00:28:32,512
WELL,
THE TRUTH IS

814
00:28:32,512 --> 00:28:33,947
I’M A CRAPPY JAZZ MUSICIAN,
ALL RIGHT?

815
00:28:33,947 --> 00:28:36,883
SOMETHING I...

816
00:28:36,883 --> 00:28:40,387
I CAN’T BELIEVE
EXISTS MYSELF.

817
00:28:40,387 --> 00:28:41,922
IF IT DOES EXIST,

818
00:28:41,922 --> 00:28:44,057
YOU CAN’T SOLVE ANYTHING
BY RUNNING.

819
00:28:44,057 --> 00:28:45,825
OH.
HOW ABOUT SPEED WALKING?

820
00:28:45,825 --> 00:28:47,993
THEN,
ON THE OTHER HAND,

821
00:28:47,993 --> 00:28:51,363
IF IT DOESN’T EXIST,
THERE’S NOTHING TO RUN FROM.

822
00:28:51,363 --> 00:28:53,165
DID YOU READ THAT
IN A FORTUNE COOKIE?

823
00:28:53,165 --> 00:28:55,768
YOU’RE A VERY WISE WOMAN,
MRS. ELLIS.

824
00:28:55,768 --> 00:28:56,837
YEAH.
IT’S JUST TOO BAD

825
00:28:56,837 --> 00:28:59,005
YOU’VE GOT
GREEN AND PINK ON.

826
00:28:59,005 --> 00:29:00,940
OH, AND THANKS
FOR THE FLOWERS.

827
00:29:00,940 --> 00:29:04,177
THEY’RE BEAUTIFUL.

828
00:29:04,177 --> 00:29:07,947
COME BACK SOON.

829
00:29:07,947 --> 00:29:09,015
LOOK OUT.

830
00:29:09,015 --> 00:29:11,450
[IMITATES FALLING]

831
00:29:11,450 --> 00:29:13,453
SESSIONS PRESENTS--
PAPER LACE.

832
00:29:13,453 --> 00:29:16,655
♪ THE NIGHT CHICAGO DIED ♪

833
00:29:20,260 --> 00:29:21,327
NO.
GO AWAY.

834
00:29:21,327 --> 00:29:23,897
MM. I PLEDGE ALLEGIANCE
TO THE FLAG...

835
00:29:23,897 --> 00:29:26,800
HALLOWED BE THY NAME.
[MUMBLING]

836
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:30,403
NO.
LEAVE ME ALONE.

837
00:29:30,403 --> 00:29:34,607
MM. TYPICAL LAZY MUSICIAN.
GET UP.

838
00:29:34,607 --> 00:29:37,543
SUDDENLY, IT’S THE SONG
OF BERNADETTE HERE.

839
00:29:44,717 --> 00:29:45,785
TOM.

840
00:29:45,785 --> 00:29:46,853
WHERE’S MY WATCH?

841
00:29:46,853 --> 00:29:48,353
TOM.

842
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:50,223
HELP ME, OBI WAN.
YOU’RE MY LAST HOPE.

843
00:29:50,223 --> 00:29:53,425
HELP ME.

844
00:29:53,425 --> 00:29:54,493
HE SEEMS REFRESHED.

845
00:29:54,493 --> 00:29:55,595
NO.

846
00:29:55,595 --> 00:29:59,498
HELP ME, TOM.
HELP ME.

847
00:29:59,498 --> 00:30:01,433
I THOUGHT I’D CHANGE
FOR THE DREAM SEQUENCE.

848
00:30:01,433 --> 00:30:02,502
- NO.
- HELP ME.

849
00:30:02,502 --> 00:30:04,837
VI, LOOK OUT.

850
00:30:04,837 --> 00:30:05,972
VI.

851
00:30:05,972 --> 00:30:07,373
HMM?

852
00:30:07,373 --> 00:30:08,508
VI.

853
00:30:08,508 --> 00:30:12,178
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

854
00:30:12,178 --> 00:30:13,378
HMM?

855
00:30:13,378 --> 00:30:16,048
NOW, I’M IN
THE SEVEN YEAR ITCH.

856
00:30:16,048 --> 00:30:17,050
VI, I--

857
00:30:17,050 --> 00:30:18,985
CON DIOS.

858
00:30:18,985 --> 00:30:21,287
VI?

859
00:30:21,287 --> 00:30:23,322
OH, MAN. I GOT
A HEADACHE THIS BIG,

860
00:30:23,322 --> 00:30:25,358
AND IT’S GOT BERT I. GORDON
WRITTEN ALL OVER IT.

861
00:30:25,358 --> 00:30:28,193
OH.
I GOTTA GET BACK TO BED.

862
00:30:28,193 --> 00:30:29,295
WAIT A MINUTE...

863
00:30:29,295 --> 00:30:30,497
I-- I’M IN BED.

864
00:30:30,497 --> 00:30:34,833
♪♪ [IMITATES GHOSTLY ECHO]

865
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:37,237
SHE’S SO TRANSPARENT.

866
00:30:37,237 --> 00:30:38,337
NO. GO AWAY.
YOU’RE DEAD.

867
00:30:38,337 --> 00:30:39,672
LEAVE ME ALONE.

868
00:30:39,672 --> 00:30:41,840
I’LL NEVER LEAVE YOU,
TOM.

869
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:43,375
I’LL ALWAYS BE HERE.

870
00:30:43,375 --> 00:30:44,443
MM.

871
00:30:44,443 --> 00:30:46,012
ALWAYS. ALWAYS.

872
00:30:46,012 --> 00:30:47,080
OH, TERRIFIC.

873
00:30:47,080 --> 00:30:49,715
I KILLED
THE LANDERS SISTERS.

874
00:30:49,715 --> 00:30:51,417
ALWAYS. ALWAYS.

875
00:30:51,417 --> 00:30:54,120
I CAN’T DECIDE WHICH ONE
OF YOU SCARES ME MORE.

876
00:30:54,120 --> 00:30:55,588
BYE.

877
00:30:55,588 --> 00:30:57,090
ALWAYS.

878
00:30:57,090 --> 00:30:59,558
SAVOIR FAIRE
IS EVERYWHERE.

879
00:30:59,558 --> 00:31:01,127
[LAUGHS]

880
00:31:01,127 --> 00:31:02,328
ALWAYS.

881
00:31:02,328 --> 00:31:04,330
SAVE ME,
TOM.

882
00:31:04,330 --> 00:31:05,698
OH, LOOK.
GET A LIFE.

883
00:31:05,698 --> 00:31:07,967
SAVE ME.
SAVE ME.

884
00:31:07,967 --> 00:31:10,670
IT’S HAYLEY MILLS
AND HAYLEY MILLS

885
00:31:10,670 --> 00:31:14,140
IN THE DEATH TRAP.

886
00:31:14,140 --> 00:31:16,042
[IMITATES GHOSTLY ECHO]

887
00:31:16,042 --> 00:31:17,943
DOODILEE-DOODILEE
DOODILEE-DOODILEE...

888
00:31:17,943 --> 00:31:19,012
DAMN.

889
00:31:19,012 --> 00:31:20,947
I’M STILL
A CRAPPY MUSICIAN.

890
00:31:22,882 --> 00:31:26,987
[SIGHS]

891
00:31:26,987 --> 00:31:28,053
HMM?

892
00:31:28,053 --> 00:31:29,488
[TICKING]

893
00:31:29,488 --> 00:31:31,690
OH, GREAT.
60 MINUTES IS AFTER ME.

894
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,627
[TICKING]

895
00:31:38,030 --> 00:31:39,532
HUH?

896
00:31:39,532 --> 00:31:41,333
BUT THIS BELONGED
TO V.I. WARSHAWSKI.

897
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:44,337
HMM.

898
00:31:44,337 --> 00:31:45,405
ALL RIGHT,
LOUIE.

899
00:31:45,405 --> 00:31:47,340
COME OUT WITH
YOUR HANDS UP.

900
00:31:52,412 --> 00:31:54,847
[HUMS]

901
00:31:54,847 --> 00:31:57,450
OH, GREAT.
I LEFT THE HOUSE ON AGAIN.

902
00:32:09,995 --> 00:32:11,630
SESSIONS PRESENTS--

903
00:32:11,630 --> 00:32:13,098
HAMILTON, JOE FRANK
& REYNOLDS.

904
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:15,502
♪ DON’T PULL YOUR LOVE
OUT ON MY HONEY ♪

905
00:32:15,502 --> 00:32:16,835
COMMODORES.

906
00:32:16,835 --> 00:32:18,672
♪ YOU’RE ONCE TWICE
THREE TIMES A LADY ♪

907
00:32:18,672 --> 00:32:19,705
SAMMY JOHNS.

908
00:32:19,705 --> 00:32:21,307
♪ MADE LOVE
IN MY CHEVY VAN ♪

909
00:32:21,307 --> 00:32:24,377
♪ AND THAT’S
ALL RIGHT WITH ME ♪

910
00:32:24,377 --> 00:32:26,478
THERE’S A BIG BAND
UP IN THE LIGHTHOUSE.

911
00:32:26,478 --> 00:32:27,613
CUCKOO.

912
00:32:27,613 --> 00:32:28,882
HEY.
COULD YOU TURN IT DOWN?

913
00:32:28,882 --> 00:32:31,117
SOME OF US HAVE
TO WORK IN THE MORNING.

914
00:32:33,318 --> 00:32:34,387
YOU KNOW,
HE’S GONNA HAVE

915
00:32:34,387 --> 00:32:35,922
HUGE CALVES BY THE END
OF THIS MOVIE.

916
00:32:35,922 --> 00:32:36,855
STAIRMASTER.

917
00:32:39,925 --> 00:32:41,860
NELSON RIDDLE,
KEEP IT DOWN.

918
00:32:48,968 --> 00:32:50,703
VI?

919
00:32:50,703 --> 00:32:53,038
LOOK. IT CAN MAKE HUGE
SHADOWS ON THE OCEAN.

920
00:32:53,038 --> 00:32:55,342
[LAUGHS]

921
00:32:55,342 --> 00:32:56,408
VI?

922
00:32:56,408 --> 00:32:57,710
"VI ASK VI?"

923
00:32:57,710 --> 00:33:00,647
[LAUGHS]

924
00:33:00,647 --> 00:33:03,648
YOU CAN’T HEAR ME,
CAN YOU?

925
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:04,983
’CAUSE YOU DON’T
EVEN EXIST.

926
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,418
CHUCK NORRIS IN OCTAGON.

927
00:33:06,418 --> 00:33:09,488
YOU’RE A SHADOW, PERHAPS.

928
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:10,757
LIGHT, PERHAPS.

929
00:33:10,757 --> 00:33:12,225
A BIT OF BEEF.
AN UNDERDONE POTATO.

930
00:33:12,225 --> 00:33:14,027
NOTHING MORE.

931
00:33:14,027 --> 00:33:15,093
PERHAPS.

932
00:33:15,093 --> 00:33:16,695
BUT...

933
00:33:16,695 --> 00:33:20,533
VI, JUST IN CASE
YOU CAN HEAR ME...

934
00:33:20,533 --> 00:33:21,767
I’VE COME
TO TELL YOU THIS--

935
00:33:21,767 --> 00:33:24,103
YOU SMELL BAD
AND YOU BROKE MY RAILING.

936
00:33:24,103 --> 00:33:26,238
I’M NOT GONNA PAY ANY
ATTENTION TO YOU ANYMORE.

937
00:33:26,238 --> 00:33:29,842
AND WHERE’D YOU PUT
MY DRESS SHOES?

938
00:33:29,842 --> 00:33:31,577
I’M GONNA LIVE MY LIFE
RIGHT HERE.

939
00:33:31,577 --> 00:33:32,645
OKAY.

940
00:33:32,645 --> 00:33:34,580
I’M GONNA STOP RUNNING.

941
00:33:34,580 --> 00:33:38,117
AND I’M GOING
TO MARRY MEG, VI.

942
00:33:38,117 --> 00:33:39,252
I’M GOING TO MARRY MEG.

943
00:33:39,252 --> 00:33:43,088
VI.

944
00:33:43,088 --> 00:33:44,557
THAT’S ALL I CAME TO SAY.

945
00:33:44,557 --> 00:33:46,492
VI?
COME ON. PICK UP.

946
00:33:46,492 --> 00:33:47,960
I KNOW YOU’RE THERE, VI.
COME ON.

947
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:51,297
...AS THOUGH
YOU NEVER EXISTED.

948
00:33:51,297 --> 00:33:53,098
I’M GOING TO MARRY MEG.

949
00:33:53,098 --> 00:33:55,167
REALLY, I AM.

950
00:33:55,167 --> 00:33:56,268
YOU KNOW,
I NEVER NOTICED

951
00:33:56,268 --> 00:33:58,170
THERE’S NO BUGS
AROUND THAT LIGHT.

952
00:33:58,170 --> 00:34:00,172
HMM.
YELLOW.

953
00:34:04,710 --> 00:34:07,347
JUST IN CASE YOU
CAN HEAR ME, VI...

954
00:34:07,347 --> 00:34:09,648
GOOD NIGHT.

955
00:34:09,648 --> 00:34:11,383
AND GOODBYE.

956
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:13,352
I’LL BE MAKING YOUR
LIFE A LIVING HELL.

957
00:34:13,352 --> 00:34:15,522
GOOD NIGHT.

958
00:34:15,522 --> 00:34:18,323
NO ONE WILL EVER
HAVE YOU BUT ME.

959
00:34:18,323 --> 00:34:21,227
[MUMBLING]
CAN’T HEAR YOU.

960
00:34:21,227 --> 00:34:23,628
♪♪ [PIANO]

961
00:34:23,628 --> 00:34:25,363
OF ALL THE LIGHTHOUSES
IN ALL THE WORLD,

962
00:34:25,363 --> 00:34:27,833
SHE HAD TO FALL
OFF OF MINE.

963
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:28,902
YEAH.
THAT’S A GOOD IDEA.

964
00:34:28,902 --> 00:34:30,035
THE MUSIC’LL
DRIVE HER AWAY.

965
00:34:30,035 --> 00:34:31,203
YEAH.

966
00:34:31,203 --> 00:34:34,040
IT’S DRIVIN’ ME AWAY.

967
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:35,207
[APPLAUSE]

968
00:34:35,207 --> 00:34:36,275
THANK YOU.

969
00:34:36,275 --> 00:34:37,743
WELL. HI.

970
00:34:37,743 --> 00:34:39,112
THERE’S COKE
IN THE REFRIGERATOR.

971
00:34:39,112 --> 00:34:40,245
HELP YOURSELF.

972
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:41,347
OKAY.

973
00:34:41,347 --> 00:34:42,815
AND THERE’S A MIRROR
ON THE TABLE.

974
00:34:42,815 --> 00:34:44,683
RAZOR BLADES.

975
00:34:44,683 --> 00:34:46,618
♪♪ PIANO MUSIC

976
00:34:49,788 --> 00:34:52,725
♪ I’D LIKE TO TEACH
THE WORLD TO SING ♪

977
00:34:52,725 --> 00:34:54,260
HEY.

978
00:34:54,260 --> 00:34:55,828
HEY.
THAT’S A ST. PAULI GIRL.

979
00:34:55,828 --> 00:34:58,330
PUT THAT DOWN.

980
00:34:58,330 --> 00:35:00,700
MRS. ELLIS SAID
YOU WANTED TO SEE ME.

981
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:02,635
WHAT ABOUT?

982
00:35:02,635 --> 00:35:04,303
I, UH...
SIT DOWN.

983
00:35:04,303 --> 00:35:05,772
I NEED SOME HELP
WITH AUTUMN LEAVES.

984
00:35:05,772 --> 00:35:07,072
I WONDERED
IF YOU’D, UH...

985
00:35:07,072 --> 00:35:09,208
TALK TO YOUR
SISTER MEG FOR ME.

986
00:35:09,208 --> 00:35:10,710
TELL HER HOW SORRY I AM.

987
00:35:10,710 --> 00:35:12,145
OKAY.

988
00:35:12,145 --> 00:35:14,547
YOU TELL HER I BEHAVED
LIKE A LITTLE BOY,

989
00:35:14,547 --> 00:35:16,115
AND I’M ASHAMED OF MYSELF.

990
00:35:16,115 --> 00:35:17,883
I’LL TELL HER.

991
00:35:17,883 --> 00:35:20,418
SHE DIDN’T CALL
ANYTHING OFF.

992
00:35:20,418 --> 00:35:21,487
SHE DIDN’T?

993
00:35:21,487 --> 00:35:22,655
MM.

994
00:35:22,655 --> 00:35:24,523
UH-UH. GUESS SHE’S
READY TO MAKE UP.

995
00:35:24,523 --> 00:35:27,860
I HAVE SOMETHING FROM
VICTORIA’S SECRET.

996
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:29,028
ARE YOU ALL READY?

997
00:35:29,028 --> 00:35:30,395
YEAH.
I’M ALL READY.

998
00:35:30,395 --> 00:35:32,632
HAVE YOU GOT THE RING,
AND EVERYTHING?

999
00:35:32,632 --> 00:35:33,900
- MM-HMM.
- LET ME SEE IT.

1000
00:35:33,900 --> 00:35:35,602
HOW COME YOU’RE NOT
WEARING ANY PANTS?

1001
00:35:35,602 --> 00:35:39,338
OOH.

1002
00:35:39,338 --> 00:35:41,707
[PLAYS CHOPSTICKS.]

1003
00:35:41,707 --> 00:35:43,108
OH.
DID YOU WRITE THAT?

1004
00:35:43,108 --> 00:35:44,643
IT’S FANTASTIC.

1005
00:35:47,580 --> 00:35:48,680
[GASPS]

1006
00:35:48,680 --> 00:35:49,948
TOM.

1007
00:35:49,948 --> 00:35:52,185
IT’S GORGEOUS.

1008
00:35:52,185 --> 00:35:53,452
BUT THINGS ARE
MOVING TOO FAST.

1009
00:35:53,452 --> 00:35:56,055
MEG SURE IS LUCKY.

1010
00:35:56,055 --> 00:35:57,122
CAN I TRY IT ON?

1011
00:35:57,122 --> 00:35:58,190
SURE.

1012
00:35:58,190 --> 00:35:59,725
ON WHAT?
YOUR WRIST?

1013
00:35:59,725 --> 00:36:02,328
WHAT I REALLY WANT
IS ONE OF MY OWN.

1014
00:36:02,328 --> 00:36:04,997
WELL, YOU MIGHT BE JUST
A LITTLE BIT YOUNG.

1015
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:06,365
I KNOW.

1016
00:36:06,365 --> 00:36:09,368
DEAR LITTLE SANDY.
SHE’S JUST A CHILD.

1017
00:36:09,368 --> 00:36:11,003
WHY,
DO YOU KNOW HOW OLD I AM?

1018
00:36:11,003 --> 00:36:12,872
I’M PRACTICALLY NINE.

1019
00:36:12,872 --> 00:36:15,708
WHY, IN CHINA
AND BORNEO AND INDIA,

1020
00:36:15,708 --> 00:36:17,042
AND PLACES LIKE THAT,

1021
00:36:17,042 --> 00:36:19,512
GIRLS ALREADY HAVE
HUSBANDS AT MY AGE.

1022
00:36:19,512 --> 00:36:20,547
MM.

1023
00:36:20,547 --> 00:36:21,980
I’D GET MARRIED TOMORROW

1024
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:23,917
IF I COULD FIND
SOMEONE LIKE YOU.

1025
00:36:23,917 --> 00:36:25,785
WELL,
LET ME CALL BILL WYMAN.

1026
00:36:25,785 --> 00:36:28,520
CAN’T I PLEASE
TRY ON THE RING?

1027
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:30,222
I JUST PUT
IT ON YOUR FINGER.

1028
00:36:30,222 --> 00:36:31,290
PUT WHAT ON MY FINGER?

1029
00:36:31,290 --> 00:36:32,358
THE RING.

1030
00:36:32,358 --> 00:36:34,027
I DON’T HAVE THE RING.

1031
00:36:34,027 --> 00:36:35,093
THAT’S WHAT I SAID.

1032
00:36:35,093 --> 00:36:37,028
THIRD BASE.

1033
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:41,267
WHOA.

1034
00:36:41,267 --> 00:36:42,768
OH.
THANK YOU, THING.

1035
00:36:42,768 --> 00:36:44,970
VI. VI.

1036
00:36:44,970 --> 00:36:46,805
IT’S THE GHOST
OF SEÑOR WENCES.

1037
00:36:46,805 --> 00:36:48,740
[GASPS]

1038
00:36:51,843 --> 00:36:53,078
TOM.

1039
00:36:53,078 --> 00:36:57,182
WHAT’S THE MATTER?
DID YOU DROP IT?

1040
00:36:57,182 --> 00:36:59,085
COULDN’T ROLL FAR.

1041
00:36:59,085 --> 00:37:00,753
IT’S GOTTA
BE HERE SOMEWHERE.

1042
00:37:00,753 --> 00:37:01,820
JAZZ HANDS.

1043
00:37:01,820 --> 00:37:02,888
JAZZ HANDS.

1044
00:37:02,888 --> 00:37:04,623
SANDY.
SANDY, DON’T TOUCH IT.

1045
00:37:04,623 --> 00:37:05,725
WHAT, TOM?

1046
00:37:05,725 --> 00:37:06,925
THAT.
RIGHT THERE.

1047
00:37:06,925 --> 00:37:08,327
SIT, THING.
SIT.

1048
00:37:08,327 --> 00:37:09,695
THERE’S NOTHING THERE.

1049
00:37:11,130 --> 00:37:13,365
COULD I HAVE ANOTHER
ST. PAULI GIRL?

1050
00:37:18,370 --> 00:37:20,472
ON MY SUMMER VACATION,

1051
00:37:20,472 --> 00:37:22,508
I BABYSAT FOR
A PARANOID PSYCHOTIC.

1052
00:37:22,508 --> 00:37:23,575
SANDY,
TELL ME THE TRUTH.

1053
00:37:23,575 --> 00:37:24,943
DIDN’T YOU SEE ANYTHING
RIGHT THERE?

1054
00:37:24,943 --> 00:37:27,547
THERE WASN’T
ANYTHING TO SEE.

1055
00:37:27,547 --> 00:37:29,382
YOU HURT.

1056
00:37:29,382 --> 00:37:30,415
I’M SORRY.

1057
00:37:30,415 --> 00:37:31,883
YOU NEED SOME DOWN TIME,
UNCLE TOM.

1058
00:37:31,883 --> 00:37:33,218
OH, I’LL...

1059
00:37:33,218 --> 00:37:35,020
FIND THE RING LATER.

1060
00:37:35,020 --> 00:37:37,222
YOU RUN ALONG NOW,
SANDY. I...

1061
00:37:37,222 --> 00:37:38,557
I GOTTA FINISH
MY PRACTICING.

1062
00:37:38,557 --> 00:37:40,092
GILLIGAN.

1063
00:37:40,092 --> 00:37:43,928
GOODBYE, SANDY.
I’LL SEE YOU LATER.

1064
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:45,230
YOU’LL BE ALL RIGHT,
UNCLE TOM.

1065
00:37:45,230 --> 00:37:46,698
[RUBS FINGER AGAINST LIPS]

1066
00:37:46,698 --> 00:37:49,368
OH, THAT HAND WAS
A NICE TOUCH, VI.

1067
00:37:49,368 --> 00:37:50,837
I KNOW NOW
YOU’VE COME BACK.

1068
00:37:50,837 --> 00:37:52,972
GUY.

1069
00:37:52,972 --> 00:37:55,040
BUT IT WON’T
DO YOU ANY GOOD.

1070
00:37:55,040 --> 00:37:58,243
BECAUSE I’M GOING
TO MARRY MEG.

1071
00:37:58,243 --> 00:38:01,147
NOW...

1072
00:38:01,147 --> 00:38:03,415
WHAT’D YOU
DO WITH THE RING, VI?

1073
00:38:03,415 --> 00:38:04,583
[LAUGHS]

1074
00:38:04,583 --> 00:38:05,583
VI.

1075
00:38:05,583 --> 00:38:06,618
HUH.

1076
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:08,087
WHAT DID YOU
DO WITH THAT RING?

1077
00:38:08,087 --> 00:38:09,722
[GULPS]

1078
00:38:09,722 --> 00:38:11,123
[IMITATES BELCH]

1079
00:38:11,123 --> 00:38:13,892
SESSIONS PRESENTS--
SUMMER HITS. TERRY JACKS.

1080
00:38:13,892 --> 00:38:15,995
♪ WE HAD JOY WE HAD FUN ♪

1081
00:38:15,995 --> 00:38:17,062
MARK LINDSAY.

1082
00:38:17,062 --> 00:38:18,497
♪ INDIANA WANTS ME ♪

1083
00:38:18,497 --> 00:38:19,565
PAUL ANKA.

1084
00:38:19,565 --> 00:38:20,667
♪ HAVIN’ MY BABY ♪

1085
00:38:20,667 --> 00:38:22,300
BARRY MANILOW.

1086
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:24,170
♪ YOU KNOW I CAN’T
SMILE WITHOUT YOU ♪

1087
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:25,738
VICKI LAWRENCE.

1088
00:38:25,738 --> 00:38:27,907
♪ THAT’S THE NIGHT THAT THE
LIGHTS WENT OUT IN GEORGIA ♪

1089
00:38:27,907 --> 00:38:28,973
RUPERT HOLMES.

1090
00:38:28,973 --> 00:38:30,743
♪ IF YOU LIKE
PIÑA COLADAS ♪

1091
00:38:30,743 --> 00:38:31,810
DONOVAN.

1092
00:38:31,810 --> 00:38:33,545
♪ WAY DOWN
UPON THE OCEAN ♪

1093
00:38:33,545 --> 00:38:34,613
OLIVIA NEWTON-JOHN.

1094
00:38:34,613 --> 00:38:36,515
♪ HONESTLY LOVE YOU ♪

1095
00:38:36,515 --> 00:38:37,850
BOBBY GOLDSBORO.

1096
00:38:37,850 --> 00:38:40,452
♪ AND HONEY I MISS YOU ♪

1097
00:38:40,452 --> 00:38:43,588
AND MANY MORE.

1098
00:38:43,588 --> 00:38:45,390
THEY WANT
US TO MOVE CLOSER.

1099
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:46,458
WHAT?

1100
00:38:46,458 --> 00:38:48,193
[STUTTERS]

1101
00:38:48,193 --> 00:38:50,328
LET’S GO SOMEWHERE QUIET,
LIKE THE BUS STATION.

1102
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:53,132
BUT I DON’T UNDERSTAND
WHAT YOU’RE GOING TO--

1103
00:38:53,132 --> 00:38:55,000
GOING TO SAY ’CAUSE IT’S
REALLY LOUD HERE AND--

1104
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:57,837
[LAUGHS]
NO MORE QUESTIONS.

1105
00:38:57,837 --> 00:38:59,105
YOU KNOW WHAT’S
WRONG WITH YOU?

1106
00:38:59,105 --> 00:39:00,105
WHAT?

1107
00:39:00,105 --> 00:39:01,173
YOU’VE BEEN
WORKING TOO HARD

1108
00:39:01,173 --> 00:39:02,240
GETTING READY
FOR YOUR CONCERT.

1109
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:03,975
YOU’VE BEEN
MURDERING TOO HARD.

1110
00:39:03,975 --> 00:39:05,043
MM-HMM.

1111
00:39:05,043 --> 00:39:06,112
...HERE ON THE ISLAND,

1112
00:39:06,112 --> 00:39:07,380
AWAY FROM ALL YOUR
MUSICIAN FRIENDS.

1113
00:39:07,380 --> 00:39:09,082
IT’S BEEN
GETTING YOU DOWN.

1114
00:39:09,082 --> 00:39:11,883
BUT I’LL TAKE CARE OF ALL
THAT ONCE WE’RE MARRIED.

1115
00:39:11,883 --> 00:39:13,152
MAYBE YOU’D BETTER
TELL YOUR MOTHER

1116
00:39:13,152 --> 00:39:14,453
THAT THE WEDDING’S
ON AGAIN.

1117
00:39:14,453 --> 00:39:15,520
HE’S MARRYING HER MOTHER?

1118
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,055
DON’T EVEN...

1119
00:39:17,055 --> 00:39:19,492
YOU’RE PRETTY SURE
OF YOURSELF, AREN’T YA?

1120
00:39:19,492 --> 00:39:20,727
YOU KNOW,
THE FIRST THING

1121
00:39:20,727 --> 00:39:22,795
YOU’RE GOING TO DO IS HAVE
A LONG VACATION.

1122
00:39:22,795 --> 00:39:23,928
IN HELL.

1123
00:39:23,928 --> 00:39:25,363
A WHOLE MONTH’S
HONEYMOON IN EUROPE.

1124
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,998
UH-UH.
YOU KNOW HOW MANY

1125
00:39:26,998 --> 00:39:29,068
HIT RECORDS I’D HAVE
TO SELL TO PAY FOR THAT?

1126
00:39:29,068 --> 00:39:30,335
MORE THAN ELVIS
OR THE BEATLES.

1127
00:39:30,335 --> 00:39:31,403
DAD’S FOOTING THE BILL.

1128
00:39:31,403 --> 00:39:32,672
IT’S HIS WEDDING
PRESENT TO US.

1129
00:39:32,672 --> 00:39:34,140
HE WANTED TO TELL
YOU HIMSELF, BUT...

1130
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:36,208
HE WON’T BE HERE TILL
RIGHT BEFORE THE WEDDING.

1131
00:39:36,208 --> 00:39:37,443
AND WHEN WE GET BACK,

1132
00:39:37,443 --> 00:39:38,977
I’M GOING TO HAVE
A BIG PARTY.

1133
00:39:38,977 --> 00:39:40,813
SO I CAN GET TO KNOW
ALL YOUR FRIENDS.

1134
00:39:40,813 --> 00:39:42,047
BEFORE YOU KILL THEM ALL.

1135
00:39:42,047 --> 00:39:43,482
WE’LL BE LIVING
IN A THREE-ROOM APARTMENT.

1136
00:39:43,482 --> 00:39:44,517
MOTHER AND DADDY WON’T MIND

1137
00:39:44,517 --> 00:39:46,118
IF WE USE THEIR
HOUSE IN BEL AIR.

1138
00:39:46,118 --> 00:39:47,285
HMM.

1139
00:39:47,285 --> 00:39:48,587
THEY SAY NOW THAT
I’M GETTING MARRIED,

1140
00:39:48,587 --> 00:39:49,855
IT’S TOO BIG
FOR THEM ANYWAY, SO...

1141
00:39:49,855 --> 00:39:51,457
THEY’LL BE TURNING IT OVER
TO US FOR GOOD,

1142
00:39:51,457 --> 00:39:52,425
ONE OF THESE DAYS.

1143
00:39:52,425 --> 00:39:54,527
ARE YOU TRYING TO SPOIL ME?

1144
00:39:54,527 --> 00:39:57,863
KIND OF LIKE
VI’S BODY IS SPOILING?

1145
00:39:57,863 --> 00:39:59,465
COME ON UP
TO THE HOUSE A MINUTE.

1146
00:39:59,465 --> 00:40:00,665
I WANT YOU
TO SEE SOMETHING.

1147
00:40:00,665 --> 00:40:01,733
- YES.
- WHAT?

1148
00:40:01,733 --> 00:40:02,868
- MY WEDDING GOWN.
- OH.

1149
00:40:02,868 --> 00:40:04,703
ISN’T THAT SUPPOSED
TO BE BAD LUCK?

1150
00:40:04,703 --> 00:40:05,972
YOU’RE NOT
SUPERSTITIOUS ABOUT

1151
00:40:05,972 --> 00:40:07,740
THINGS LIKE THAT,
ARE YOU?

1152
00:40:07,740 --> 00:40:09,108
NO. NO.
OF COURSE NOT.

1153
00:40:09,108 --> 00:40:10,608
OH. LOOK OUT FOR
THAT HAND, THERE.

1154
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:12,077
WHATEVER YOU DO.
[LAUGHS]

1155
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:27,627
♪ THE SNOWBIRD SINGS
THE SONG HE ALWAYS SINGS ♪

1156
00:40:27,627 --> 00:40:28,927
HEY, UH, JOEL.
WHAT’S GOIN’ ON?

1157
00:40:28,927 --> 00:40:31,230
OH. WELL, CROW,
IN TODAY’S EXPERIMENT

1158
00:40:31,230 --> 00:40:32,765
THE MAIN CHARACTER
ALLOWED A SINGER

1159
00:40:32,765 --> 00:40:33,865
TO PLUMMET TO HER DEATH.

1160
00:40:33,865 --> 00:40:35,133
AND I THOUGHT
IT’D BE INTERESTING

1161
00:40:35,133 --> 00:40:37,102
IF WE WERE TO TAKE
SOME OF TODAY’S SINGERS--

1162
00:40:37,102 --> 00:40:39,070
AND MAKE ’EM PLUMMET
TO THEIR DEATH?

1163
00:40:39,070 --> 00:40:40,138
WHAT A GREAT IDEA.

1164
00:40:40,138 --> 00:40:41,507
JOEL ROBINSON,
I COULD KISS YOU.

1165
00:40:41,507 --> 00:40:42,742
WHOA.
WAIT A MINUTE.

1166
00:40:42,742 --> 00:40:44,610
NOBODY IS GOING TO PLUMMET
TO THEIR DEATH HERE.

1167
00:40:44,610 --> 00:40:45,743
- OH.
- YOU KNOW?

1168
00:40:45,743 --> 00:40:47,012
WE’LL PUT A TRAMPOLINE
DOWN THERE,

1169
00:40:47,012 --> 00:40:48,080
ATTACH A BUNGEE CORD--

1170
00:40:48,080 --> 00:40:49,315
- TO THEIR NECK.
- YEAH. [LAUGHS]

1171
00:40:49,315 --> 00:40:50,983
NO.
NOBODY’S GONNA GET KILLED.

1172
00:40:50,983 --> 00:40:53,052
WE JUST WANNA PUT
THE FEAR OF GOD INTO ’EM

1173
00:40:53,052 --> 00:40:54,320
- FOR A LITTLE BIT, OKAY?
- OH.

1174
00:40:54,320 --> 00:40:56,622
SO, WHICH OF TODAY’S
POP SINGERS

1175
00:40:56,622 --> 00:40:58,757
WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE DROP
FROM A TALL LIGHTHOUSE?

1176
00:40:58,757 --> 00:41:00,658
OH, WELL, MY FIRST CHOICE
WOULD BE KENNY ROGERS.

1177
00:41:00,658 --> 00:41:03,195
I’D LIKE TO WATCH HIM HANG
BY HIS BEARD FOR A WHILE

1178
00:41:03,195 --> 00:41:04,830
TILL HE PLEADED FOR MERCY
AND FINALLY ADMITTED

1179
00:41:04,830 --> 00:41:06,498
THAT HE WAS
THE COWARD OF THE COUNTY.

1180
00:41:06,498 --> 00:41:07,567
OH,
REUBEN JAMES...

1181
00:41:07,567 --> 00:41:08,633
[ALL IMITATE SCREAMING]

1182
00:41:08,633 --> 00:41:09,702
[LAUGHTER]

1183
00:41:09,702 --> 00:41:10,970
YOU KNOW,
I’D LIKE TO SEE

1184
00:41:10,970 --> 00:41:12,572
THE MANHATTAN TRANSFER
ALL PLUNGE TO THEIR DOOM.

1185
00:41:12,572 --> 00:41:15,373
- OKAY.
- INSTEAD OF SINGIN’ SCAT,
THEY COULD BE SCAT.

1186
00:41:15,373 --> 00:41:17,677
AH, DO DO DA DA
DA, DA, DA.

1187
00:41:17,677 --> 00:41:19,110
[LAUGHTER]

1188
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:20,512
OH. FUN.

1189
00:41:20,512 --> 00:41:21,780
HEY. DON’T FORGET
KENNY LOGGINS.

1190
00:41:21,780 --> 00:41:23,348
- OKAY.
- OH NO, HE’S TOO SKINNY.

1191
00:41:23,348 --> 00:41:26,252
- HE’D JUST FLOAT.
- OH. UH... WELL THEN,
JIM MESSINA.

1192
00:41:26,252 --> 00:41:28,387
- OKAY.
- THINK I’M GONNA
HAVE A SON-- AAH!

1193
00:41:28,387 --> 00:41:29,455
[LAUGHTER]

1194
00:41:29,455 --> 00:41:30,522
LET’S TRY
KENNY LOGGINS ANYWAY.

1195
00:41:30,522 --> 00:41:32,525
OH, FALLING INTO
THE DANGER ZONE.

1196
00:41:32,525 --> 00:41:33,992
HE FELL GOOD.

1197
00:41:33,992 --> 00:41:35,660
YOU KNOW, NOW, REMEMBER,
WE’RE NOT KILLIN’ ANYBODY.

1198
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,728
- OH, YES WE ARE.
- YEAH.

1199
00:41:36,728 --> 00:41:37,763
WHAT ABOUT DR. HOOK?

1200
00:41:37,763 --> 00:41:39,265
OH, I’M SYLVIA’S MOTHER,
AH...

1201
00:41:39,265 --> 00:41:40,933
PHYSICIAN,
HEAL THYSELF.

1202
00:41:40,933 --> 00:41:42,668
- JONATHAN EDWARDS.
- AHH.

1203
00:41:42,668 --> 00:41:43,735
- DONOVAN.
- AHH.

1204
00:41:43,735 --> 00:41:45,103
UH, [STUTTERS]
LIONEL RICHIE.

1205
00:41:45,103 --> 00:41:46,572
- AHH.
- UH, MICHAEL BOLTON.

1206
00:41:46,572 --> 00:41:47,640
- AHH.
- BEN SIDRAN.

1207
00:41:47,640 --> 00:41:49,007
- AHH.
- MICHAEL FRANKS.

1208
00:41:49,007 --> 00:41:50,075
AHH.
POPSICLE TOES.

1209
00:41:50,075 --> 00:41:51,143
NEW KIDS ON THE BLOCK.

1210
00:41:51,143 --> 00:41:52,210
AHH.

1211
00:41:52,210 --> 00:41:53,278
STARLAND VOCAL BAND.

1212
00:41:53,278 --> 00:41:55,013
- AHH.
- AFTERNOON "DE-DIE."

1213
00:41:55,013 --> 00:41:56,248
OH,
THE CARNAGE.

1214
00:41:56,248 --> 00:41:57,315
[LAUGHS]

1215
00:41:57,315 --> 00:41:58,383
- OKAY.
- AH.

1216
00:41:58,383 --> 00:41:59,452
THAT WAS--
IT’S PRETTY FUN.

1217
00:41:59,452 --> 00:42:01,187
DO YOU GUYS MIND
IF I TRY ONE?

1218
00:42:01,187 --> 00:42:02,253
[BOTH]
OH, SURE.

1219
00:42:02,253 --> 00:42:03,755
OKAY.
HOW ABOUT, UH...

1220
00:42:03,755 --> 00:42:05,490
PETER HIMMELMAN.
AHH.

1221
00:42:05,490 --> 00:42:07,292
AHH.
[LAUGHTER]

1222
00:42:07,292 --> 00:42:09,060
THAT FELT GOOD.
OKAY.

1223
00:42:09,060 --> 00:42:10,128
TIME’S RUNNING OUT.

1224
00:42:10,128 --> 00:42:11,597
YOU EACH GET ONE
MORE CHOICE. OKAY?

1225
00:42:11,597 --> 00:42:13,198
[BOTH]
HMM.

1226
00:42:13,198 --> 00:42:14,267
OH, UH...

1227
00:42:14,267 --> 00:42:15,333
- ANNE MURRAY.
- OKAY.

1228
00:42:15,333 --> 00:42:16,402
YEAH.
[LAUGHS]

1229
00:42:16,402 --> 00:42:17,970
SPREAD YOUR TINY WI...

1230
00:42:17,970 --> 00:42:19,037
AHH.

1231
00:42:19,037 --> 00:42:20,105
[LAUGHTER]

1232
00:42:20,105 --> 00:42:21,340
CLASSIC CHOICE,
CROW.

1233
00:42:21,340 --> 00:42:22,775
OKAY. OKAY.
KENNY ROGERS.

1234
00:42:22,775 --> 00:42:24,410
OH, WELL--
YOU PICKED HIM ALREADY.

1235
00:42:24,410 --> 00:42:26,312
I KNOW, BUT I’M STILL
MAD ABOUT SIX PACK.

1236
00:42:26,312 --> 00:42:27,378
MM-HMM.
GOOD POINT.

1237
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:28,447
- DOWN YOU GO.
- NO, MAN.

1238
00:42:28,447 --> 00:42:30,082
DON’T TAKE YOUR
LOVE TO-- AHH.

1239
00:42:30,082 --> 00:42:31,583
[LAUGHTER]

1240
00:42:31,583 --> 00:42:32,752
[ALL]
AH.

1241
00:42:32,752 --> 00:42:34,118
FUN.

1242
00:42:34,118 --> 00:42:35,520
YOU KNOW, GUYS,
THIS WHOLE EXERCISE

1243
00:42:35,520 --> 00:42:37,088
WAS REALLY
KIND OF JUVENILE.

1244
00:42:37,088 --> 00:42:38,890
YEAH. PRETTY DESTRUCTIVE
AND NEGATIVE.

1245
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:40,758
YEAH. I THOUGHT IT WOULD
BE KIND OF CATHARTIC,

1246
00:42:40,758 --> 00:42:42,762
BUT IT REALLY WASN’T,
WAS IT?

1247
00:42:42,762 --> 00:42:43,828
DARN RIGHT,
IT WAS.

1248
00:42:43,828 --> 00:42:45,463
[LAUGHTER]

1249
00:42:45,463 --> 00:42:47,398
WE GOT MOVIE SIGN.
LET’S GO.

1250
00:42:55,107 --> 00:42:56,375
MY GARDEN’S FULL OF ROSES.

1251
00:42:56,375 --> 00:42:58,977
[ALL CHEERING]

1252
00:42:58,977 --> 00:43:01,680
[LAUGHTER]

1253
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:03,048
HELLO, STRANGER.

1254
00:43:03,048 --> 00:43:04,383
HI, KITTY.

1255
00:43:04,383 --> 00:43:06,252
WHERE HAVE YOU BEEN
KEEPING YOURSELF LATELY?

1256
00:43:06,252 --> 00:43:07,352
SOME BEAUTIFUL GIFTS
HAVE ARRIVED,

1257
00:43:07,352 --> 00:43:08,820
AND YOU HAVEN’T
SEEN ANY OF THEM.

1258
00:43:08,820 --> 00:43:09,888
HEY, LOOK AT THIS.

1259
00:43:09,888 --> 00:43:11,190
BUT YOU’RE HERE ANYWAY.

1260
00:43:11,190 --> 00:43:13,392
HEY. LOOK AT ME.
I WON THE STANLEY CUP.

1261
00:43:13,392 --> 00:43:15,160
[LAUGHS]

1262
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:17,295
OH, GEEZ. SHE’S INTO
THE EXCELSIOR AGAIN.

1263
00:43:17,295 --> 00:43:18,363
LOOK.

1264
00:43:18,363 --> 00:43:19,965
ANOTHER ONE.

1265
00:43:19,965 --> 00:43:22,968
UH-OH.
THERE’S MY GIRL.

1266
00:43:22,968 --> 00:43:24,002
JUST WHO IS HE MARRYING?

1267
00:43:24,002 --> 00:43:25,070
- HI, PAL.
- HI.

1268
00:43:25,070 --> 00:43:26,172
LOLITA.

1269
00:43:26,172 --> 00:43:27,873
IS EVERYTHING MADE
UP WITH YOU AND MEG?

1270
00:43:27,873 --> 00:43:29,240
WELL,
I’M WORKIN’ ON IT.

1271
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:31,777
BUT DON’T TELL ANYBODY
ABOUT MY TRIPPIN’ OUT.

1272
00:43:31,777 --> 00:43:33,078
NICE GIRL.

1273
00:43:33,078 --> 00:43:34,145
HI,
MRS. ELLIS.

1274
00:43:34,145 --> 00:43:35,380
TOM.

1275
00:43:35,380 --> 00:43:36,448
ANOTHER PAIR.

1276
00:43:36,448 --> 00:43:37,515
I KNOW.

1277
00:43:37,515 --> 00:43:38,583
PEOPLE MUST
THINK NEWLYWEDS

1278
00:43:38,583 --> 00:43:40,285
LIVE ON LETTUCE
BY CANDLELIGHT.

1279
00:43:40,285 --> 00:43:41,953
THIS MAKES NINE PAIRS
OF CANDLESTICKS,

1280
00:43:41,953 --> 00:43:43,388
AND 12 SALAD BOWLS.

1281
00:43:43,388 --> 00:43:45,890
AND MORE COMING EVERY TIME
THE MAIL BOAT ARRIVES.

1282
00:43:45,890 --> 00:43:47,660
MEG GOT HER WEDDING
GOWN TODAY, AND TOM--

1283
00:43:47,660 --> 00:43:49,962
OH, THAT VOICE.
UGH.

1284
00:43:49,962 --> 00:43:51,030
WHAT A BRIDE GOES THROUGH

1285
00:43:51,030 --> 00:43:52,865
TO MAKE HERSELF
ATTRACTIVE FOR YOU MEN.

1286
00:43:52,865 --> 00:43:54,265
LADIES,
BACK ME UP ON THIS.

1287
00:43:54,265 --> 00:43:56,768
THREE FITTINGS TO GET
THE BODICE RIGHT,

1288
00:43:56,768 --> 00:43:57,837
AND THREE LAYERS OF MESH

1289
00:43:57,837 --> 00:43:59,103
TO MAKE THE SKIRT
FULL ENOUGH.

1290
00:43:59,103 --> 00:44:00,072
YEE...

1291
00:44:00,072 --> 00:44:01,440
- [LAUGHS]
- HMM.

1292
00:44:01,440 --> 00:44:03,108
HARDLY SEEMS WORTH IT.
AFTER ALL, I’M ONLY...

1293
00:44:03,108 --> 00:44:05,210
DON’T LOOK NOW,
BUT ARTHUR MURRAY’S HERE.

1294
00:44:05,210 --> 00:44:06,345
MM.

1295
00:44:06,345 --> 00:44:07,913
SANDY, SEE IF THERE’S
A WINDOW OPEN.

1296
00:44:07,913 --> 00:44:10,148
THERE’S A COLD DRAFT
ALL OF A SUDDEN.

1297
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:13,085
AW, GEE. I COULD GO FOR
A COLD DRAFT RIGHT NOW.

1298
00:44:13,085 --> 00:44:15,120
SANDY, CHECK THE DOOR.
SANDY, DO THIS.

1299
00:44:15,120 --> 00:44:16,555
I HAVE TO DO EVERYTHING.

1300
00:44:16,555 --> 00:44:19,190
CHANGE THE OIL
IN THE CAR...

1301
00:44:19,190 --> 00:44:21,427
OH, MAYBE I SHOULD
CHILL THE CHAMPAGNE, HUH?

1302
00:44:21,427 --> 00:44:23,928
HOW ABOUT THAT?
WELL, I... [MUMBLES]

1303
00:44:23,928 --> 00:44:25,997
MM. YOU KNOW, BOOZE IS YOUR
BEST DRUG VALUE.

1304
00:44:25,997 --> 00:44:27,498
WHAT’S THAT SWEET SMELL?

1305
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:28,567
JAGERMEISTER, HONEY.

1306
00:44:28,567 --> 00:44:30,035
MUST BE THE FRESH ROSES.

1307
00:44:31,603 --> 00:44:33,605
MY ROSES NEVER
SMELLED LIKE THAT.

1308
00:44:33,605 --> 00:44:35,040
THEN IT MUST BE YOU.

1309
00:44:35,040 --> 00:44:36,475
IT’S A WOMAN’S PERFUME.

1310
00:44:36,475 --> 00:44:37,508
SAY.

1311
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,177
HELP ME MAKE ROOM
FOR THESE, DEAR.

1312
00:44:39,177 --> 00:44:40,378
IN MY DAY,
IT WASN’T CANDLESTICKS.

1313
00:44:40,378 --> 00:44:41,380
IT WAS TEASPOONS.

1314
00:44:41,380 --> 00:44:42,447
SHUT UP.

1315
00:44:42,447 --> 00:44:43,848
...RECEIVED NO LESS
THAN 78 OF THEM

1316
00:44:43,848 --> 00:44:44,850
WHEN WE WERE MARRIED.

1317
00:44:44,850 --> 00:44:46,052
[HIGH-PITCHED IMITATION]

1318
00:44:46,052 --> 00:44:47,452
MAYBE THAT’S A REASON
FOR HIS ATTITUDE.

1319
00:44:47,452 --> 00:44:48,487
LET’S DITCH HER.

1320
00:44:48,487 --> 00:44:49,888
WHEN HE WENT BACK
TO THE MAINLAND,

1321
00:44:49,888 --> 00:44:52,090
HE SAID HE WAS GOING
TO GO RIGHT TO THE OFFICE

1322
00:44:52,090 --> 00:44:53,292
AND STAY THERE
UNTIL THE WEDDING.

1323
00:44:53,292 --> 00:44:54,427
I’M SURE YOU’LL NEVER

1324
00:44:54,427 --> 00:44:56,095
TREAT YOUR WIFE LIKE THAT,
WILL YA, TOM?

1325
00:44:56,095 --> 00:44:57,763
YOU CLEARED THE ROOM,
GRANDMA.

1326
00:44:57,763 --> 00:44:59,498
HE ISN’T HERE,
MOTHER.

1327
00:44:59,498 --> 00:45:00,565
WHERE IS HE?

1328
00:45:00,565 --> 00:45:01,833
[MIMICS SQUEAKING]

1329
00:45:01,833 --> 00:45:03,435
I THINK MEG’S DOING
SOMETHING TO THE DRESS.

1330
00:45:03,435 --> 00:45:04,503
[SCREAMS]

1331
00:45:04,503 --> 00:45:07,105
- OH.
- NEXT.

1332
00:45:07,105 --> 00:45:08,740
GUESS SHE DIDN’T LIKE IT.

1333
00:45:08,740 --> 00:45:11,610
MY WEDDING DRESS.

1334
00:45:11,610 --> 00:45:12,878
NOW,
IT’S GARBAGE.

1335
00:45:12,878 --> 00:45:14,312
WHAT IS IT?

1336
00:45:14,312 --> 00:45:15,880
WHAT DID SHE FIND?

1337
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:16,982
SEAWEED.

1338
00:45:16,982 --> 00:45:18,650
WELL, SHE DID ASK
FOR THE MERMAID CUT.

1339
00:45:18,650 --> 00:45:22,053
WELL, WE’LL CHANGE THE
BRIDESMAID DRESSES TO GREEN.

1340
00:45:24,857 --> 00:45:25,923
TOM?

1341
00:45:25,923 --> 00:45:27,192
YES, MRS. ELLIS.
I’M IN HERE.

1342
00:45:27,192 --> 00:45:28,627
NO, I WASN’T PRETENDING
I WAS A PLAYMATE.

1343
00:45:31,430 --> 00:45:32,932
I BROUGHT YOU SOME HONEY.

1344
00:45:32,932 --> 00:45:34,198
OR IT MIGHT BE MOTOR OIL.

1345
00:45:34,198 --> 00:45:35,300
DON’T GET UP.

1346
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:37,102
I’LL JUST PUT
IT ON THE BAR HERE.

1347
00:45:37,102 --> 00:45:39,438
LET’S WRESTLE.
NOW.

1348
00:45:42,107 --> 00:45:44,375
I REALLY BROUGHT THE HONEY
ONLY AS AN EXCUSE,

1349
00:45:44,375 --> 00:45:46,077
BECAUSE I KNEW
YOU WERE UPSET.

1350
00:45:46,077 --> 00:45:49,147
TOM, THERE’S NOTHING
SUPERNATURAL ABOUT

1351
00:45:49,147 --> 00:45:51,082
WHAT HAPPENED
TO MEG’S DRESS.

1352
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:53,818
THERE MUST BE A LOGICAL
EXPLANATION.

1353
00:45:53,818 --> 00:45:54,887
I KNOW.
I KNOW.

1354
00:45:54,887 --> 00:45:56,355
MAYBE SHE WAS
ROLLING SUSHI ON IT.

1355
00:45:56,355 --> 00:45:57,455
BUT THE SEAWEED.

1356
00:45:57,455 --> 00:45:59,057
IT’S JUST LIKE
THAT SAMUELS BOY.

1357
00:45:59,057 --> 00:46:01,793
THERE HAVE BEEN
NO RECENT DEATHS, TOM.

1358
00:46:01,793 --> 00:46:04,897
[LAUGHS]
DEFINE "RECENT."

1359
00:46:04,897 --> 00:46:06,265
ANYWAY,
I’M SURE OF ONE THING--

1360
00:46:06,265 --> 00:46:07,265
I’M A TURTLE.

1361
00:46:07,265 --> 00:46:08,267
I’VE HAD ENOUGH OF HER.

1362
00:46:08,267 --> 00:46:10,102
WHO ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

1363
00:46:10,102 --> 00:46:12,103
OH. A--

1364
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:14,973
A FRIEND I USED TO HAVE.
A GIRL NAMED VI.

1365
00:46:14,973 --> 00:46:16,142
THAT I DON’T
HAVE ANYMORE.

1366
00:46:16,142 --> 00:46:18,210
SHE CAME OVER HERE
TO THE ISLAND TO SEE ME.

1367
00:46:18,210 --> 00:46:19,410
FELL DOWN.
[LAUGHS]

1368
00:46:19,410 --> 00:46:20,478
WE QUARRELED--

1369
00:46:20,478 --> 00:46:21,513
OFF THE ISLAND.

1370
00:46:21,513 --> 00:46:22,680
...UP IN THE LIGHTHOUSE.

1371
00:46:22,680 --> 00:46:23,982
SHE DIED--
DIDN’T-- DIDN’T, UH...

1372
00:46:23,982 --> 00:46:26,017
WELL, AT ANY RATE, SHE WENT
BACK TO THE MAINLAND.

1373
00:46:26,017 --> 00:46:27,118
THE GIRL-- THING...

1374
00:46:27,118 --> 00:46:28,320
ARE YOU SURE
THAT’S WHAT HAPPENED?

1375
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:30,288
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
AM I SURE?

1376
00:46:30,288 --> 00:46:32,123
WELL, MAYBE SHE DIDN’T
GO BACK TO THE MAINLAND.

1377
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:33,158
HMM.

1378
00:46:33,158 --> 00:46:35,127
MAYBE THIS GIRL
VI IS STILL HERE,

1379
00:46:35,127 --> 00:46:36,595
AND IS PLAYING
TRICKS TO GET EVEN.

1380
00:46:36,595 --> 00:46:37,662
HEY.
CHECK OUT PETER LUCAS.

1381
00:46:37,662 --> 00:46:38,730
NOW,
WHERE DO YOU SUPPOSE

1382
00:46:38,730 --> 00:46:40,198
A WOMAN COULD HIDE
ON THIS ISLAND?

1383
00:46:40,198 --> 00:46:43,068
WHO’S HIDING?

1384
00:46:43,068 --> 00:46:44,368
NEVER MIND,
SANDY.

1385
00:46:44,368 --> 00:46:46,538
AYE AYE, SIR.

1386
00:46:46,538 --> 00:46:48,907
THING WILL WORK OUT.
YOU’LL SEE.

1387
00:46:48,907 --> 00:46:53,245
[LAUGHTER]

1388
00:46:53,245 --> 00:46:57,548
TURN. TURN.
RIGHT.

1389
00:46:57,548 --> 00:46:59,050
GOOD.

1390
00:46:59,050 --> 00:47:03,255
[IMITATES DOG]

1391
00:47:03,255 --> 00:47:05,057
HELLO.

1392
00:47:05,057 --> 00:47:09,795
OH. HEY, A KITTY.
[IMITATES BARKING]

1393
00:47:09,795 --> 00:47:12,730
ANN B. DAVIS
AS MRS. LONGSTREET.

1394
00:47:14,900 --> 00:47:17,602
MRS. ELLIS.
MRS. ELLIS.

1395
00:47:17,602 --> 00:47:21,473
♪ IT SURE ISN’T YOU ♪

1396
00:47:21,473 --> 00:47:24,208
WHY ARE PEOPLE ALWAYS
SAYING "NEVER MIND?"

1397
00:47:24,208 --> 00:47:26,412
BECAUSE THERE ARE SOME
THINGS THAT GROWN-UPS

1398
00:47:26,412 --> 00:47:29,147
DON’T WANT CHILDREN
TO KNOW ABOUT, SANDY.

1399
00:47:29,147 --> 00:47:31,583
THOSE ARE ALWAYS THE MOST
INTERESTING THINGS.

1400
00:47:31,583 --> 00:47:33,018
AND ’CAUSE YOU’RE
A BAD PERSON, SANDY.

1401
00:47:33,018 --> 00:47:34,553
WHO IS TOM LOOKING FOR?

1402
00:47:34,553 --> 00:47:35,853
NEVER MIND.

1403
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:37,155
WHAT IS SHE,
LIZ SMITH?

1404
00:47:37,155 --> 00:47:39,423
I BET HE’S LOOKING FOR
HER AT THE LIGHTHOUSE.

1405
00:47:39,423 --> 00:47:41,560
HE’S ALWAYS HANGING
AROUND THERE.

1406
00:47:41,560 --> 00:47:43,795
THE LIGHTHOUSE IS A VERY
DANGEROUS PLACE, SANDY.

1407
00:47:43,795 --> 00:47:45,497
GO PLAY THERE,
SANDY.

1408
00:47:45,497 --> 00:47:48,000
IT’LL SOON BE TORN DOWN.

1409
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:50,168
THAT DOESN’T KEEP PEOPLE
FROM GOING THERE.

1410
00:47:50,168 --> 00:47:52,437
BUT YOU MUSTN’T
GO THERE, SANDY.

1411
00:47:52,437 --> 00:47:56,107
NOT EVER.
RUN ALONG HOME NOW.

1412
00:47:56,107 --> 00:47:59,645
GEE, YOU’RE A SPOOKY,
OLD DAME.

1413
00:47:59,645 --> 00:48:02,447
LEFT. LEFT, MR. BUCKAL--
OH, HONEY. LOOK OUT...

1414
00:48:02,447 --> 00:48:03,682
CONK.

1415
00:48:05,117 --> 00:48:06,952
THE DOG’S PLAYING
A CRUEL JOKE ON HER.

1416
00:48:06,952 --> 00:48:08,020
[DOG BARKS]

1417
00:48:08,020 --> 00:48:09,520
WILFRED.

1418
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:10,822
WOOF. I GUESS
WHAT I’M SAYING IS...

1419
00:48:10,822 --> 00:48:12,090
I DON’T WANNA GO IN THERE.

1420
00:48:12,090 --> 00:48:15,160
I’M SURPRISED AT YOU.

1421
00:48:15,160 --> 00:48:17,295
YOU’RE BEING
AS SILLY AS TOM.

1422
00:48:17,295 --> 00:48:21,032
DON’T EVER SAY THAT.

1423
00:48:21,032 --> 00:48:24,035
ALL RIGHT.
I’LL GO ALONE.

1424
00:48:24,035 --> 00:48:27,872
[DOG BARKING]

1425
00:48:30,208 --> 00:48:32,343
YOUNG LADY?

1426
00:48:32,343 --> 00:48:33,412
YOUNG LADY?

1427
00:48:33,412 --> 00:48:37,715
YOUNG, HELLO, LADY.
MRS. LADY THING?

1428
00:48:37,715 --> 00:48:38,850
WHY,
IT’S MRS. BUTTERWORTH.

1429
00:48:38,850 --> 00:48:41,720
THAT’S A LOVELY PERFUME
YOU’RE WEARING.

1430
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:43,422
IT’S NO USE.

1431
00:48:43,422 --> 00:48:45,190
I KNOW YOU’RE
IN HERE SOMEWHERE.

1432
00:48:45,190 --> 00:48:47,058
[DISTANT ECHOES]

1433
00:48:47,058 --> 00:48:48,893
I CAN HEAR YOU TOO.

1434
00:48:48,893 --> 00:48:51,630
DON’T YOU THINK IT’S
RIDICULOUS TO HIDE?

1435
00:48:51,630 --> 00:48:53,432
JUST A SECOND.
I’M IN THE BATHROOM.

1436
00:48:53,432 --> 00:48:55,700
THERE’S SOMETHING
I WANT TO SAY TO YOU.

1437
00:48:55,700 --> 00:48:56,968
GRAB SOMETHING
OUT OF THE FRIDGE.

1438
00:48:56,968 --> 00:48:58,037
I’LL BE RIGHT DOWN.

1439
00:48:58,037 --> 00:48:59,103
IF YOU WON’T,

1440
00:48:59,103 --> 00:49:00,572
THEN I’LL
GO UP AND FIND YOU.

1441
00:49:00,572 --> 00:49:03,942
WELL, BETTER UNPACK
ANOTHER BODY BAG.

1442
00:49:03,942 --> 00:49:05,377
- YEAH.
- MM.

1443
00:49:05,377 --> 00:49:07,445
UM, IS SHE WEARIN’ A LIFE
JACKET UNDER THAT SWEATER?

1444
00:49:07,445 --> 00:49:09,648
NO.
SHE’S MRS. MICHELIN MAN.

1445
00:49:09,648 --> 00:49:11,317
OH.

1446
00:49:11,317 --> 00:49:12,383
LISTEN TO ME, PLEASE.

1447
00:49:12,383 --> 00:49:13,752
[MOCKING]
"LISTEN TO ME, PLEASE."

1448
00:49:13,752 --> 00:49:16,120
I DON’T USUALLY
GIVE PEOPLE ADVICE,

1449
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,388
BUT TOM IS A DEAR FRIEND,

1450
00:49:17,388 --> 00:49:21,460
AND I WANT TO ASK YOU
TO LEAVE HIM ALONE.

1451
00:49:21,460 --> 00:49:23,695
ARE YOU LISTENING TO ME?

1452
00:49:23,695 --> 00:49:25,963
YOU MIGHT AT LEAST HAVE
THE POLITENESS TO ANSWER.

1453
00:49:25,963 --> 00:49:27,198
[VI LAUGHS]

1454
00:49:27,198 --> 00:49:29,467
MY, THAT’S A NASTY
LAUGH YOU HAVE.

1455
00:49:29,467 --> 00:49:31,570
WELL, AS YOU SEE,
I’M DEAD, AND...

1456
00:49:31,570 --> 00:49:33,705
WHAT TRICKS ARE
YOU UP TO NOW?

1457
00:49:33,705 --> 00:49:34,773
[FOOTSTEP]

1458
00:49:34,773 --> 00:49:37,575
WAIT.
LISTEN TO ME.

1459
00:49:37,575 --> 00:49:39,778
AN AGING KIM NOVAK
RECREATES

1460
00:49:39,778 --> 00:49:42,347
THIS SCENE FROM VERTIGO.

1461
00:49:42,347 --> 00:49:43,648
THIS PLACE
SOUNDS REAL NICE.

1462
00:49:43,648 --> 00:49:45,517
I LOVE WHAT I THINK
YOU’VE DONE WITH IT.

1463
00:49:45,517 --> 00:49:46,585
YOU KNOW YOU’RE WORRYING

1464
00:49:46,585 --> 00:49:48,053
AND FRIGHTENING TOM
HALF TO DEATH?

1465
00:49:48,053 --> 00:49:52,157
WELL, THAT’S THE POINT
OF BEING A GHOST.

1466
00:49:52,157 --> 00:49:54,558
I KNOW MEG
DOESN’T CONCERN YOU,

1467
00:49:54,558 --> 00:49:55,827
BUT YOU WOULDN’T
WANT TO MAKE

1468
00:49:55,827 --> 00:49:57,428
AN INNOCENT PERSON SUFFER,
WOULD YOU?

1469
00:49:57,428 --> 00:49:58,997
WELL, SURE.
THAT’S THE MOST FUN.

1470
00:49:58,997 --> 00:50:00,265
I WISH YOU’D SPEAK
MORE CLEARLY.

1471
00:50:00,265 --> 00:50:01,332
[VI WHIMPERS]

1472
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:02,600
WHAT DO YOU WANT?
I’M DEAD.

1473
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:04,602
MY "LARNYX" IS ROTTEN.

1474
00:50:04,602 --> 00:50:05,737
YOU’RE TRYING TO MAKE ME

1475
00:50:05,737 --> 00:50:07,738
SORRY FOR YOU,
I SUPPOSE.

1476
00:50:07,738 --> 00:50:09,875
BUT I CAN’T HELP THINKING
HOW FOOLISH YOU ARE,

1477
00:50:09,875 --> 00:50:11,543
PLAYING THIS ABSURD GAME.

1478
00:50:11,543 --> 00:50:13,212
I CAN’T HELP THINKING
HOW FOOLISH SHE IS,

1479
00:50:13,212 --> 00:50:15,080
CLIMBING UP THAT LADDER.

1480
00:50:18,450 --> 00:50:21,052
STAND STILL AND LET ME
TALK TO YOU, PLEASE.

1481
00:50:21,052 --> 00:50:23,688
HEY. I CAN’T SEE
MY HOUSE FROM UP HERE.

1482
00:50:23,688 --> 00:50:26,558
--ALL THE UNHAPPINESS
YOU NEED TO.

1483
00:50:26,558 --> 00:50:27,925
IT’S TIME YOU STOPPED.

1484
00:50:27,925 --> 00:50:29,660
I MEAN,
IT’S FUN, BUT...

1485
00:50:29,660 --> 00:50:31,095
YOU DON’T BELONG HERE,
YOU KNOW.

1486
00:50:31,095 --> 00:50:33,665
WHY DON’T YOU LEAVE
TOM AND MEG ALONE,

1487
00:50:33,665 --> 00:50:34,800
AND GO BACK?

1488
00:50:34,800 --> 00:50:37,235
[VI’S ECHOES]

1489
00:50:37,235 --> 00:50:38,637
WHAT ARE YOU SAYING?

1490
00:50:38,637 --> 00:50:40,205
SHE’S SAYING,
"WATCH THAT FIRST STEP."

1491
00:50:40,205 --> 00:50:41,840
I CAN’T HEAR YOU.

1492
00:50:41,840 --> 00:50:45,610
ON THE 50 METER BOARD...

1493
00:50:45,610 --> 00:50:46,678
YEAH.
THE DOG’S DOWNSTAIRS

1494
00:50:46,678 --> 00:50:48,213
CHECKING THE WANT ADS
RIGHT NOW.

1495
00:50:48,213 --> 00:50:50,082
YEAH.

1496
00:50:50,082 --> 00:50:51,750
WHAT A FIEND YOU ARE.

1497
00:50:51,750 --> 00:50:53,918
I HATE THESE
ONE-WOMAN SHOWS.

1498
00:50:53,918 --> 00:50:56,320
YOU’RE NOT FOOLING ME.

1499
00:50:56,320 --> 00:50:58,457
I KNOW EXACTLY
WHAT YOU ARE.

1500
00:50:58,457 --> 00:51:00,458
YOU’RE A SUPERSTAR.
THAT’S WHAT YOU ARE.

1501
00:51:00,458 --> 00:51:01,593
MM.

1502
00:51:01,593 --> 00:51:02,693
[PLAYS CHOPSTICKS]

1503
00:51:02,693 --> 00:51:05,163
♪ TORMENTED TORMENTED
TORMENTED ♪

1504
00:51:05,163 --> 00:51:07,132
♪ TOR-MEN-TED ♪

1505
00:51:07,132 --> 00:51:08,200
[DISSONANT CHORD]

1506
00:51:08,200 --> 00:51:11,002
OH.
JOHN CAGE.

1507
00:51:11,002 --> 00:51:12,737
NOT FAIR.

1508
00:51:12,737 --> 00:51:16,240
YOU’RE GETTIN’ THE PARTY,
PRESENTS, THE HUSBAND...

1509
00:51:16,240 --> 00:51:18,143
I GET NOTHING.

1510
00:51:18,143 --> 00:51:19,443
BE NICE TO ME,
PEANUT.

1511
00:51:19,443 --> 00:51:21,312
IN TWO MORE DAYS,
I’LL BE A MARRIED WOMAN,

1512
00:51:21,312 --> 00:51:22,380
AND YOU’LL MISS ME.

1513
00:51:22,380 --> 00:51:23,882
I’LL MISS TOM MORE.

1514
00:51:23,882 --> 00:51:25,083
SANDY.

1515
00:51:25,083 --> 00:51:26,752
OH. WHAT A BEAUTIFUL
CRYSTAL CHAMBER POT.

1516
00:51:26,752 --> 00:51:27,918
HOW’S MY FAMILY?

1517
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:29,020
WRONG FAMILY.

1518
00:51:29,020 --> 00:51:30,188
[BOTH]
DADDY.

1519
00:51:30,188 --> 00:51:31,823
AM I TOO EARLY
OR TOO LATE?

1520
00:51:31,823 --> 00:51:33,792
I’M SO HAPPY YOU
MADE IT IN TIME.

1521
00:51:33,792 --> 00:51:35,460
YOU DON’T THINK
I’D LET MY DAUGHTER MARRY

1522
00:51:35,460 --> 00:51:37,662
WITHOUT HER FAVORITE FATHER
BEING AROUND, NOW, DO YA?

1523
00:51:37,662 --> 00:51:38,797
OH.
[LAUGHS]

1524
00:51:38,797 --> 00:51:40,465
WELL, ROLL UP YOUR
SLEEVES AND PITCH IN.

1525
00:51:40,465 --> 00:51:41,833
THE PARTY’S RIGHT AFTER
TOMORROW’S REHEARSAL.

1526
00:51:41,833 --> 00:51:42,967
- HI, HONEY.
- FRANK.

1527
00:51:42,967 --> 00:51:45,237
DO I LIVE HERE?

1528
00:51:45,237 --> 00:51:46,303
WHERE’S THE GROOM?

1529
00:51:46,303 --> 00:51:47,705
WHERE’S MY SCOTCH?

1530
00:51:47,705 --> 00:51:49,107
WHAT’S THE MATTER
WITH HIM?

1531
00:51:49,107 --> 00:51:50,408
[MEG]
HE’S BEEN OVERWORKING.

1532
00:51:50,408 --> 00:51:51,477
ARE YOU A HUMAN?

1533
00:51:51,477 --> 00:51:52,877
AT THE PIANO,
I SUPPOSE.

1534
00:51:52,877 --> 00:51:54,478
PLEASE DON’T
START THAT AGAIN.

1535
00:51:54,478 --> 00:51:56,982
OH.

1536
00:51:56,982 --> 00:51:58,717
IT’S BAD ENOUGH TO ACCEPT
A MUSICIAN INTO THIS FAMILY,

1537
00:51:58,717 --> 00:52:02,520
BUT A JAZZ MUSICIAN
IS ASKING TOO DAMN MUCH.

1538
00:52:02,520 --> 00:52:03,688
WHY DON’T YOU GO TO BED,
DEAR.

1539
00:52:03,688 --> 00:52:04,688
YOU MUST BE TIRED.

1540
00:52:04,688 --> 00:52:05,690
YEAH.
STAY THERE FOR TEN YEARS.

1541
00:52:05,690 --> 00:52:06,858
WHAT’S THE MATTER

1542
00:52:06,858 --> 00:52:08,327
WITH A JAZZ MUSICIAN?

1543
00:52:08,327 --> 00:52:10,462
BE STILL,
BRAT.

1544
00:52:12,030 --> 00:52:13,265
POOR TOM.

1545
00:52:13,265 --> 00:52:15,367
MM.

1546
00:52:15,367 --> 00:52:16,935
I THINK THERE’S
ENOUGH NAPKINS THERE.

1547
00:52:16,935 --> 00:52:18,803
THANK YOU.

1548
00:52:18,803 --> 00:52:21,238
MM. OUT FOR MORE NAPKINS.
RAN OUT OF NAPKINS.

1549
00:52:21,238 --> 00:52:23,675
NEED LOTS OF NAPKINS.

1550
00:52:23,675 --> 00:52:26,612
OH. THIS IS WHERE THEY MAKE
CAPE COD POTATO CHIPS.

1551
00:52:26,612 --> 00:52:27,878
I THINK I’LL CHECK IT OUT.

1552
00:52:27,878 --> 00:52:31,750
TRICK-OR-TREAT
FOR UNICEF.

1553
00:52:31,750 --> 00:52:32,817
TOM?

1554
00:52:32,817 --> 00:52:33,885
SHE SOUNDS LIKE A SEAL.

1555
00:52:33,885 --> 00:52:35,820
TOM?

1556
00:52:39,423 --> 00:52:41,425
OH. SHE’S LIKE
THE GORTON’S FISHERMAN.

1557
00:52:41,425 --> 00:52:42,593
BABY.

1558
00:52:42,593 --> 00:52:44,595
TOM?

1559
00:52:44,595 --> 00:52:45,663
HMM?

1560
00:52:45,663 --> 00:52:48,533
OKAY.
I’LL COME BACK LATER.

1561
00:52:48,533 --> 00:52:49,600
HMM?

1562
00:52:49,600 --> 00:52:51,368
HMM.

1563
00:52:51,368 --> 00:52:52,637
STUPID HAT TRICK.

1564
00:52:57,475 --> 00:53:00,045
HEY.
TWO-YEAR SOBRIETY.

1565
00:53:00,045 --> 00:53:01,680
"MY NAME IS VI.
I’M A SCHNAUZER.

1566
00:53:01,680 --> 00:53:02,747
I BELONG TO TOM STEWART?"

1567
00:53:02,747 --> 00:53:05,017
[WIND HOWLING]

1568
00:53:06,718 --> 00:53:08,052
UGH.

1569
00:53:08,052 --> 00:53:09,287
WHAT DO YOU KNOW?

1570
00:53:09,287 --> 00:53:12,557
VI’S FIXED THE WINDOWS
AND THE RAILINGS.

1571
00:53:18,230 --> 00:53:19,497
DID YOU CALL A CAB?

1572
00:53:21,498 --> 00:53:23,568
YOU LIVE HERE,
KID?

1573
00:53:23,568 --> 00:53:25,570
JUST MOVE AWAY.

1574
00:53:25,570 --> 00:53:27,205
DON’T MAKE ME USE
THIS THING.

1575
00:53:27,205 --> 00:53:28,273
CAN’T YOU HEAR
OR SOMETHING?

1576
00:53:28,273 --> 00:53:29,707
I ASKED IF YOU LIVE HERE.

1577
00:53:29,707 --> 00:53:31,643
IN THE LIGHTHOUSE?

1578
00:53:31,643 --> 00:53:34,245
NO.
ON THE ISLAND.

1579
00:53:34,245 --> 00:53:35,580
ON THE ISLAND.

1580
00:53:35,580 --> 00:53:37,715
HEY.
I’M JUST A LITTLE KID.

1581
00:53:37,715 --> 00:53:39,250
LOOK, KID.
I REALLY DON’T CARE.

1582
00:53:39,250 --> 00:53:40,518
I’M A NEW YORK
METHOD ACTOR.

1583
00:53:40,518 --> 00:53:41,820
GIMME A BREAK.

1584
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:43,555
I’M LOOKIN’ FOR A GUY
CALLED TOM STEWART.

1585
00:53:43,555 --> 00:53:44,990
DO YOU KNOW HIM?

1586
00:53:44,990 --> 00:53:46,825
WHAT DO YOU WANT HIM FOR?

1587
00:53:46,825 --> 00:53:48,727
- IT’S LOU REED.
- MM-HMM.

1588
00:53:48,727 --> 00:53:51,062
HE WON 200 THOU
ON A SWEEPSTAKES TICKET.

1589
00:53:51,062 --> 00:53:52,497
I’M HERE TO GIVE
HIM THE MONEY.

1590
00:53:52,497 --> 00:53:54,665
I DON’T BELIEVE YOU.

1591
00:53:54,665 --> 00:53:56,300
OKAY. I’M FROM
THE LAND OF LEPRECHAUNS.

1592
00:53:56,300 --> 00:53:57,902
DIG?

1593
00:53:57,902 --> 00:53:59,972
I SEEM TO BE HAVING
A MEMORY PROBLEM.

1594
00:53:59,972 --> 00:54:04,042
GREASE MY PALM
WITH A SAWBUCK.

1595
00:54:04,042 --> 00:54:07,078
FIGHT OR FLIGHT?
FIGHT OR FLIGHT?

1596
00:54:07,078 --> 00:54:08,613
HMM.
FLIGHT.

1597
00:54:08,613 --> 00:54:12,483
HMM.
I SHOULDA WHACKED ’EM.

1598
00:54:12,483 --> 00:54:14,418
SPEAK TO ME,
OH, MAGIC PENDANT.

1599
00:54:19,123 --> 00:54:20,225
OH, GEE.

1600
00:54:20,225 --> 00:54:21,358
THE KID’S SINGIN’
LIKE A BIRD.

1601
00:54:23,862 --> 00:54:25,830
SESSIONS PRESENTS--
LOOKING GLASS.

1602
00:54:25,830 --> 00:54:28,032
♪ BRANDY
YOU’RE A FINE GIRL ♪

1603
00:54:28,032 --> 00:54:29,968
WHATCHA LOOKIN’ FOR,
DAD?

1604
00:54:33,338 --> 00:54:36,140
AND THE COLORED GIRLS
GO DOOT DOO DOO--

1605
00:54:36,140 --> 00:54:40,145
OH, WOW.
THIS IS A CRAZY PAD.

1606
00:54:40,145 --> 00:54:41,445
AREN’T YOU LOST,
BUDDY?

1607
00:54:41,445 --> 00:54:44,348
OH, MAN.
THIS SURE IS.

1608
00:54:44,348 --> 00:54:45,817
REALLY?
COME ON IN.

1609
00:54:45,817 --> 00:54:46,885
CAN I GET YOU ANYTHING?

1610
00:54:46,885 --> 00:54:49,053
NOW,
WAIT A MINUTE.

1611
00:54:49,053 --> 00:54:50,055
WHAT IS THIS?

1612
00:54:50,055 --> 00:54:51,088
HMM?

1613
00:54:51,088 --> 00:54:52,090
LOOK,
I DON’T WANT NOTHIN’

1614
00:54:52,090 --> 00:54:53,190
FROM YOU, DAD,
I REALLY DON’T.

1615
00:54:53,190 --> 00:54:54,458
SHE OWES ME A FIN.
THAT’S ALL.

1616
00:54:54,458 --> 00:54:55,893
AND I THOUGHT IT’D
BE NICE TO HAVE.

1617
00:54:55,893 --> 00:54:57,495
AND THE COLORED GIRLS
GO DOOT DOO DOO--

1618
00:54:57,495 --> 00:54:58,563
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

1619
00:54:58,563 --> 00:54:59,663
DON’T SWEAT,
DAD.

1620
00:54:59,663 --> 00:55:00,798
I DON’T WANT
NOTHIN’ FROM YOU.

1621
00:55:00,798 --> 00:55:02,200
SHE OWES ME A FIN.
THAT’S ALL.

1622
00:55:02,200 --> 00:55:03,435
UH, IN ENGLISH,
PLEASE.

1623
00:55:03,435 --> 00:55:05,937
I DON’T DIG WITH YOU,
FREAKY LACTOSE MAN.

1624
00:55:05,937 --> 00:55:08,840
WOW. YOU SURE HAVE
A NICE PAD, DAD.

1625
00:55:08,840 --> 00:55:10,442
NOW, LOOK.
I DON’T MEAN TO BE RUDE,

1626
00:55:10,442 --> 00:55:11,910
BUT YOU’LL EITHER
HAVE TO TELL ME

1627
00:55:11,910 --> 00:55:13,545
WHAT YOU’RE TALKIN’ ABOUT,
OR GET OUTTA HERE.

1628
00:55:13,545 --> 00:55:15,047
LOOK. THE BLONDE.
THE ONE WITH THE...

1629
00:55:15,047 --> 00:55:16,113
BUICK?

1630
00:55:16,113 --> 00:55:17,582
SHE OWES ME SOME BREAD.
THAT’S ALL.

1631
00:55:17,582 --> 00:55:18,950
IT’S NOTHING
TO GET BUGGED ABOUT.

1632
00:55:18,950 --> 00:55:20,418
WHAT SHE DOES HERE
IS YOUR BUSINESS.

1633
00:55:20,418 --> 00:55:21,853
HMM.

1634
00:55:21,853 --> 00:55:23,788
I CAN SEE YOU DIG ME,
DAD.

1635
00:55:23,788 --> 00:55:24,855
LOOK.
I MOTORED THIS CHICK,

1636
00:55:24,855 --> 00:55:25,923
VI MASON,
OVER TO THE ISLAND.

1637
00:55:25,923 --> 00:55:28,125
- I GOT A BOAT.
- A GRAVY BOAT.

1638
00:55:28,125 --> 00:55:29,660
NOW, WHEN SHE ASKED
ME IF I’D TAKE HER,

1639
00:55:29,660 --> 00:55:30,728
WELL,
I SAY OKAY,

1640
00:55:30,728 --> 00:55:32,397
BUT SHE SAID SHE
DOESN’T HAVE THE CHANGE.

1641
00:55:32,397 --> 00:55:33,665
THIS IS WHAT SHE SAID.

1642
00:55:33,665 --> 00:55:34,932
OKAY.
SO, WE MAKE A DEAL.

1643
00:55:34,932 --> 00:55:36,935
FIVE BUCKS OVER,
AND FIVE BUCKS BACK.

1644
00:55:36,935 --> 00:55:39,970
SO, YOU PLACED THE WOMAN
IN YOUR AUTOMOBILE?

1645
00:55:39,970 --> 00:55:41,105
I HAVEN’T THE FAINTEST IDEA

1646
00:55:41,105 --> 00:55:43,073
WHO OR WHAT YOU’RE
TALKING ABOUT.

1647
00:55:43,073 --> 00:55:45,510
LOOK, DAD.
ALL I WANT IS THE BREAD.

1648
00:55:45,510 --> 00:55:46,712
WHEN SHE DIDN’T
SHOW BY MORNING,

1649
00:55:46,712 --> 00:55:48,045
I FIGURED I’D BEEN HAD.

1650
00:55:48,045 --> 00:55:49,980
AND I KNOW SHE DIDN’T
GO BACK ON THE REGULAR RUN,

1651
00:55:49,980 --> 00:55:51,817
BECAUSE I ASKED THE PUT-PUT
JOCKEY AND HE SAID...

1652
00:55:51,817 --> 00:55:52,883
LOOK.
NO HABLA BEATNIK, OKAY?

1653
00:55:52,883 --> 00:55:54,118
NOW...

1654
00:55:54,118 --> 00:55:56,287
I’M A REAL SQUARE,
DAD.

1655
00:55:56,287 --> 00:55:58,490
I DIDN’T REMEMBER THE NAME
OF THE GUY SHE SAID.

1656
00:55:58,490 --> 00:56:00,725
DID NOT.

1657
00:56:00,725 --> 00:56:02,793
TODAY, I REMEMBER.
HOW DO YOU LIKE THAT?

1658
00:56:02,793 --> 00:56:04,062
HMM.

1659
00:56:04,062 --> 00:56:05,297
TOM STEWART.

1660
00:56:05,297 --> 00:56:06,430
MURDERER.

1661
00:56:06,430 --> 00:56:08,032
THAT’S THE NAME
OF THE GUY SHE SAID

1662
00:56:08,032 --> 00:56:09,100
WHEN WE MADE THE RUN.

1663
00:56:09,100 --> 00:56:10,368
SO, ENOUGH OF THIS JAZZ,
DAD.

1664
00:56:10,368 --> 00:56:13,605
COME ON.

1665
00:56:13,605 --> 00:56:15,640
I HAVE TO LEAVE.
GET OUT.

1666
00:56:15,640 --> 00:56:16,908
WELL...

1667
00:56:16,908 --> 00:56:19,243
MAYBE I BETTER WAIT AROUND
UNTIL THE CHICK SHOWS.

1668
00:56:19,243 --> 00:56:20,545
YOU’LL DO NOTHING OF THE--

1669
00:56:20,545 --> 00:56:22,313
KIND. TYPE. SORT.

1670
00:56:22,313 --> 00:56:24,648
ALL RIGHT.

1671
00:56:24,648 --> 00:56:27,085
MAYBE IT’S WORTH THE $5
JUST TO GET RID OF YOU.

1672
00:56:27,085 --> 00:56:28,152
HERE.

1673
00:56:28,152 --> 00:56:29,553
THERE YA GO.

1674
00:56:29,553 --> 00:56:32,223
FIVE BUCKS.
I’M SET FOR LIFE.

1675
00:56:32,223 --> 00:56:33,692
WHAT YOU DO IS YOUR
BUSINESS, DAD.

1676
00:56:33,692 --> 00:56:35,360
ALL I WANT IS WHAT’S
COMIN’ TO ME.

1677
00:56:35,360 --> 00:56:37,162
UH, WELL,
IT WAS NICE MEETING YOU,

1678
00:56:37,162 --> 00:56:39,897
MR. HEPCAT,
WAS IT?

1679
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:41,365
UM...

1680
00:56:41,365 --> 00:56:43,100
I’M COMING DOWN THE ROAD,
WILD MAN.

1681
00:56:43,100 --> 00:56:44,835
UH, KEEP ON TRUCKING,
I-- I THINK.

1682
00:56:50,007 --> 00:56:52,343
MM. I THINK THE DOG
WANTS TO EAT.

1683
00:56:52,343 --> 00:56:54,612
YEAH. I WANT
A KEN-L RATION OMELETTE.

1684
00:56:54,612 --> 00:56:55,880
THEY MAKE
A GREAT ONE HERE.

1685
00:56:55,880 --> 00:56:57,148
BE RIGHT WITH YOU,
MRS. ELLIS.

1686
00:56:57,148 --> 00:56:58,348
HEY.
YOU’RE MERRITT STONE.

1687
00:56:58,348 --> 00:56:59,417
THAT’S MERRITT STONE.

1688
00:56:59,417 --> 00:57:01,218
HUH?

1689
00:57:01,218 --> 00:57:02,753
PLEASE.
TWO BOILERMAKERS

1690
00:57:02,753 --> 00:57:04,922
IN A GRAVY TRAIN WITH
A BEER BACK, BARTENDER.

1691
00:57:06,992 --> 00:57:08,460
[LAUGHS]
SOME LIGHT BEACH FARE.

1692
00:57:08,460 --> 00:57:10,362
MM-HMM.

1693
00:57:10,362 --> 00:57:12,730
THERE YOU ARE.

1694
00:57:12,730 --> 00:57:13,798
PLENTY OF PICKLES?

1695
00:57:13,798 --> 00:57:16,067
YES, SIREE.
PLENTY OF PICKLES.

1696
00:57:16,067 --> 00:57:20,338
HEY.
WE’RE DRESSED ALIKE.

1697
00:57:20,338 --> 00:57:21,405
SO,
HOW’S LIFE

1698
00:57:21,405 --> 00:57:22,940
IN THE MERCHANT MARINES,
LITTLE GIRL?

1699
00:57:22,940 --> 00:57:24,408
[LAUGHS]

1700
00:57:26,543 --> 00:57:27,612
HERE WE ARE.

1701
00:57:27,612 --> 00:57:29,447
TUMBLER OF SCOTCH,
AND A MENU.

1702
00:57:29,447 --> 00:57:30,982
ANYTHING ELSE?

1703
00:57:30,982 --> 00:57:32,417
HOW ARE YOU,
MRS. ELLIS?

1704
00:57:32,417 --> 00:57:33,752
WARM,
MR. NELSON.

1705
00:57:33,752 --> 00:57:35,487
IT’S A VERY WARM DAY.

1706
00:57:35,487 --> 00:57:36,787
I THINK I’LL HAVE
SOMETHING LIGHT.

1707
00:57:36,787 --> 00:57:37,855
LIKE PORK RIBS.

1708
00:57:37,855 --> 00:57:39,157
UM,
EGG SALAD SANDWICH,

1709
00:57:39,157 --> 00:57:41,358
AND A GLASS OF ICED TEA
WITH LEMON.

1710
00:57:41,358 --> 00:57:42,627
DON’T LIKE SUGAR
IN MY TEA,

1711
00:57:42,627 --> 00:57:43,695
BUT PLENTY OF LEMON.

1712
00:57:43,695 --> 00:57:44,762
[LAUGHS]

1713
00:57:44,762 --> 00:57:46,130
WELL, HOW ABOUT
A NICE HAMBURGER,

1714
00:57:46,130 --> 00:57:48,098
OR A TUNA FISH SALAD?

1715
00:57:48,098 --> 00:57:49,600
WHAT’S THE MATTER
WITH YOUR EGGS?

1716
00:57:49,600 --> 00:57:51,068
OH, THERE’S NOTHING
THE MATTER WITH THEM.

1717
00:57:51,068 --> 00:57:52,337
- I JUST DON’T HAVE ANY.
- HMM?

1718
00:57:52,337 --> 00:57:54,472
I’VE BEEN OUT OF EGGS
FOR ALMOST A WEEK NOW.

1719
00:57:54,472 --> 00:57:56,740
KRAMER’S HENS
JUST STOPPED LAYING.

1720
00:57:56,740 --> 00:57:58,042
IT’S A FUNNY THING.

1721
00:57:58,042 --> 00:57:59,777
NOTHING LIKE THIS
EVER HAPPENED BEFORE.

1722
00:57:59,777 --> 00:58:00,912
EXCEPT ONCE.

1723
00:58:00,912 --> 00:58:02,713
ABOUT THE TIME
THE SAMUELS BOY DIED.

1724
00:58:02,713 --> 00:58:03,782
[IMITATES ALARM]

1725
00:58:03,782 --> 00:58:05,217
[ALL]
PLOT POINT. PLOT POINT.

1726
00:58:05,217 --> 00:58:07,852
WOULD YOU LIKE
A TUNA FISH SALAD?

1727
00:58:07,852 --> 00:58:09,253
JUST THE ICED TEA.

1728
00:58:09,253 --> 00:58:12,723
DO YOU CHARGE EXTRA
FOR THE PLOT POINT?

1729
00:58:13,925 --> 00:58:16,560
OH, THIS IS REAL GONE,
DADDY-O.

1730
00:58:16,560 --> 00:58:18,062
SAY, DAD.
COULD I HAVE A COKE?

1731
00:58:18,062 --> 00:58:19,897
HEY, POPS.
CATCH YA ON THE DRINK JANK.

1732
00:58:19,897 --> 00:58:22,267
THE HUBBARDS HAD TO SEND
OVER TO THE MAINLAND SPECIAL

1733
00:58:22,267 --> 00:58:24,068
TO GET SOME EGGS
FOR THEIR PARTY.

1734
00:58:24,068 --> 00:58:26,337
CAN’T BAKE A CAKE
WITHOUT EGGS.

1735
00:58:26,337 --> 00:58:27,672
HMM.

1736
00:58:27,672 --> 00:58:29,940
SPEAKING OF THE WEDDING,
ARE YOU STILL THERE, SANDY?

1737
00:58:29,940 --> 00:58:31,742
[SCREAMS AND COUGHS]

1738
00:58:31,742 --> 00:58:33,545
SHOULDN’T YOU
BE AT THE REHEARSAL?

1739
00:58:33,545 --> 00:58:37,148
HOLY COW.
CHARGE IT, MR. NELSON.

1740
00:58:37,148 --> 00:58:39,417
YOU KNOW,
MR. NELSON,

1741
00:58:39,417 --> 00:58:41,485
I WISH I COULD HAVE
MY SIGHT BACK,

1742
00:58:41,485 --> 00:58:43,855
LONG ENOUGH TO SEE
TOM AND MEG MARRIED.

1743
00:58:43,855 --> 00:58:45,690
THEY MUST
BE A LOVELY COUPLE.

1744
00:58:45,690 --> 00:58:49,227
LADY, YOU’RE SCARIN’
MY CUSTOMERS.

1745
00:58:49,227 --> 00:58:51,362
THEY’RE A HANDSOME
COUPLE ALL RIGHT.

1746
00:58:51,362 --> 00:58:54,465
TOM STEWART’S MARRYING
A BEAUTIFUL GAL.

1747
00:58:54,465 --> 00:58:55,533
AND THE NICEST
OF FAMILIES.

1748
00:58:55,533 --> 00:58:57,002
[SPITS]
TOM STEWART?

1749
00:58:57,002 --> 00:58:58,637
SAY, DAD...

1750
00:58:58,637 --> 00:58:59,903
WHAT DID YOU SAY
THE HANDLE

1751
00:58:59,903 --> 00:59:01,338
OF THE GUY
GETTING SPLICED WAS?

1752
00:59:01,338 --> 00:59:02,407
TOM STEWART.

1753
00:59:02,407 --> 00:59:04,142
GIRL’S NAME
IS MEG HUBBARD.

1754
00:59:07,345 --> 00:59:09,280
THIS CAT’S ONTO
MY HIP LINGO TOO QUICK.

1755
00:59:09,280 --> 00:59:11,215
I AM OUT OF HERE.

1756
00:59:11,215 --> 00:59:12,483
AND LITTLE SANDY
WILL BE STANDING

1757
00:59:12,483 --> 00:59:14,718
HERE TO MY RIGHT.
NEXT TO THE BRIDE.

1758
00:59:14,718 --> 00:59:16,520
IT’S NOT FAIR.

1759
00:59:16,520 --> 00:59:17,655
...AND YOU’LL
BE STANDING HERE.

1760
00:59:17,655 --> 00:59:19,523
THE PARENTS WILL
BE IN THEIR PEWS, AND--

1761
00:59:19,523 --> 00:59:22,593
AND THEN, THE MILKMAN
WILL ENTER FROM THE BACK.

1762
00:59:22,593 --> 00:59:23,695
MAY I HELP YOU?

1763
00:59:23,695 --> 00:59:27,332
YEAH. I WANNA SPEAK
TO TOM STEWART.

1764
00:59:27,332 --> 00:59:28,432
OH. AH. UH...

1765
00:59:28,432 --> 00:59:30,435
SOMETHING ABOUT,
UH, SOME HALF & HALF...

1766
00:59:30,435 --> 00:59:32,237
FOR THE WEDDING.

1767
00:59:32,237 --> 00:59:33,503
WHAT?
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

1768
00:59:33,503 --> 00:59:36,440
HEY. REALLY GONE WEDDING,
POPPY-O.

1769
00:59:39,143 --> 00:59:41,947
FORGIVE ME, TOM,
FOR I HAVE SLANG-ED.

1770
00:59:41,947 --> 00:59:44,015
YOU’RE INTERRUPTING
A WEDDING REHEARSAL IN THERE.

1771
00:59:44,015 --> 00:59:46,483
LIKE I SAID, DAD,
WHAT YOU DO IS YOUR BUSINESS.

1772
00:59:46,483 --> 00:59:48,953
I MEAN, IT’S CRAZY WITH ME
IF YOU WANNA MARRY ONE CHICK,

1773
00:59:48,953 --> 00:59:51,022
AND KEEP ANOTHER ONE
ON THE SIDE FOR KICKS. WOW.

1774
00:59:51,022 --> 00:59:53,023
BUT I FEEL SORT
OF A RESPONSIBILITY,

1775
00:59:53,023 --> 00:59:55,560
SEEING AS HOW I BROUGHT
YOUR BROAD OVER ON MY TUG.

1776
00:59:55,560 --> 00:59:56,627
SEE WHAT I MEAN?

1777
00:59:56,627 --> 00:59:57,795
WHAT ARE YOU DRIVING AT?

1778
00:59:57,795 --> 00:59:59,697
COME ON, DAD,
DON’T YA KNOW?

1779
00:59:59,697 --> 01:00:01,165
I GAVE YOU THE MONEY
YOU’RE AFTER.

1780
01:00:01,165 --> 01:00:02,833
- WHAT MORE DO YOU WANT?
- THREE MORE BUCKS.

1781
01:00:02,833 --> 01:00:04,968
IT SEEMS THAT OUR DEAL
IS IN LINE FOR SOME...

1782
01:00:04,968 --> 01:00:06,937
- RENEGOTIATIONS.
- WHAT--
- TOM. HURRY.

1783
01:00:06,937 --> 01:00:08,272
WE’RE WAITING FOR YOU.

1784
01:00:08,272 --> 01:00:10,908
YEAH. GO AHEAD BACK.
WE’LL PICK IT UP LATER.

1785
01:00:10,908 --> 01:00:12,677
TIME, I GOT PLENTY OF.

1786
01:00:12,677 --> 01:00:14,045
UM...

1787
01:00:14,045 --> 01:00:15,112
OKAY, THEN.
[CLEARS THROAT]

1788
01:00:15,112 --> 01:00:17,282
SORRY I WAS
THE WRONG TOM STEWART.

1789
01:00:17,282 --> 01:00:19,650
HOPE YOU FIND
THE RIGHT TOM STEWART.

1790
01:00:19,650 --> 01:00:21,418
HUH. MISTAKE.

1791
01:00:21,418 --> 01:00:23,420
SEEMS LIKE
A REALLY NICE GUY, UH...

1792
01:00:23,420 --> 01:00:24,988
JUST WISH HE WASN’T
BLACKMAILIN’ ME.

1793
01:00:32,130 --> 01:00:33,832
THE NAZIS FORTIFIED NORMANDY AND
WAITED IN THEIR BEACH HOUSES.

1794
01:00:33,832 --> 01:00:36,700
♪♪ [PIANO]

1795
01:00:40,672 --> 01:00:42,040
[HUMMING]

1796
01:00:42,040 --> 01:00:43,507
WAIT A MINUTE.
HE’S PULLING A SHIFT

1797
01:00:43,507 --> 01:00:46,977
AT HIS OWN PARTY.

1798
01:00:46,977 --> 01:00:49,313
♪♪ [PIANO]

1799
01:00:49,313 --> 01:00:51,482
TOMORROW NIGHT,
I’LL BE MRS. STEWART.

1800
01:00:51,482 --> 01:00:53,017
ISN’T THAT RIGHT,
MR. STEWART?

1801
01:00:53,017 --> 01:00:54,385
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

1802
01:00:54,385 --> 01:00:55,553
[SMOOCHING SOUND]

1803
01:00:55,553 --> 01:00:56,820
I’LL BE RIGHT BACK.

1804
01:00:56,820 --> 01:00:58,790
YEAH.

1805
01:00:58,790 --> 01:01:01,558
OH, AND-- HUH?!

1806
01:01:01,558 --> 01:01:03,060
DEVILED EGGS! NO!

1807
01:01:07,832 --> 01:01:09,033
- SWEETIE--
- ALL RIGHT, COME ON.

1808
01:01:09,033 --> 01:01:11,468
YOU’RE NOT PAID TO MINGLE.

1809
01:01:11,468 --> 01:01:13,805
- --I WANTED TO GET A DRINK.
- YEAH, I’LL GET IT FOR YOU.

1810
01:01:13,805 --> 01:01:15,873
JUST ONE MORE NUMBER.
I WANNA SHOW YOU OFF.

1811
01:01:15,873 --> 01:01:18,275
YOU PLAYED IT FOR HER.
YOU CAN PLAY IT FOR ME.

1812
01:01:24,448 --> 01:01:26,317
HEY, QUIT TALKING ABOUT ME.

1813
01:01:29,020 --> 01:01:31,822
WOW, NICE OF EDWARD TELLER
TO DROP BY.

1814
01:01:31,822 --> 01:01:34,658
OH, YOU KNOW,
SHOULDN’T WEAR BUFFALO CHECKS.

1815
01:01:34,658 --> 01:01:36,027
NO ONE SHOULD.

1816
01:01:36,027 --> 01:01:37,162
IT’S A JAZZ
MUSICIAN’S PARTY,

1817
01:01:37,162 --> 01:01:38,662
AND THERE’S NOT
ONE BLACK PERSON HERE.

1818
01:01:38,662 --> 01:01:39,930
AWW.

1819
01:01:39,930 --> 01:01:41,632
I NEED BOOZE. NOW.

1820
01:01:41,632 --> 01:01:45,002
HMMM.

1821
01:01:45,002 --> 01:01:46,270
DRINK IT. DRINK IT ALL.

1822
01:01:46,270 --> 01:01:47,505
SORRY I STARTLED YOU, TOM.

1823
01:01:47,505 --> 01:01:49,173
BUT CANDIDS ARE
THE BEST KIND.

1824
01:01:49,173 --> 01:01:51,575
I HAD MY MOUTH OPEN
AND MY EYES CLOSED.

1825
01:01:51,575 --> 01:01:53,343
- WHAT ELSE IS NEW?
- [MEG MUTTERS]

1826
01:01:53,343 --> 01:01:55,580
YOU DON’T LIKE IT,
I CAN TAKE ANOTHER.

1827
01:01:58,850 --> 01:02:00,918
NO.

1828
01:02:00,918 --> 01:02:03,153
PHOTOGRAPHS DO ADD
TEN POUNDS.

1829
01:02:03,153 --> 01:02:04,555
NO, THAT’S FINE.

1830
01:02:04,555 --> 01:02:06,090
- ARE YOU SURE?
- I’M SURE.

1831
01:02:06,090 --> 01:02:07,425
DARLING, LOOK--

1832
01:02:07,425 --> 01:02:09,593
NO, DARLING, YOU’RE REALLY
KIND OF UGLY IN IT.

1833
01:02:09,593 --> 01:02:12,230
I’M GONNA GET A DRINK.

1834
01:02:12,230 --> 01:02:14,532
I HATE PHOTO-COLLAGE.

1835
01:02:16,300 --> 01:02:20,070
JUST HAVE A BOTTLE
OF KETCHUP HERE.

1836
01:02:20,070 --> 01:02:22,773
[SERVO GULPS]

1837
01:02:22,773 --> 01:02:24,242
TOM, WHAT’S WRONG WITH IT?

1838
01:02:24,242 --> 01:02:25,577
NOTHING.

1839
01:02:25,577 --> 01:02:26,810
WHY, IT’S ONLY A PICTURE.

1840
01:02:26,810 --> 01:02:28,478
WHY ARE YOU SO UPSET?

1841
01:02:28,478 --> 01:02:30,013
I’M NOT UPSET.

1842
01:02:30,013 --> 01:02:31,648
- SHUT UP.
- TOM, WHAT’S BOTHERING YOU?

1843
01:02:31,648 --> 01:02:33,317
IT’S NOT AS IF
YOU KILLED SOMEONE--

1844
01:02:33,317 --> 01:02:36,687
- SHUT UP, SHUT UP!
- IS IT ANOTHER GIRL?

1845
01:02:36,687 --> 01:02:37,988
YOU CAN TELL ME. I--

1846
01:02:37,988 --> 01:02:39,857
I’LL TRY NOT TO BE JEALOUS.

1847
01:02:39,857 --> 01:02:42,560
WELL, OKAY. THERE’S A HUGE
DISEMBODIED HEAD FLOATING AROUND
YOUR LIVING ROOM.

1848
01:02:42,560 --> 01:02:43,828
--VI.

1849
01:02:43,828 --> 01:02:45,797
SHE’S DEAD.
SHE DOESN’T EXIST.

1850
01:02:45,797 --> 01:02:48,298
SHE’S A PERFUME.

1851
01:02:48,298 --> 01:02:49,733
SHE’S A FOOTPRINT.
SHE’S A HAND.

1852
01:02:49,733 --> 01:02:51,235
- SHE’S A--
- SOUNDS LIKE?

1853
01:02:51,235 --> 01:02:52,670
--A FACE IN A PICTURE.

1854
01:02:52,670 --> 01:02:54,072
WHO COULD BE JEALOUS OF VI?

1855
01:02:54,072 --> 01:02:57,040
YOU’RE TALKING CRAZY, TOM.

1856
01:02:57,040 --> 01:03:00,578
- LET ME SEE THE PICTURE.
- NO.

1857
01:03:00,578 --> 01:03:03,347
YOU’RE NOT MAKING ANY SENSE.

1858
01:03:03,347 --> 01:03:05,550
LOOK, I’M A MUSICIAN.
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

1859
01:03:08,618 --> 01:03:10,488
HER FACE BETWEEN
THE TWO OF US.

1860
01:03:10,488 --> 01:03:13,690
OH, THAT’S GREAT, TOM.
[MAKES "CRAZY" SOUND WITH LIPS]

1861
01:03:13,690 --> 01:03:15,025
I DON’T SEE ANYTHING.

1862
01:03:15,025 --> 01:03:16,760
EXCEPT FOR A HUGE,
DISEMBODIED HEAD.

1863
01:03:16,760 --> 01:03:19,063
IT’S YOU AND ME.

1864
01:03:19,063 --> 01:03:22,132
AND A DOG NAMED EE? EE-OO?

1865
01:03:28,105 --> 01:03:30,775
WELL, WHO’S VI?

1866
01:03:30,775 --> 01:03:33,577
UH-OH.

1867
01:03:33,577 --> 01:03:34,845
SO A GIRL NAMED VI.

1868
01:03:34,845 --> 01:03:36,347
HE DIDN’T WANT
TO TELL ME ABOUT HER.

1869
01:03:36,347 --> 01:03:39,350
HMM-HMM-HMM.

1870
01:03:39,350 --> 01:03:40,752
DID YOU PUT OUT THE LIGHTS?

1871
01:03:40,752 --> 01:03:43,253
DID YOU MAKE TINKLE?

1872
01:03:43,253 --> 01:03:45,288
WHAT’S THE MATTER?

1873
01:03:45,288 --> 01:03:47,592
YOU DON’T LOOK TOO HAPPY.

1874
01:03:47,592 --> 01:03:49,527
YOU OUGHTA BE.

1875
01:03:49,527 --> 01:03:51,162
YOU’RE GETTING
MARRIED TOMORROW.

1876
01:03:51,162 --> 01:03:52,597
♪ DING-DONG, THE BELLS
ARE GONNA CHIME ♪

1877
01:03:52,597 --> 01:03:56,200
WELL, I WONDER, THE WAY
TOM’S BEEN ACTING LATELY.

1878
01:03:56,200 --> 01:03:59,237
ANYTHING TOM DOES
IS ALL RIGHT.

1879
01:03:59,237 --> 01:04:02,607
HE’S PERFECT IN YOUR EYES
ANYHOW, ISN’T HE?

1880
01:04:02,607 --> 01:04:05,042
OH, DON’T WORRY, SANDY.
I LOVE HIM.

1881
01:04:05,042 --> 01:04:06,543
BUT HIS TOUCH REPULSES ME.

1882
01:04:06,543 --> 01:04:10,380
I SUPPOSE EVERY GIRL HAS
A FEW LAST-MINUTE DOUBTS.

1883
01:04:10,380 --> 01:04:13,050
’CAUSE HE FOLLOWED YOU
IN THE LIGHTHOUSE?

1884
01:04:13,050 --> 01:04:15,553
JUST IMAGINE THE THINGS
THAT AREN’T SO.

1885
01:04:15,553 --> 01:04:17,187
OH, LIKE MacBETH.

1886
01:04:17,187 --> 01:04:18,923
EVERYTHING WILL BE
ALL RIGHT.

1887
01:04:18,923 --> 01:04:21,558
IT’S LATE.

1888
01:04:21,558 --> 01:04:24,095
I’M GONNA STAY UP
AND WATCH ARSENIO.

1889
01:04:24,095 --> 01:04:26,630
I’LL GET THE WINDOWS.

1890
01:04:26,630 --> 01:04:28,832
- OH, HI, TOM.
- AH-- HMM?

1891
01:04:28,832 --> 01:04:31,235
THERE’S A LIGHT UP THERE.

1892
01:04:31,235 --> 01:04:33,303
I WONDER WHO IT COULD BE.

1893
01:04:33,303 --> 01:04:34,705
A BOY AND GIRL, PROBABLY.

1894
01:04:34,705 --> 01:04:37,040
- YOU WOULDN’T UNDERSTAND.
- TRY ME.

1895
01:04:37,040 --> 01:04:39,743
--THEY USED TO GO THERE
TO NECK.

1896
01:04:39,743 --> 01:04:41,312
NOT ANYMORE.

1897
01:04:41,312 --> 01:04:44,815
EVERYBODY SAYS
IT’S TOO COLD AND DAMP
AND SMELLY.

1898
01:04:44,815 --> 01:04:46,283
HOW DID YOU KNOW THAT
ABOUT TOM?

1899
01:04:46,283 --> 01:04:47,718
DOES TOM GO THERE
WITH ANYBODY?

1900
01:04:47,718 --> 01:04:49,753
OR DOES ANYBODY
MEET HIM THERE?

1901
01:04:49,753 --> 01:04:51,722
NOW WHO’S IMAGINING THINGS?

1902
01:04:51,722 --> 01:04:54,325
- NOW WHO’S ASKING QUESTIONS?
- NEVER MIND.

1903
01:04:58,562 --> 01:05:01,165
WHY, THAT’S PROBABLY ONLY
A REFLECTION OF THE MOONLIGHT

1904
01:05:01,165 --> 01:05:03,533
- ON A LOOSE PANE OF GLASS.
- OR THE DEVIL.

1905
01:05:03,533 --> 01:05:07,438
HMM.

1906
01:05:07,438 --> 01:05:10,908
SESSIONS PRESENTS!

1907
01:05:10,908 --> 01:05:12,310
♪ I WRITE THE SONGS ♪

1908
01:05:12,310 --> 01:05:14,178
♪ THAT MAKE
THE SOMETHING... ♪

1909
01:05:14,178 --> 01:05:16,147
♪ SOMETHING... ♪

1910
01:05:16,147 --> 01:05:17,982
HMM.

1911
01:05:17,982 --> 01:05:19,750
TOM.

1912
01:05:19,750 --> 01:05:21,452
- TOM.
- VI, LISTEN,

1913
01:05:21,452 --> 01:05:23,853
IF YOU’RE GONNA HAUNT ME,
YOU’LL HAUNT ME ON MY TERMS.

1914
01:05:26,357 --> 01:05:28,492
♪♪ [HEAVIER PLAYING]

1915
01:05:28,492 --> 01:05:31,995
OOH.

1916
01:05:31,995 --> 01:05:33,597
TOM.

1917
01:05:33,597 --> 01:05:37,435
- TOM, PLAY "FREE BIRD."
- WHOO!

1918
01:05:37,435 --> 01:05:40,603
WHERE ARE YOU?

1919
01:05:40,603 --> 01:05:42,673
I’M OVER HERE.

1920
01:05:45,008 --> 01:05:47,043
OKAY, PUT YOUR HANDS
BEHIND YOU.

1921
01:05:47,043 --> 01:05:50,280
NOW SLOWLY PUT YOUR WALLET
ON THE PIANO.

1922
01:05:52,883 --> 01:05:54,585
VI, WHERE--

1923
01:05:54,585 --> 01:05:57,522
VI, YOU’VE LOST
A LOT OF WEIGHT.

1924
01:05:57,522 --> 01:06:00,157
HERE, LET ME PUT
A COASTER UNDER YOU.

1925
01:06:03,460 --> 01:06:05,628
[SERVO GIGGLES]

1926
01:06:05,628 --> 01:06:08,565
- WHAT DO YOU WANT?
- MY BODY.

1927
01:06:08,565 --> 01:06:10,167
I WANT YOU, TOM.

1928
01:06:10,167 --> 01:06:12,770
I WANT TO SAVE YOU
FROM YOUR OWN MISTAKE.

1929
01:06:12,770 --> 01:06:16,140
MY ONLY MISTAKE WAS
IN KNOWING YOU.

1930
01:06:16,140 --> 01:06:17,908
AND THE ONLY WAY
YOU COULD CORRECT IT

1931
01:06:17,908 --> 01:06:19,510
WAS FOR ME TO DIE,
WASN’T IT?

1932
01:06:19,510 --> 01:06:21,812
- HMM.
- IT’S NOT MY FAULT
YOU’RE DEAD!

1933
01:06:21,812 --> 01:06:23,580
YOU’RE IN CHARGE
OF YOUR OWN DESTINY, SISTER.

1934
01:06:23,580 --> 01:06:24,982
I COULDN’T’VE SAVED YOU.

1935
01:06:24,982 --> 01:06:26,417
COULDN’T YOU?

1936
01:06:26,417 --> 01:06:28,185
MAYBE YOU’VE CONVINCED
YOURSELF OF THAT,

1937
01:06:28,185 --> 01:06:29,420
BUT NOT ME.

1938
01:06:29,420 --> 01:06:31,322
- HOW DO THEY OD THAT?
- I WAS THERE, REMEMBER.

1939
01:06:31,322 --> 01:06:34,525
YOU HAD TO SHUT ME UP
SO YOU COULD MARRY MEG.

1940
01:06:34,525 --> 01:06:36,293
YOU GOT AWAY WITH THAT
ALL RIGHT,

1941
01:06:36,293 --> 01:06:38,028
BUT NOW WHAT ARE YOU
GONNA DO?

1942
01:06:38,028 --> 01:06:39,530
[ALL]
GHOSTBUSTERS!

1943
01:06:39,530 --> 01:06:42,467
I’LL NEVER
LET YOU MARRY MEG.

1944
01:06:42,467 --> 01:06:44,102
YOU BELONG TO ME, TOM.

1945
01:06:44,102 --> 01:06:45,970
YOU BELONG TO A GHOST.

1946
01:06:45,970 --> 01:06:48,705
UH, CAN I GET YOU
A BEER OR ANYTHING?

1947
01:06:48,705 --> 01:06:50,340
--ONE FIRST SLIP.

1948
01:06:50,340 --> 01:06:51,875
YOU’LL HAVE TO GO
FROM BAD TO WORSE

1949
01:06:51,875 --> 01:06:53,310
TO KEEP IT QUIET.

1950
01:06:53,310 --> 01:06:54,745
THEY GOT NICE HAIRSTYLISTS
IN THE AFTERLIFE.

1951
01:06:54,745 --> 01:06:57,313
WHAT WILL YOU DO
IF MEG GETS WISE TO YOU?

1952
01:06:57,313 --> 01:06:59,650
STOP HER THE SAME WAY
YOU STOPPED ME?

1953
01:06:59,650 --> 01:07:01,952
I DIDN’T KILL YOU, VI.

1954
01:07:01,952 --> 01:07:04,388
I NEVER KILLED ANYBODY,
AND I NEVER WILL.

1955
01:07:04,388 --> 01:07:06,857
AND ONCE I’M MARRIED,
I GOING TO LIVE

1956
01:07:06,857 --> 01:07:08,858
A VERY HAPPY,
VERY NORMAL LIFE

1957
01:07:08,858 --> 01:07:11,395
- WITH MEG
AND WITH OUR FRIENDS.
- AND YOUR HEAD.

1958
01:07:11,395 --> 01:07:13,497
THERE’S REALLY NOTHING
YOU CAN DO ABOUT IT.

1959
01:07:13,497 --> 01:07:15,198
ISN’T THERE?

1960
01:07:15,198 --> 01:07:17,535
YOU MAY HAVE NOTICED
I’VE FOUND MY VOICE NOW.

1961
01:07:17,535 --> 01:07:19,937
- HMM.
- I PICK THINGS UP FAST.

1962
01:07:19,937 --> 01:07:22,807
I’M GOING TO USE IT
TO TELL THE WORLD ABOUT YOU.

1963
01:07:22,807 --> 01:07:24,342
I TOLD YOU, TOM,
NO ONE WILL

1964
01:07:24,342 --> 01:07:25,608
EVER HAVE YOU BUT ME.

1965
01:07:25,608 --> 01:07:26,743
STOP IT, VI!

1966
01:07:26,743 --> 01:07:28,378
TRY AND MAKE ME.

1967
01:07:28,378 --> 01:07:30,647
TOM STEWART KILLED ME!

1968
01:07:30,647 --> 01:07:33,017
[SERVO]
TOM STEWART KILLED ME,
EVERYBODY!

1969
01:07:33,017 --> 01:07:35,218
[ALL]
TOM STEWART KILLED ME!

1970
01:07:35,218 --> 01:07:37,588
- TOM STEWART KILLED ME.
- COME ON, JOIN IN!

1971
01:07:37,588 --> 01:07:40,190
TOM STEWART KILLED ME.

1972
01:07:40,190 --> 01:07:41,592
TOM STEWART KILLED ME--

1973
01:07:41,592 --> 01:07:43,393
COME ON.
WE’RE GOING BOWLING.

1974
01:07:43,393 --> 01:07:45,428
TOM STEWART KILLED ME.

1975
01:07:45,428 --> 01:07:48,032
[MUFFLED] TOM STEWART
KILLED ME.

1976
01:07:48,032 --> 01:07:50,400
[SERVO, MUFFLED]

1977
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:51,735
THIS IS LIKE
BARTON FINK NOW.

1978
01:07:51,735 --> 01:07:54,205
TOM STEWART KILLED ME.

1979
01:07:54,205 --> 01:07:55,638
TOM STEWART--

1980
01:07:55,638 --> 01:07:58,642
AHH-- [CROW GRUNTS]

1981
01:08:02,480 --> 01:08:04,482
HEY, NICE HEAD.
I’D SAY THAT’S ABOUT

1982
01:08:04,482 --> 01:08:08,052
A FOUR- OR FIVE-POUND HEAD.

1983
01:08:08,052 --> 01:08:09,220
GET OUT OF HERE--

1984
01:08:09,220 --> 01:08:10,720
DON’T BE IN
SUCH A HURRY, DAD.

1985
01:08:10,720 --> 01:08:12,355
YOU’RE ALWAYS IN A HURRY.
YOU SHOULDN’T BE LIKE THAT.

1986
01:08:12,355 --> 01:08:14,057
- GIVE ME THAT.
- I JUST WANNA TALK TO YOU,
CHUM.

1987
01:08:14,057 --> 01:08:15,860
A NICE, FRIENDLY TALK.
THAT’S ALL.

1988
01:08:15,860 --> 01:08:17,193
GIVE ME THAT.

1989
01:08:17,193 --> 01:08:19,062
AND SHAZAM!

1990
01:08:19,062 --> 01:08:21,632
WELL, THERE’S ANOTHER TRICK
I CAN’T DO.

1991
01:08:21,632 --> 01:08:24,435
UH, I GOT THESE FOR YOU.

1992
01:08:24,435 --> 01:08:26,803
YOU LOOK SICK, DAD.

1993
01:08:26,803 --> 01:08:28,105
SOMETHING’S WRONG.

1994
01:08:28,105 --> 01:08:29,740
LOOK, ARE YOU
GONNA TALK TO ME OR NOT?

1995
01:08:29,740 --> 01:08:32,142
- QUIT PICKING YOUR NOSE.
- LET’S GET THIS THING
OVER WITH.

1996
01:08:32,142 --> 01:08:35,778
OKAY, I NEED
TWO QUARTS OF 2% MILK.

1997
01:08:35,778 --> 01:08:37,247
WHAT IS IT YOU WANT?

1998
01:08:37,247 --> 01:08:39,850
LIKE I SAID, DAD, ALL I WANT
IS WHAT’S COMING TO ME.

1999
01:08:39,850 --> 01:08:41,318
YOU KNOW,
THE WAY IT LOOKS TO ME,

2000
01:08:41,318 --> 01:08:42,653
WE SHOULD BE
SORT OF PARTNERS.

2001
01:08:42,653 --> 01:08:44,288
I HELP YOU, AND YOU HELP ME.

2002
01:08:53,730 --> 01:08:55,132
HEY, TOM, CROW.

2003
01:08:55,132 --> 01:08:56,567
DO YOU GUYS WANNA--

2004
01:08:56,567 --> 01:08:58,102
AAH!

2005
01:08:58,102 --> 01:08:59,670
IT WORKS! HEY, GYPSY.

2006
01:08:59,670 --> 01:09:01,405
TOLD YOU.
WE’RE DOWNRIGHT TERRIFYING.

2007
01:09:01,405 --> 01:09:02,873
OKAY, HOW ABOUT THIS?

2008
01:09:02,873 --> 01:09:05,375
JOEL ROBINSON KILLED US.

2009
01:09:05,375 --> 01:09:07,878
JOEL ROBINSON KILLED US.

2010
01:09:07,878 --> 01:09:10,013
[BOTH]
JOEL ROBINSON KILLED US.

2011
01:09:10,013 --> 01:09:11,348
- HEY, YOU GUYS.
- JOEL ROBINSON--

2012
01:09:11,348 --> 01:09:12,917
WHAT IN THE WORLD
HAPPENED OVER THERE?

2013
01:09:12,917 --> 01:09:15,718
I SAW GYPSY RUNNING AWAY LIKE
SHE’D SEEN A GHOST OR SOMETHING.

2014
01:09:15,718 --> 01:09:17,755
THAT, JOEL,
IS BECAUSE SHE DID.

2015
01:09:17,755 --> 01:09:19,055
[BOTH]
WHOO...

2016
01:09:19,055 --> 01:09:20,858
JOEL ROBINSON KILLED US.

2017
01:09:20,858 --> 01:09:22,527
JOEL ROBINSON KILLED US.

2018
01:09:22,527 --> 01:09:24,662
- HEY, I DID NOT.
- YOU DID TOO!

2019
01:09:24,662 --> 01:09:26,663
- I DID NOT.
- THEN WHY ARE WE DEAD?

2020
01:09:26,663 --> 01:09:29,200
WELL, YOU’RE NOT DEAD,
AND YOU’RE CERTAINLY NOT GHOSTS.

2021
01:09:29,200 --> 01:09:31,702
AND EVEN IF YOU WERE GHOSTS,
I WOULDN’T BE AFRAID OF YOU.

2022
01:09:31,702 --> 01:09:34,638
’CAUSE I’VE SEEN YOU THIS WAY
ABOUT A MILLION TIMES BEFORE.

2023
01:09:34,638 --> 01:09:36,407
BUT THIS TIME
IT’S DIFFERENT, JOEL.

2024
01:09:36,407 --> 01:09:38,408
THIS TIME WE REALLY DIED.

2025
01:09:38,408 --> 01:09:39,910
AND NOW MUST SPEND ETERNITY

2026
01:09:39,910 --> 01:09:42,947
TORMENTING THE VERY MAN
WHO GAVE US LIFE.

2027
01:09:42,947 --> 01:09:44,415
♪ TORMENTED! ♪

2028
01:09:44,415 --> 01:09:47,150
♪♪ ["GOLDFINGER" TRUMPET]

2029
01:09:47,150 --> 01:09:48,952
TO ESCAPE
THIS HEINOUS LIVING HELL,

2030
01:09:48,952 --> 01:09:50,353
YOU HAVE ONLY ONE OPTION.

2031
01:09:50,353 --> 01:09:52,022
YOU MUST OFFER GYPSY TO US

2032
01:09:52,022 --> 01:09:54,123
IN A PAGAN EARTH CEREMONY,

2033
01:09:54,123 --> 01:09:55,792
WHICH WE HOLD
EVERY TUESDAY AT 8:00.

2034
01:09:55,792 --> 01:09:57,995
IT’S THE ONLY THING
THAT MAKES ANY SENSE ANYMORE.

2035
01:09:57,995 --> 01:10:00,263
YEAH, WELL, LISTEN.
YOU GUYS AREN’T FUNNY ANYMORE.

2036
01:10:00,263 --> 01:10:01,965
AND YOU DESERVE EACH OTHER.

2037
01:10:01,965 --> 01:10:04,067
I’M GONNA TAKE YOUR BODIES
AND GET GOING, OKAY?

2038
01:10:04,067 --> 01:10:06,103
HEY, JOEL, WE’RE SORRY!
WE’RE JUST HAVING A LITTLE FUN!

2039
01:10:06,103 --> 01:10:09,540
JOEL! HEY,
DON’T TURN THE LIGHTS OFF!

2040
01:10:09,540 --> 01:10:11,942
"IT’S THE ONLY THING
THAT MAKES SENSE ANYMORE."

2041
01:10:11,942 --> 01:10:13,443
THAT’S WHAT REALLY
MADE HIM MAD, YOU KNOW.

2042
01:10:13,443 --> 01:10:15,745
OH, LIKE HE WAS GOING ALONG
WITH THE SACRIFICE IDEA

2043
01:10:15,745 --> 01:10:17,413
UNTIL THEN.
FACE IT, CROW.

2044
01:10:17,413 --> 01:10:19,650
WE USED POOR JUDGMENT,
SCARED GYPSY,

2045
01:10:19,650 --> 01:10:21,918
IRKED JOEL, AND NOW
WE’RE STUCK HERE IN THE DARK

2046
01:10:21,918 --> 01:10:23,753
WITH NO BODIES.

2047
01:10:23,753 --> 01:10:26,090
- I’M NOT SCARED, THOUGH.
- NO, ME NEITHER.

2048
01:10:26,090 --> 01:10:27,457
I MEAN,
NOT ONE LITTLE BIT.

2049
01:10:27,457 --> 01:10:30,193
OH, I KNOW.

2050
01:10:30,193 --> 01:10:33,230
SERVO? SERVO?

2051
01:10:33,230 --> 01:10:34,598
- SERVO!
- I’M RIGHT HERE.

2052
01:10:34,598 --> 01:10:36,700
[BOTH]
AAH! AAH!

2053
01:10:44,040 --> 01:10:45,608
I BRING YOUR PLAYGIRL
OVER TO THE ISLAND, AND I--

2054
01:10:45,608 --> 01:10:47,077
THANKS FOR PUTTING
OUR HEADS BACK, JOEL.

2055
01:10:47,077 --> 01:10:48,578
- YEAH. IT’S OKAY.
- SORRY.

2056
01:10:48,578 --> 01:10:50,982
- --SORT OF A SILENCER,
CATCH?

2057
01:10:50,982 --> 01:10:53,283
THE WORD YOU’RE REACHING FOR
IS BLACKMAIL.

2058
01:10:53,283 --> 01:10:54,918
THAT’S NOT IT AT ALL, DAD.

2059
01:10:54,918 --> 01:10:56,420
WE SHOULD BE SORT OF PALS.

2060
01:10:56,420 --> 01:10:58,355
I’VE DONE YOU A FAVOR.
NOW YOU CAN DO ME ONE.

2061
01:10:58,355 --> 01:11:00,257
IN OTHER WORDS,
IF I DON’T PAY YOU BLACKMAIL,

2062
01:11:00,257 --> 01:11:03,260
YOU’LL GO TO MY FIANCEE
AND EXPOSE MY LIFE OF SIN.

2063
01:11:03,260 --> 01:11:06,297
- IS THAT IT?
- GEE, I WAS JUST GONNA
HAVE YOU BUY ME LUNCH.

2064
01:11:06,297 --> 01:11:08,365
--DAD, BUT YOU’RE
GETTING THE IDEA.

2065
01:11:08,365 --> 01:11:09,867
WELL, IT WON’T
DO YOU ANY GOOD.

2066
01:11:09,867 --> 01:11:12,168
I’M NOT GONNA PAY YOU
ONE LOUSY CENT.

2067
01:11:12,168 --> 01:11:14,203
IN THE FIRST PLACE,
I DON’T KNOW A GIRL NAMED VI.

2068
01:11:14,203 --> 01:11:15,938
AND EVEN IF I DID,
IT WOULDN’T DO YOU ANY GOOD.

2069
01:11:15,938 --> 01:11:17,240
BECAUSE UNFORTUNATELY,

2070
01:11:17,240 --> 01:11:19,577
I’M NOT SHARING
MY COTTAGE WITH ANYONE.

2071
01:11:19,577 --> 01:11:21,445
IF IT’LL MAKE YOU FEEL BETTER,
YOU CAN LOOK FOR YOURSELF.

2072
01:11:21,445 --> 01:11:23,080
THAT’S NOT NECESSARY, DAD.
NOT AT ALL.

2073
01:11:23,080 --> 01:11:24,982
YOU SEE, I ALREADY HAVE.

2074
01:11:24,982 --> 01:11:26,383
WELL THEN,
YOU KNOW SHE’S NOT HERE.

2075
01:11:26,383 --> 01:11:28,352
WELL, YES AND NO.

2076
01:11:28,352 --> 01:11:30,820
YOU SEE, WHEN YOU WERE
SO EAGER TO COME UP WITH
THAT FIVE-SPOT,

2077
01:11:30,820 --> 01:11:32,088
I FIGURED YOU WERE...

2078
01:11:32,088 --> 01:11:34,992
- [SERVO YAWNS]
- NOW--

2079
01:11:34,992 --> 01:11:37,695
WELCOME TO
DIALOGUE DUMPING GROUND.

2080
01:11:37,695 --> 01:11:39,597
--STORY’S EVEN
GETTING BETTER TO READ.

2081
01:11:39,597 --> 01:11:41,298
NOW HERE COMES THE PART
I LIKE THE BEST.

2082
01:11:41,298 --> 01:11:43,200
- OKAY.
- I DO A LITTLE SNOOPING

2083
01:11:43,200 --> 01:11:44,735
WHEN YOU’RE NOT AROUND.

2084
01:11:44,735 --> 01:11:46,370
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

2085
01:11:46,370 --> 01:11:48,205
I-- I JUST THOUGHT OF
A NEW JAZZ TUNE.

2086
01:11:48,205 --> 01:11:49,673
STILL WITH ME, DAD?

2087
01:11:49,673 --> 01:11:50,740
GO ON.

2088
01:11:50,740 --> 01:11:52,075
YOU SEE,
THAT’S THE PUNCH LINE.

2089
01:11:52,075 --> 01:11:54,110
- THERE’S YOUR PUNCH.
- THAT’S THE GIMMICK.

2090
01:11:54,110 --> 01:11:56,047
THIS DOLL VI ISN’T
HIDING IN YOUR COTTAGE,

2091
01:11:56,047 --> 01:11:57,682
AND SHE ISN’T ANY PLACE ELSE
ON THE ISLAND,

2092
01:11:57,682 --> 01:11:59,148
AND SHE NEVER
LEFT THE ISLAND.

2093
01:11:59,148 --> 01:12:00,683
- HMM.
- NOW,

2094
01:12:00,683 --> 01:12:02,753
WHAT DO YOU SUPPOSE
COULD’VE HAPPENED TO HER, HUH?

2095
01:12:02,753 --> 01:12:04,153
YOU TELL ME.

2096
01:12:04,153 --> 01:12:05,788
- I ASKED YOU FIRST.
- YOU’RE A COMEDIAN.

2097
01:12:05,788 --> 01:12:09,125
UH-UH. YOU’RE THE ONE THAT
HAS THE REST OF THE ANSWERS.

2098
01:12:10,960 --> 01:12:12,662
YOU KNOW SOMETHING?

2099
01:12:12,662 --> 01:12:15,598
EVERYTHING YOU’VE JUST SAID
IS ALL BLUFF.

2100
01:12:15,598 --> 01:12:17,133
YOU DON’T KNOW A DAMN THING.

2101
01:12:17,133 --> 01:12:19,202
THAT’S NOT FRIENDLY, DAD.
NOT FRIENDLY AT ALL.

2102
01:12:19,202 --> 01:12:21,372
IN FACT, I THOUGHT
YOU’D TAKE THE WRONG OUT...

2103
01:12:21,372 --> 01:12:24,408
SO I SORT OF
BORROWED SOMETHING.

2104
01:12:24,408 --> 01:12:25,808
HEY, THAT’S THE KEY
TO MY HEART.

2105
01:12:25,808 --> 01:12:27,878
I ASSUME
IT’S A FRIEND OF YOURS.

2106
01:12:30,247 --> 01:12:33,317
♪ OH GYPSIES,
TRAMPS AND THIEVES ♪

2107
01:12:35,318 --> 01:12:37,453
LET’S GET OUT OF HERE.

2108
01:12:37,453 --> 01:12:39,355
I CAN SEE THAT
YOU’RE FINALLY SEEING--

2109
01:12:39,355 --> 01:12:41,058
HEY, WAIT A MINUTE,
ISN’T THAT TOM STEWART?

2110
01:12:41,058 --> 01:12:43,427
HEY, TOM STEWART!

2111
01:12:43,427 --> 01:12:45,895
I FORGOT WHY
I WAS COMING THIS WAY.

2112
01:12:45,895 --> 01:12:49,867
WHAT’S MY BOYFRIEND’S NAME?

2113
01:12:49,867 --> 01:12:51,668
HERE AT GORTON’S
OF GLOUCESTER,

2114
01:12:51,668 --> 01:12:53,803
WE MAKE FISH STICKS
THE OLD-FASHIONED WAY.

2115
01:12:53,803 --> 01:12:57,473
- OKAY.
- WE FREEZE ’EM.

2116
01:12:57,473 --> 01:12:59,175
WHAT’D WE COME UP HERE FOR?

2117
01:12:59,175 --> 01:13:01,245
[AS AURIC GOLDFINGER]
SO I CAN KILL YOU, MR. BOND.

2118
01:13:01,245 --> 01:13:02,880
SO THAT YOU AND I CAN
HAVE A LITTLE TALK

2119
01:13:02,880 --> 01:13:04,415
IN PEACE AND QUIET.

2120
01:13:04,415 --> 01:13:06,317
I SUGGEST YOU ORDER THE COD.

2121
01:13:06,317 --> 01:13:10,187
JUST WHAT DO YOU WANT?

2122
01:13:10,187 --> 01:13:11,355
FIVE THOU.

2123
01:13:11,355 --> 01:13:13,990
--SAND DOLLARS.

2124
01:13:13,990 --> 01:13:16,058
- FIVE THOU?
- --SAND DOLLARS.

2125
01:13:16,058 --> 01:13:17,460
DON’T TELL ME
YOU DON’T GOT IT.

2126
01:13:17,460 --> 01:13:19,697
YOUR FUTURE FATHER-IN-LAW
IS LOADED.

2127
01:13:19,697 --> 01:13:23,000
TOM... TOM...

2128
01:13:23,000 --> 01:13:25,102
[SERVO AS VI]
OFFER HIM 3,500.

2129
01:13:25,102 --> 01:13:28,372
- WHO ARE YOU TALKING TO?
- SAM?

2130
01:13:28,372 --> 01:13:30,473
YOU DIDN’T HEAR ANYTHING?

2131
01:13:30,473 --> 01:13:32,308
I DIDN’T HEAR ANYTHING.
I’M WAITING TO HEAR SOMETHING
FROM YOU.

2132
01:13:32,308 --> 01:13:34,343
OKAY, I’LL SING
"NIGHTS OF WHITE SATIN."

2133
01:13:34,343 --> 01:13:35,845
THEY’RE CLOSING IN
ON YOU, TOM.

2134
01:13:35,845 --> 01:13:38,548
- SAY...
- YOU’D BETTER TAKE CARE
OF HIM RIGHT NOW.

2135
01:13:39,983 --> 01:13:41,952
NO.

2136
01:13:41,952 --> 01:13:44,320
NO...
THAT YOUR FINAL ANSWER?

2137
01:13:44,320 --> 01:13:47,190
HOW MUCH DID YOU WAGER?
ALL OF IT? OOH, I’M SORRY.

2138
01:13:49,527 --> 01:13:51,528
HE’S SO EASY, TOM.

2139
01:13:51,528 --> 01:13:53,497
JUST AS EASY AS I WAS.

2140
01:13:53,497 --> 01:13:55,598
I DO BELIEVE IN SPOOKS.
I DO BELIEVE IN SPOOKS.

2141
01:13:55,598 --> 01:13:57,433
I DO, I DO, I DO, I DO,
I DO BELIEVE IN SPOOKS.

2142
01:13:57,433 --> 01:13:58,868
ONE GOOD BLOW
IS ALL IT TAKES.

2143
01:13:58,868 --> 01:14:00,403
SO DO I.

2144
01:14:00,403 --> 01:14:02,305
YOU GOT RID OF ME, BUT YOU’LL
NEVER GET RID OF HIM.

2145
01:14:02,305 --> 01:14:04,207
AS LONG AS HE LIVES.

2146
01:14:04,207 --> 01:14:06,243
HE’LL BLEED YOU
OF EVERY PENNY, TOM.

2147
01:14:06,243 --> 01:14:07,845
- HMM.
- AND ALL THE TIME--

2148
01:14:07,845 --> 01:14:11,748
SHE’S PRETTY LONG-WINDED
FOR A GHOST.

2149
01:14:11,748 --> 01:14:13,883
WHAT IF MEG FINDS OUT?

2150
01:14:13,883 --> 01:14:16,620
YOU CAN’T LET HIM DO IT, TOM.
YOU’LL LOSE EVERYTHING.

2151
01:14:16,620 --> 01:14:17,922
THE CONDO, THE CAR,
AND THE VACATION

2152
01:14:17,922 --> 01:14:19,923
TO PUERTO VALLARTA.

2153
01:14:19,923 --> 01:14:21,325
LOOK, YOU’VE HAD
ENOUGH TIME.

2154
01:14:21,325 --> 01:14:22,592
PUT YOUR PENCILS
DOWN, PLEASE.

2155
01:14:22,592 --> 01:14:23,660
DING.

2156
01:14:23,660 --> 01:14:26,128
DO I GET THE MONEY,
OR DON’T I?

2157
01:14:26,128 --> 01:14:28,332
YES, TOM, DOES HE GET PAID?

2158
01:14:28,332 --> 01:14:29,667
UH, DO YOU TAKE VISA?

2159
01:14:29,667 --> 01:14:32,635
NO.

2160
01:14:32,635 --> 01:14:34,203
ALL RIGHT.

2161
01:14:34,203 --> 01:14:37,373
YOU KNOW WHAT’S BEST.

2162
01:14:37,373 --> 01:14:39,308
LET’S SEE WHAT YOUR CHICK
HAS TO SAY ABOUT THIS.

2163
01:14:39,308 --> 01:14:41,812
NO MORE YOGURT.

2164
01:14:41,812 --> 01:14:44,247
KILL HIM, TOM!

2165
01:14:44,247 --> 01:14:46,583
WAIT.

2166
01:14:46,583 --> 01:14:47,817
CHANGE YOUR MIND?

2167
01:14:47,817 --> 01:14:50,320
KILL HIM, TOM.

2168
01:14:50,320 --> 01:14:52,388
- NO.
- YES.

2169
01:14:52,388 --> 01:14:53,390
- NO.
- YES.

2170
01:14:53,390 --> 01:14:55,425
- KILL HIM!
- NO!

2171
01:14:55,425 --> 01:14:58,128
NO-- YES!

2172
01:14:58,128 --> 01:14:59,930
THE ORIGINAL DEAD MILKMAN.

2173
01:15:06,337 --> 01:15:07,737
HE’S DEAD, JIM.

2174
01:15:07,737 --> 01:15:10,340
EITHER THIS MAN IS DEAD,
OR MY WATCH HAS STOPPED.

2175
01:15:16,880 --> 01:15:19,448
- WELL, AT LEAST HE’S TIDY.
- MM-HMM.

2176
01:15:19,448 --> 01:15:21,017
TONIGHT’S EPISODE.
"I’VE SEEN THE BEST MINDS

2177
01:15:21,017 --> 01:15:23,620
OF MY GENERATION...
MURDERED."

2178
01:15:27,958 --> 01:15:30,060
MM-HMM?

2179
01:15:34,832 --> 01:15:37,733
[CROW GASPS]

2180
01:15:37,733 --> 01:15:39,670
♪ I SAW TOMMY ♪

2181
01:15:39,670 --> 01:15:42,205
♪ KILLING BEAT-NIK ♪

2182
01:15:42,205 --> 01:15:45,242
SEE THAT THE ROCKFORD PROBLEM
IS TAKEN CARE OF, PERMANENTLY.

2183
01:15:45,242 --> 01:15:47,877
JIM HENSON’S
WITNESS BABIES.

2184
01:15:47,877 --> 01:15:49,647
[SERVO HUMS DRAMATICALLY]

2185
01:15:49,647 --> 01:15:53,217
RACKET SQUAD.

2186
01:15:53,217 --> 01:15:55,585
OH, THAT’S WHERE
SHE LEFT HER SHOES.

2187
01:15:57,187 --> 01:15:58,655
HUH.

2188
01:15:58,655 --> 01:16:00,323
WELL, SHE’S REALLY
KIND OF FLAT, AND--

2189
01:16:00,323 --> 01:16:03,593
OH, OH, IT’S...

2190
01:16:03,593 --> 01:16:07,297
TOM TAUGHT ME
THE MEANING OF LOSS
LAST NIGHT.

2191
01:16:07,297 --> 01:16:10,167
[DISTANT VOICE]
SANDY, COME HERE.

2192
01:16:10,167 --> 01:16:13,303
[MALE VOICE]
SANDY, DID YOU HEAR
YOUR MOTHER CALL YOU?

2193
01:16:13,303 --> 01:16:14,738
WHAT IS IT?

2194
01:16:14,738 --> 01:16:17,073
STOP WHATEVER YOU’RE DOING
AND COME HERE AT ONCE.

2195
01:16:17,073 --> 01:16:18,842
BUT I’M HARBORING
A HORRIBLE SECRET

2196
01:16:18,842 --> 01:16:22,345
WHICH I’M SUBLIMATING
INTO MY UNCONSCIOUS, MOM.

2197
01:16:28,852 --> 01:16:31,955
HAVE YOU FOUND
MY KILL WALDO BOOKS?

2198
01:16:31,955 --> 01:16:34,792
OH, SANDY, WE HAVE TO BE
AT THE CHURCH IN 20 MINUTES,

2199
01:16:34,792 --> 01:16:36,427
AND YOU’RE NOT EVEN
DRESSED YET.

2200
01:16:36,427 --> 01:16:38,528
NEVER MIND THAT NOW.
MEG SNAGGED HER HEM.

2201
01:16:38,528 --> 01:16:41,197
COME AND HOLD IT, VI.
TAKE IT UP.

2202
01:16:41,197 --> 01:16:43,133
YOU’LL MAKE
A LOVELY WIFE, MEG.

2203
01:16:43,133 --> 01:16:45,835
- PAUL FREES.
- THANKS.

2204
01:16:45,835 --> 01:16:47,837
MEG...

2205
01:16:47,837 --> 01:16:51,040
DO YOU REALLY LOVE HIM
A WHOLE LOT?

2206
01:16:51,040 --> 01:16:53,943
WELL, WHATEVER MAKES YOU ASK
A THING LIKE THAT?

2207
01:16:53,943 --> 01:16:55,778
HE’S A KILLER!
HE’S A KILLER!

2208
01:16:55,778 --> 01:16:58,115
--SAID YOU WEREN’T SURE.

2209
01:16:58,115 --> 01:17:00,350
WELL, I’M SURE NOW.

2210
01:17:00,350 --> 01:17:02,218
OH, YOU’LL REMEMBER
TO TAKE THE BOUQUET

2211
01:17:02,218 --> 01:17:04,320
WHEN I HAND IT TO YOU,
WON’T YOU?

2212
01:17:04,320 --> 01:17:05,655
I’LL REMEMBER.

2213
01:17:05,655 --> 01:17:07,423
IF WE’RE NOT ALL DEAD.

2214
01:17:07,423 --> 01:17:10,260
I MEAN, SUPPOSE
HE’D DONE SOMETHING

2215
01:17:10,260 --> 01:17:12,495
AWFUL BAD.

2216
01:17:12,495 --> 01:17:15,298
THE WAY I FEEL NOW,
I’D MARRY HIM NO MATTER WHAT.

2217
01:17:15,298 --> 01:17:16,600
CAN YOU SAY "DENIAL?"

2218
01:17:16,600 --> 01:17:18,635
--DON’T FORGET,
YOU STAND CLOSE BEHIND ME.

2219
01:17:18,635 --> 01:17:20,837
BUT NOT TOO CLOSE.

2220
01:17:20,837 --> 01:17:22,472
[MEG’S MOTHER]
THERE. THAT’S DONE.

2221
01:17:22,472 --> 01:17:24,942
AND YOU, YOUNG LADY.
GET INTO YOUR GOWN THIS INSTANT.

2222
01:17:24,942 --> 01:17:26,877
THINK I’M GONNA WEAR
MY BLACK DRESS.

2223
01:17:26,877 --> 01:17:29,378
♪ PEOPLE DON’T FEAR
THE REAPER ♪

2224
01:17:29,378 --> 01:17:32,182
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

2225
01:17:32,182 --> 01:17:33,483
MRS. HUBBARD LOANED US
HER RING

2226
01:17:33,483 --> 01:17:34,818
IN PLACE OF
THE ONE YOU LOST,

2227
01:17:34,818 --> 01:17:36,185
SO THAT’S OKAY.

2228
01:17:36,185 --> 01:17:37,853
I’VE GOT THE MINISTER’S FEE
HERE IN MY POCKET,

2229
01:17:37,853 --> 01:17:39,255
AND EVERYTHING’S
UNDER CONTROL.

2230
01:17:39,255 --> 01:17:40,357
SO SNAP OUT OF IT.

2231
01:17:40,357 --> 01:17:41,725
OKAY, OKAY.
I’LL BE ALL RIGHT.

2232
01:17:41,725 --> 01:17:43,960
AND GET THAT FUNEREAL LOOK
OFF YOUR FACE.

2233
01:17:43,960 --> 01:17:45,295
THIS IS A WEDDING, MAN.

2234
01:17:45,295 --> 01:17:47,897
COME ON, LET’S SWING!

2235
01:17:47,897 --> 01:17:49,532
CHEER HIM UP, HONEY.

2236
01:17:49,532 --> 01:17:51,568
KINDA LIKE HAVING
SYLVIA PLATH CHEER YOU UP.

2237
01:17:51,568 --> 01:17:54,170
- HMM.
- YOU CAN BUY
MY SILENCE, TOM.

2238
01:17:54,170 --> 01:17:57,673
WOW, THAT’S--

2239
01:17:57,673 --> 01:17:59,608
YOU HAVE
A PRETTY DRESS, SANDY.

2240
01:17:59,608 --> 01:18:02,545
YOU’RE REALLY
GONNA MARRY MY SISTER,

2241
01:18:02,545 --> 01:18:03,880
AREN’T YOU?

2242
01:18:03,880 --> 01:18:05,148
YUP.

2243
01:18:05,148 --> 01:18:06,817
OH, DON’T FEEL LIKE THAT.

2244
01:18:06,817 --> 01:18:09,753
I CAN’T HELP IT.

2245
01:18:09,753 --> 01:18:13,390
SUPPOSE YOU LOVED SOMEBODY.

2246
01:18:13,390 --> 01:18:17,193
SOMEBODY WHO DID
SOMETHING BAD.

2247
01:18:17,193 --> 01:18:20,130
AND ONLY YOU KNEW.

2248
01:18:20,130 --> 01:18:21,532
WOULD YOU KEEP IT SECRET?

2249
01:18:21,532 --> 01:18:23,433
WHY, YES I WOULD,
I WOULD TUCK IT DEEP

2250
01:18:23,433 --> 01:18:24,835
INTO MY SUBCONSCIOUS.

2251
01:18:24,835 --> 01:18:28,138
GOOD FRIENDS GENERALLY TRY
TO STAND BY ONE ANOTHER.

2252
01:18:28,138 --> 01:18:30,607
BUT WHAT IF IT WAS SOMETHING

2253
01:18:30,607 --> 01:18:32,308
REAL, REAL BAD?

2254
01:18:32,308 --> 01:18:34,043
THEN KEEP IT
REAL, REAL SECRET.

2255
01:18:34,043 --> 01:18:35,812
"REAL BAD," LIKE WHAT?

2256
01:18:35,812 --> 01:18:37,413
MURDER?

2257
01:18:44,620 --> 01:18:48,358
♪ IN-A-GADDA-DA-VIDA, BABY ♪

2258
01:18:48,358 --> 01:18:50,860
COMIN’ THROUGH.
TUGBOAT, COMIN’ THROUGH.

2259
01:18:50,860 --> 01:18:52,928
AND ONCE AGAIN,
THERE IS NO SMOKING

2260
01:18:52,928 --> 01:18:54,163
IN YOUR METRODOME.

2261
01:18:54,163 --> 01:18:57,567
[SERVO MIMICS CROWD]

2262
01:18:57,567 --> 01:18:59,435
- DEARLY BELOVED--
- AND THE REST OF YOU.

2263
01:18:59,435 --> 01:19:00,803
WE ARE GATHERED
TOGETHER HERE--

2264
01:19:00,803 --> 01:19:03,373
- AND TUCKED THERE--
- IN THE SIGHT OF GOD

2265
01:19:03,373 --> 01:19:05,942
AND IN THE PEACE
OF HIS COMPANY

2266
01:19:05,942 --> 01:19:07,810
TO JOIN TOGETHER THIS MAN--

2267
01:19:07,810 --> 01:19:09,512
- AND THIS VICTIM.
- AND THIS WOMAN.

2268
01:19:09,512 --> 01:19:12,248
THEY’RE GETTING MARRIED
IN A NURSING HOME CHAPEL.

2269
01:19:12,248 --> 01:19:14,450
--WHICH IS
AN HONORABLE ESTATE.

2270
01:19:14,450 --> 01:19:16,653
- INSTITUTED OF GOD.
- MM-HMM.

2271
01:19:16,653 --> 01:19:19,122
SIGNIFYING UNTO US
THE MYSTICAL UNION--

2272
01:19:19,122 --> 01:19:21,190
- MM-HMM.
- THAT IS BETWIXT CHRIST

2273
01:19:21,190 --> 01:19:23,025
AND HIS CHURCH.

2274
01:19:23,025 --> 01:19:25,795
[CROW YAWNS]
- WHICH HOLY ESTATE...

2275
01:19:25,795 --> 01:19:27,663
QUIT PADDING YOUR PART,
PADRE.

2276
01:19:27,663 --> 01:19:30,233
--FIRST MIRACLE THAT
HE WROUGHT IN CANA OF GALILEE.

2277
01:19:30,233 --> 01:19:33,237
- NOW SUPPERING--
- AND IS COMMENDED TO ST. PAUL

2278
01:19:33,237 --> 01:19:36,707
TO BE HONORABLE
AMONG ALL MEN.

2279
01:19:36,707 --> 01:19:39,108
AND THEREFORE,
IS NOT BY ANY

2280
01:19:39,108 --> 01:19:41,978
TO BE ENTERED INTO
UNADVISEDLY OR LIGHTLY.

2281
01:19:41,978 --> 01:19:44,647
I DID IT-- OH!
I DO. I DO.

2282
01:19:44,647 --> 01:19:46,415
--DISCRETELY,

2283
01:19:46,415 --> 01:19:49,185
ADVISEDLY, SOBERLY.

2284
01:19:49,185 --> 01:19:50,687
AND IN THE FEAR OF GOD.

2285
01:19:50,687 --> 01:19:52,522
HI, MURDERER.

2286
01:19:52,522 --> 01:19:54,390
INTO THIS HOLY ESTATE,

2287
01:19:54,390 --> 01:19:56,292
THESE TWO PERSONS PRESENT

2288
01:19:56,292 --> 01:19:57,860
COME NOW TO BE JOINED.

2289
01:19:57,860 --> 01:19:59,830
HEY, IT’S A TWISTER DRESS.

2290
01:19:59,830 --> 01:20:01,998
- RIGHT HAND RED.
- HEY.

2291
01:20:01,998 --> 01:20:03,600
--MAY BE JOINED TOGETHER,

2292
01:20:03,600 --> 01:20:04,935
LET HIM NOW SPEAK

2293
01:20:04,935 --> 01:20:07,270
OR ELSE HEREAFTER, FOREVER--

2294
01:20:07,270 --> 01:20:09,738
FIVE THOU,
OR I SING LIKE A CANARY.

2295
01:20:12,975 --> 01:20:14,677
UH... UH...

2296
01:20:14,677 --> 01:20:18,615
ELAAAAINE!

2297
01:20:18,615 --> 01:20:19,950
ARE YOU ON THE BRIDE SIDE

2298
01:20:19,950 --> 01:20:22,385
OR THE GROOM SIDE?

2299
01:20:22,385 --> 01:20:24,053
♪ WELL, I’LL BE DAMNED ♪

2300
01:20:24,053 --> 01:20:26,690
♪ HERE COMES
YOUR GHOST AGAIN ♪

2301
01:20:26,690 --> 01:20:28,057
EWW.

2302
01:20:28,057 --> 01:20:29,625
OOH.

2303
01:20:29,625 --> 01:20:31,795
B.O.

2304
01:20:31,795 --> 01:20:34,363
[DEEP VOICE]
♪ B.O. ♪

2305
01:20:37,700 --> 01:20:40,403
PHEW, I’D HATE TO HAVE
TO SIT NEXT TO THAT GHOST.

2306
01:20:49,947 --> 01:20:52,348
- AAH!
- EWW, YOU PAID 50 FOR THAT?

2307
01:20:55,018 --> 01:20:56,953
HUH? OH.

2308
01:20:56,953 --> 01:20:59,688
THE MASS HAS ENDED--
LET US GO IN PEACE--
LET’S GET OUT OF HERE!

2309
01:21:04,560 --> 01:21:06,462
RECEPTION TO FOLLOW
AT THE LIGHTHOUSE.

2310
01:21:06,462 --> 01:21:07,930
R.S.V.R.I.P.

2311
01:21:07,930 --> 01:21:11,100
HMM.

2312
01:21:11,100 --> 01:21:12,502
OH, HE’S GOTTA
GET THE MATCHBOOKS

2313
01:21:12,502 --> 01:21:14,837
AND THE NAPKINS NOW.

2314
01:21:17,807 --> 01:21:20,643
[CROW IMITATES EXPLOSION]

2315
01:21:20,643 --> 01:21:23,580
THERE WE GO.

2316
01:21:23,580 --> 01:21:26,082
♪ WE’RE GETTING MARRIED
IN THE MORNING ♪

2317
01:21:26,082 --> 01:21:30,720
♪♪ [SERVO HUMS]

2318
01:21:30,720 --> 01:21:32,522
THANK YOU, VI.
JUST BECAUSE YOU COULDN’T

2319
01:21:32,522 --> 01:21:33,823
FIND ANYTHING
TO WEAR TO THE WEDDING

2320
01:21:33,823 --> 01:21:38,295
DIDN’T MEAN YOU HAD
TO RUIN IT FOR EVERYBODY.

2321
01:21:38,295 --> 01:21:39,862
♪ OPEN THE DOOR ♪

2322
01:21:39,862 --> 01:21:43,567
♪ FOR YOUR MYSTERY DATE ♪

2323
01:21:43,567 --> 01:21:46,803
VI.

2324
01:21:46,803 --> 01:21:48,438
I’VE COME TO TELL YOU
YOU’VE WON.

2325
01:21:48,438 --> 01:21:50,440
AND HERE’S WHAT YOU’VE WON.
TELL ’EM, JOHNNY!

2326
01:21:50,440 --> 01:21:53,377
--LIKE TO HEAR THAT.

2327
01:21:53,377 --> 01:21:55,478
I’M GOING AWAY, VI,
AND I’M NOT GOING BACK.

2328
01:21:55,478 --> 01:21:59,482
I GOT A WIFE AND KIDS
IN BALTIMORE, JACK.

2329
01:21:59,482 --> 01:22:01,050
- VI?
- MOM AND DAD

2330
01:22:01,050 --> 01:22:04,320
ARE GONNA SEND YOU
TO MILITARY SCHOOL.

2331
01:22:04,320 --> 01:22:06,690
VI, I’M RUNNING OUT ON MEG.

2332
01:22:06,690 --> 01:22:08,157
I’M NOT COMING BACK.

2333
01:22:08,157 --> 01:22:09,725
HMM.

2334
01:22:09,725 --> 01:22:11,828
[FOOTSTEPS]

2335
01:22:17,000 --> 01:22:19,502
SANDY’S BACK,
AND SHE’S PISSED.

2336
01:22:21,503 --> 01:22:23,473
SANDY.

2337
01:22:23,473 --> 01:22:24,607
WHAT’RE YOU DOING HERE?

2338
01:22:24,607 --> 01:22:27,377
- PAYBACK TIME.
- I FOLLOWED YOU.

2339
01:22:27,377 --> 01:22:31,113
WHY DID YOU
HAVE TO KILL HIM?

2340
01:22:31,113 --> 01:22:35,718
THOMAS DEWEY.

2341
01:22:35,718 --> 01:22:37,153
I KNEW SOMETHING
WOULD HAPPEN.

2342
01:22:37,153 --> 01:22:38,455
I WAS AGAINST THE MARRIAGE
FROM THE BEGINNING.

2343
01:22:38,455 --> 01:22:40,490
I’M LEAVING
FOR ANOTHER TEN YEARS.

2344
01:22:40,490 --> 01:22:43,827
LET ME HELP YOU
WITH YOUR GOWN, DEAR.

2345
01:22:43,827 --> 01:22:45,928
DON’T BOTHER, MOTHER.
SANDY WILL HELP ME.

2346
01:22:45,928 --> 01:22:47,497
SANDY, HELP YOUR SISTER.

2347
01:22:47,497 --> 01:22:50,167
SHE’S OUT INTERROGATING TOM.

2348
01:22:50,167 --> 01:22:51,668
- WHERE IS SANDY?
- SANDY.

2349
01:22:51,668 --> 01:22:54,370
I THOUGHT SHE CAME HOME
AHEAD OF US.

2350
01:22:54,370 --> 01:22:56,538
WELL, IF SHE DID,
SHE’S NOT HERE NOW.

2351
01:22:56,538 --> 01:23:00,410
I WISH YOU HADN’T
SEEN IT, SANDY.

2352
01:23:00,410 --> 01:23:02,212
NOW I’M AFRAID
YOU’LL TELL EVERYBODY,

2353
01:23:02,212 --> 01:23:04,513
AND I DON’T KNOW
WHAT TO DO.

2354
01:23:04,513 --> 01:23:06,415
- I’M WEARING A WIRE, TOM.
- I WON’T TELL.

2355
01:23:06,415 --> 01:23:08,352
BUT HOW CAN
I BE SURE OF THAT?

2356
01:23:08,352 --> 01:23:12,055
GOOD FRIENDS
PROTECT EACH OTHER.

2357
01:23:12,055 --> 01:23:14,257
YES.

2358
01:23:14,257 --> 01:23:17,027
SOMETIMES THEY CAN’T
HELP THEMSELVES.

2359
01:23:17,027 --> 01:23:18,628
THINGS LEAK OUT.

2360
01:23:18,628 --> 01:23:20,530
- HMM.
- POLICE HEAR ABOUT IT.

2361
01:23:20,530 --> 01:23:22,932
DO YOU KNOW WHAT WOULD HAPPEN
IF THE POLICE HEARD ABOUT THIS?

2362
01:23:22,932 --> 01:23:24,867
YOU’RE GONNA FRY, STEWART,
AND I’M GONNA BE THERE

2363
01:23:24,867 --> 01:23:27,103
- WHEN THEY FLIP THE SWITCH.
- THE GAS CHAMBER.

2364
01:23:29,772 --> 01:23:31,073
SANDY.

2365
01:23:31,073 --> 01:23:33,410
YOU’RE GONNA HAVE
TO TAKE THE FALL, SANDY.

2366
01:23:33,410 --> 01:23:34,910
SANDY, WHY DID YOU
HAVE TO SEE IT?

2367
01:23:34,910 --> 01:23:37,813
- OH, BLAME ME.
- I COULDN’T HELP IT.

2368
01:23:37,813 --> 01:23:40,150
NO.

2369
01:23:40,150 --> 01:23:43,420
NOBODY COULD HELP
ANY OF IT EXCEPT ME.

2370
01:23:43,420 --> 01:23:44,487
I COULD’VE SAVED VI.

2371
01:23:44,487 --> 01:23:46,022
I COULD’VE
PUT MY HAND OUT TO HER.

2372
01:23:46,022 --> 01:23:47,557
BUT THE SUN WAS IN MY EYES.

2373
01:23:47,557 --> 01:23:49,958
BUT I KILLED HER.

2374
01:23:52,495 --> 01:23:55,698
SANDY, HOW’D YOU LIKE TO
BUNGEE-JUMP WITHOUT THE BUNGEE?

2375
01:23:57,967 --> 01:23:59,802
SANDY, YOU...

2376
01:23:59,802 --> 01:24:01,703
KNOW I LOVE YOU VERY MUCH,
DON’T YOU?

2377
01:24:01,703 --> 01:24:03,873
LOOK, TOM, I GOT A FRIEND
AT THE D.A.’S OFFICE.

2378
01:24:03,873 --> 01:24:07,443
IF I DON’T SHOW UP,
THEY OPEN MY LUNCHBOX.

2379
01:24:09,145 --> 01:24:11,513
- [SERVO GASPS]
- THANK YOU, REVEREND.

2380
01:24:11,513 --> 01:24:12,915
- SHE ISN’T THERE.
- HMM.

2381
01:24:12,915 --> 01:24:13,983
I CAN’T IMAGINE
WHERE SHE COULD’VE GONE.

2382
01:24:13,983 --> 01:24:15,452
I’VE CHECKED
EVERY BAR IN TOWN.

2383
01:24:15,452 --> 01:24:16,787
WHERE’S TOM?

2384
01:24:16,787 --> 01:24:19,722
THE LEAST HE COULD DO
IS BE HERE WHEN MEG NEEDS HIM.

2385
01:24:19,722 --> 01:24:21,257
[MEG’S MOTHER]
CAN’T YOU LEAVE HIM ALONE?

2386
01:24:21,257 --> 01:24:25,662
JUST BECAUSE
HE RUINED OUR LIVES?

2387
01:24:25,662 --> 01:24:27,597
- THERE’S A LIGHT
IN THE LIGHTHOUSE.
- HUH.

2388
01:24:27,597 --> 01:24:28,998
SANDY COULD BE THERE.

2389
01:24:28,998 --> 01:24:31,700
SHE TALKS ABOUT THE PLACE
ALL THE TIME.

2390
01:24:31,700 --> 01:24:34,103
HEY, HOW MANY DALMATIANS
DIED FOR THAT DRESS?

2391
01:24:34,103 --> 01:24:36,238
- 101.
- HMM.

2392
01:24:36,238 --> 01:24:39,208
WE’D BETTER MAKE SURE.

2393
01:24:39,208 --> 01:24:41,443
AFTER I KNOCK BACK
A ROB ROY OR THREE.

2394
01:24:41,443 --> 01:24:44,913
[JOEL CHUCKLES]

2395
01:24:44,913 --> 01:24:47,283
WHY ARE WE GOING UP THERE?

2396
01:24:47,283 --> 01:24:49,785
LET’S GO UP
AND LOOK AT THE SEA.

2397
01:24:49,785 --> 01:24:52,322
YOU’RE NOT AFRAID OF ME,
ARE YOU?

2398
01:24:52,322 --> 01:24:54,490
I NEVER USED TO BE.

2399
01:24:54,490 --> 01:24:56,158
COME ON, THEN.

2400
01:24:56,158 --> 01:24:58,393
ALFRED HITCHCOCK’S
VERTIGO BABIES.

2401
01:24:58,393 --> 01:25:01,630
THIS IS ONE DARK
MAMMA-JAMMA OF A MOVIE, GUYS.

2402
01:25:01,630 --> 01:25:04,167
- YEAH.
- MM-HMM.

2403
01:25:04,167 --> 01:25:07,770
HE’D BETTER HURRY UP.
HE’S GOTTA RETURN THAT TUX.

2404
01:25:07,770 --> 01:25:09,072
WHEN THE MOON SHINES,

2405
01:25:09,072 --> 01:25:11,975
YOU CAN SEE THE WHOLE ISLAND
FROM UP HERE.

2406
01:25:11,975 --> 01:25:14,243
LOOK, IF I DISAPPEAR,
THERE’S A CRAYON DRAWING

2407
01:25:14,243 --> 01:25:16,512
THAT’LL GO TO MY LAWYER.

2408
01:25:19,915 --> 01:25:23,953
DIARRHEA IS LIKE
A STORM RAGING INSIDE YOU.

2409
01:25:23,953 --> 01:25:25,922
YOU DIDN’T TELL ANYONE
WE WERE COMING UP HERE, DID YOU?

2410
01:25:25,922 --> 01:25:28,692
YES, I DID.
I PAPERED THE CITY WITH FLYERS!

2411
01:25:28,692 --> 01:25:31,493
GOOD. GOOD.

2412
01:25:31,493 --> 01:25:33,963
LET’S GO BACK.

2413
01:25:33,963 --> 01:25:36,598
- ARE YOU AFRAID?
- YES.

2414
01:25:36,598 --> 01:25:38,735
SANDY.

2415
01:25:38,735 --> 01:25:40,737
SANDY, WHY DID YOU
HAVE TO SEE IT?

2416
01:25:40,737 --> 01:25:42,938
’CAUSE THE CRITICS GAVE IT
A GOOD REVIEW.

2417
01:25:42,938 --> 01:25:44,740
TOM.

2418
01:25:44,740 --> 01:25:49,678
VI, THIS ISN’T A GOOD TIME.

2419
01:25:49,678 --> 01:25:52,315
[SERVO IMITATES WIND]

2420
01:25:54,950 --> 01:25:56,418
[ALL]
AHH. OOH!

2421
01:25:56,418 --> 01:25:58,187
[TOM SCREAMS]

2422
01:25:58,187 --> 01:25:59,655
- [SANDY SCREAMS]
- SANDY HAS GROWN UP
A LOT THIS WEEK.

2423
01:25:59,655 --> 01:26:01,523
- YEP.
- MM-HMM.

2424
01:26:01,523 --> 01:26:03,827
THANKS FOR COMING INTO
OUR LIVES, TOM.

2425
01:26:03,827 --> 01:26:05,695
SO DOES THIS
MAKE MEG A WIDOW?

2426
01:26:05,695 --> 01:26:07,730
YEAH. WIDOW-MAKER.

2427
01:26:07,730 --> 01:26:10,867
TECHNICALLY.

2428
01:26:10,867 --> 01:26:12,868
SUDDENLY, PEOPLE LIVE HERE.

2429
01:26:12,868 --> 01:26:14,603
SESSIONS PRESENTS
FACES OF DEATH--

2430
01:26:14,603 --> 01:26:16,405
OH, STOP IT.

2431
01:26:19,342 --> 01:26:22,545
IT’S A KEEPER.

2432
01:26:22,545 --> 01:26:24,180
THAT’S NOT TOM,
IT’S A WOMAN.

2433
01:26:24,180 --> 01:26:25,615
HOW DO YOU TELL-- OH.

2434
01:26:25,615 --> 01:26:28,483
OH.

2435
01:26:28,483 --> 01:26:31,020
- WHERE DID HE FIND HER?
- WASHED IN THE ROCKS.

2436
01:26:31,020 --> 01:26:32,555
SHE’S BEEN DOWN THERE
A WEEK, I’D SAY.

2437
01:26:32,555 --> 01:26:36,092
ROB, MAKE HIM STOP.

2438
01:26:36,092 --> 01:26:38,493
SAMMY CAHN IS THE DOCTOR.

2439
01:26:46,903 --> 01:26:48,805
[MEG GROANS]

2440
01:26:48,805 --> 01:26:51,173
OH, HE’S CHEATING ON ME,
EVEN IN DEATH.

2441
01:26:51,173 --> 01:26:53,743
IF YOU COULD SEE
WHAT I HEAR.

2442
01:26:53,743 --> 01:26:56,745
I HAVE BEEN ACQUAINTED
WITH THE NIGHT.

2443
01:26:56,745 --> 01:26:59,648
TOM...

2444
01:26:59,648 --> 01:27:01,783
I NOW PRONOUNCE YOU

2445
01:27:01,783 --> 01:27:04,320
MAN AND DEATH.

2446
01:27:06,388 --> 01:27:08,958
CHARLES MOFFETT.

2447
01:27:08,958 --> 01:27:10,460
OR IS IT?

2448
01:27:10,460 --> 01:27:12,828
- D’OH.
- WHOA!

2449
01:27:27,643 --> 01:27:29,745
IT’S ONLY A MOVIE...

2450
01:27:29,745 --> 01:27:31,713
IT’S ONLY A MOVIE...

2451
01:27:31,713 --> 01:27:33,983
[ALL]
IT’S ONLY A MOVIE...

2452
01:27:33,983 --> 01:27:35,918
IT’S ONLY A MOVIE...

2453
01:27:35,918 --> 01:27:38,622
[ALL SOB]

2454
01:27:40,790 --> 01:27:43,927
IT’S ONLY A CRAPPY MOVIE
BY BERT I. GORDON

2455
01:27:43,927 --> 01:27:46,428
THAT HE MADE TO MASSAGE
THE MARKETPLACE.

2456
01:27:46,428 --> 01:27:48,865
IT’S ONLY NURTURING
ONE’S BASEST INSTINCT

2457
01:27:48,865 --> 01:27:52,435
AND TRYING WAY TOO HARD
TO BE FILM NOIR.

2458
01:27:52,435 --> 01:27:55,572
JEEZ, JOEL, I’M RIDING
SUCH A MAJOR BUMMER.

2459
01:27:55,572 --> 01:27:57,940
I FEEL LIKE I JUST SPENT
A COUPLE HOURS

2460
01:27:57,940 --> 01:28:01,043
AT LIQUOR LYLE’S
TALKING TO NEIL YOUNG.

2461
01:28:03,312 --> 01:28:05,415
HEY, WAIT,
I KNOW WHAT LET’S DO.

2462
01:28:05,415 --> 01:28:06,748
- WAIT A MINUTE, GUYS.
- HUH?

2463
01:28:06,748 --> 01:28:09,018
WE COULD THINK HAPPY THOUGHTS
AND ABOUT GOOD THINGS,

2464
01:28:09,018 --> 01:28:11,020
AND THOSE HAPPY THOUGHTS
AND GOOD THINGS

2465
01:28:11,020 --> 01:28:14,123
WILL SHOO AWAY
ALL THOSE DARK SMELLY IMAGES

2466
01:28:14,123 --> 01:28:16,025
THAT ARE CANERPING
FOR MOISTURE.

2467
01:28:16,025 --> 01:28:18,593
OH, LIKE THE WAY
SUNSHINE CHASES AWAY CLOUDS.

2468
01:28:18,593 --> 01:28:19,828
YEAH, YEAH.

2469
01:28:19,828 --> 01:28:21,463
LIKE THE WAY LYSOL SPRAY

2470
01:28:21,463 --> 01:28:23,800
ERASES BATHROOM ODORS
WITHOUT HEAVY PERFUME.

2471
01:28:23,800 --> 01:28:25,668
- YEAH.
- AND KILLS HOUSEHOLD GERMS

2472
01:28:25,668 --> 01:28:27,037
IN EMPTY GARBAGE CANS.

2473
01:28:27,037 --> 01:28:29,072
- YEAH.
- EMPTY HAMPERS,
TOILET AREAS,

2474
01:28:29,072 --> 01:28:30,473
- YEAH.
- UNDER SINKS, PET AREAS,

2475
01:28:30,473 --> 01:28:32,208
DIAPER PAILS, SICK ROOMS--

2476
01:28:32,208 --> 01:28:34,010
- YEAH!
- OH, SORRY.

2477
01:28:34,010 --> 01:28:35,712
[ALL]
YEAH!

2478
01:28:35,712 --> 01:28:37,947
EXACTLY.
COME ON, YOU GUYS.

2479
01:28:37,947 --> 01:28:40,717
♪ OH, THERE’S
A MARSHMALLOW RAINBOW ♪

2480
01:28:40,717 --> 01:28:42,085
♪ WAITING FOR YOU ♪

2481
01:28:42,085 --> 01:28:45,355
♪ WITH KITTIES
AND DOGGIES TOO ♪

2482
01:28:45,355 --> 01:28:48,490
♪ AND A SUPER-SOAKER 202 ♪

2483
01:28:48,490 --> 01:28:51,460
♪ AND I JUST GOT $10
FROM GRAMMA ♪

2484
01:28:51,460 --> 01:28:54,363
♪ AND I DON’T HAVE
TO SHARE IT WITH NO ONE ♪

2485
01:28:54,363 --> 01:28:57,467
♪ AND WE ALL GET TO GO
TO THE VALLEY HIGH DRIVE ♪

2486
01:28:57,467 --> 01:28:58,802
♪ IN OUR PAJAMAS AND WATCH ♪

2487
01:28:58,802 --> 01:29:01,203
♪ THE STAR WARS
TRIPLE FEATURE ♪

2488
01:29:01,203 --> 01:29:04,207
♪ DUSK TO DAWN ♪

2489
01:29:04,207 --> 01:29:06,542
♪ AND MY DAD JUST BECAME
REALLY GOOD FRIENDS ♪

2490
01:29:06,542 --> 01:29:08,443
♪ WITH MIKE CONNORS
OF MANNIX FAME ♪

2491
01:29:08,443 --> 01:29:11,580
♪ AND HE’S GOT
A TRIPLE-DECKER TREEHOUSE ♪

2492
01:29:11,580 --> 01:29:13,750
♪ AND I’LL SWING DOWN
ON MY VINE ♪

2493
01:29:13,750 --> 01:29:15,552
♪ TO MY OWN ROOM ♪

2494
01:29:15,552 --> 01:29:18,788
♪ I’M HAVING LADYLAND DINNERS
FOR BREAKFAST ♪

2495
01:29:18,788 --> 01:29:21,457
♪ AND KING VITAMAN
FOR DINNER ♪

2496
01:29:21,457 --> 01:29:22,825
♪ AND THE GOOD HUMOR TRUCK ♪

2497
01:29:22,825 --> 01:29:26,528
♪ ROLLED OVER
IN FRONT OF MY HOUSE ♪

2498
01:29:26,528 --> 01:29:28,030
AAH!

2499
01:29:28,030 --> 01:29:29,832
♪ --THE WORLD
OF SUPER MARIO BROTHERS ♪

2500
01:29:29,832 --> 01:29:31,400
♪ AND WE CAPTURED ROMMEL ♪

2501
01:29:31,400 --> 01:29:32,902
♪ AND GAVE HIM
TO THE PRESIDENT ♪

2502
01:29:32,902 --> 01:29:35,905
♪ AND HE GAVE ME
MY OWN HALF-HOUR SITCOM ♪

2503
01:29:35,905 --> 01:29:37,973
♪ FOLLOWING CHEERS ♪

2504
01:29:37,973 --> 01:29:41,177
[BOTS]
♪ AND THERE’S
NO SUCH THING AS ♪

2505
01:29:41,177 --> 01:29:43,112
♪ GIRLS! ♪

2506
01:29:43,112 --> 01:29:45,280
OH WAIT, I THINK
YOU WANNA THINK ABOUT THAT.

2507
01:29:45,280 --> 01:29:47,250
- [BOTS] HUH?
- WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

2508
01:29:47,250 --> 01:29:50,720
♪ AND MISTER DOCTOR
CLAYTON FORRESTER ♪

2509
01:29:50,720 --> 01:29:53,555
♪ WILL SWITCH TRAINS
AT THE TRAIN YARD ♪

2510
01:29:53,555 --> 01:29:57,058
♪ AND THERE WILL BE
A HORRIBLE ACCIDENT ♪

2511
01:29:57,058 --> 01:29:59,462
♪ FOR WHICH DR. FORRESTER ♪

2512
01:29:59,462 --> 01:30:00,963
♪ WILL BE BLAMED ♪

2513
01:30:00,963 --> 01:30:03,732
♪ POSTHUMOUSLY, OF COURSE ♪

2514
01:30:03,732 --> 01:30:05,300
♪ AND THEN
THE ROBOTS AND I ♪

2515
01:30:05,300 --> 01:30:07,537
♪ WILL BECOME
REALLY GOOD FRIENDS ♪

2516
01:30:07,537 --> 01:30:10,840
♪ AND THEN WILL BE ROOMMATES
WITH TRIPLE BUNK BEDS ♪

2517
01:30:10,840 --> 01:30:13,008
♪ AND WE WILL
STAY UP ALL NIGHT ♪

2518
01:30:13,008 --> 01:30:15,478
♪ TALKING ABOUT
REALLY COOL STUFF ♪

2519
01:30:15,478 --> 01:30:17,747
♪ AND THEY’LL THINK
I’M REALLY NEAT ♪

2520
01:30:17,747 --> 01:30:21,050
♪ AND THEN I’LL INVITE THEM
OVER TO MY HOUSE ♪

2521
01:30:21,050 --> 01:30:23,118
♪ AND WE’LL
CAMP... OUT... ♪

2522
01:30:23,118 --> 01:30:25,588
- [GRENADE TICKS]
- AND...

2523
01:30:25,588 --> 01:30:27,623
POOPIE.

2524
01:30:27,623 --> 01:30:29,458
[TICKING CONTINUES]

2525
01:30:29,458 --> 01:30:31,927
[EXPLOSION]

2526
01:30:34,197 --> 01:30:35,998
♪♪ [THEME]

2527
01:31:30,385 --> 01:31:32,588
TOM STEWART KILLED ME!

2528
01:31:32,588 --> 01:31:34,990
TOM STEWART KILLED ME!
